BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Douds Duo
DTSTART:20251207T000000Z
DTEND:20251207T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20251027T180102Z
UID:e68cfe66-b35e-11f0-8fde-0242ac11001c
DESCRIPTION:https://mrsmalls.com/events/the-douds-duo/\nThe Acousticafe Son
 gwriter Series is a showcase of local and regional up-and-coming talent!\n
 The Douds Duo: Vacillating between sweet\, angsty\, sultry\, and salty\, N
 adine Douds’s music is full of both hope and regret\, as well as a hefty
  dose of love and revenge. The vocal lines explore the beautiful tension o
 f dissonance\, keeping the ear intrigued and the heart twinging. Nadine’
 s music has been described as ‘extrovert music by an introvert’. The D
 ouds Duo (Nadine and Nathan Douds) can be heard performing their own uniqu
 e takes on popular covers\, as well as performing Nadine Douds originals. 
 See nadinedouds.com for more info.\nMatt Eddy: Matt Eddy is a songwriter f
 rom Tampa Bay\, currently residing in the Pittsburgh area. His gentle and 
 wide-ranging voice and sensitive approach to the acoustic guitar provide a
 n intimate atmosphere that enable his poetic lyrics to resonate with the l
 istener.\nAbbey Martin: Abbey Martin is an alt-folk singer songwriter who 
 found and developed a love for writing music during the pandemic. Her song
 s frequently include themes of nature\, weather\, and emotional conflict (
 adding in satire and humor when possible). She loves to sing harmony with 
 others and dreams of starting of an alternative choir.\n6:30PM to 9PM\n$10
  Suggested Donation (Collected at the door!)\nThis Event Is All Ages
LOCATION:Mr. Smalls Cafe
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:COWGIRL CLUE
DTSTART:20251210T010000Z
DTEND:20251210T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20251028T040106Z
UID:ba5d7718-b3b2-11f0-b864-0242ac11001c
DESCRIPTION:https://app.opendate.io/e/cowgirl-clue-december-09-2025-610742\
 n  COWGIRL CLUE with support from HER NEW KNIFE SWEET93  $18 ADV / $20 DOS
  7PM DOORS / 8PM MUSIC ALL AGES  for fans of... Grimes\, Alice Glass\, Yae
 ji\, Uffie\, HEALTH  BIO: Born and raised in the heart of the Lonestar Sta
 te\, Cowgirl Clue is an artist\, electronic producer\, and singer songwrit
 er best known for her eclectic\, electronic music and esoterically-trendse
 tting visuals. Taking influence from her experience as an underground DJ i
 n her teenage years\; Ashley blends classic rave sounds stylized with twan
 gy country guitars\, witch house saws and electropop elements\, she often 
 refers to her sound as “Y’allternative Music”.  Cowgirl Clue’s ear
 liest release\, “Cherry Jubilee” showcases her creative soar with drum
  and bass meets sugary vocals. Her debut album in 2019\, Icebreaker was an
  introduction to her Y2K revival sound that captured a niche\, stylish aud
 ience.  Her most recent sophomore album\, Rodeo Star released in August of
  2023 diving deeper into her Southern roots with twangy guitar tones and h
 ard techno bass styles. From her unique take on Country Pop\, songs like 
 “Trailblaze ☆” and “Gold Switchblade” to her more electronic bas
 ed songs like “$somethin’s in The Air” and “Picket Fence”\, Ashl
 ey demonstrates a vast range of expression to make for an culture defining
  and meaningful album. Cowgirl Clue’s live performances are often consid
 ered highly energetic\, mystical and punk. Cowgirl Clue is a longtime asse
 t and contributor to California based collective\, Vada Vada. She ignites 
 her ability to innovate genres while articulating suburban-fantasy-nostalg
 ia in a present day fashion. Her carving sound and visual world has been k
 nown to be quite influential among the internet. Cowgirl Clue has shared t
 he stage with acts such as Crystal Castles\, Sky Ferriera\, The Garden\, W
 hite Ring\, Enjoy\, Kumo 99\, MGNA CRRTA and more.   
LOCATION:Bottlerocket Social Hall
END:VEVENT
