BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Poetry Workshop with Ken Waldman
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251119T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20251119T190000
DTSTAMP:20251031T020100Z
UID:72f98860-b5fd-11f0-a616-0242ac11001c
DESCRIPTION:https://www.poetrymillvale.com/event/poetry-workshop-with-ken-w
 aldman/\nFOUR PROMPTS: THE BEGINNING OF FOUR NEW POEMS \n  \nThe more you
  write\, the luckier you get—and each time you start a piece\, there’s
  an opportunity to get luckier than ever. The trick is getting started. He
 re\, you’ll not only begin four new poems\, but will learn strategies to
  begin many more. The session is open to writers of all levels and experie
 nce. \n  \nIn addition to being a fiddler (with 12 CDs)\, Ken Waldman is 
 a former college professor with an MFA in Creative Writing from University
  of Alaska Fairbanks. He has 17 full-length poetry collections\, a memoir 
 (about his life as a touring artist)\, 3 children’s poetry collections\,
  a creative writing manual\, a short story collection\, and a novel. Over 
 400 of his stories\, poems\, and essays have appeared in such journals as 
 Beloit Poetry Journal\, Massachusetts Review\, and Poets & Writers.
LOCATION:Poetry Lounge\, 313 North Ave.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AcoustiCafe Open Stage
DTSTART:20251104T000000Z
DTEND:20251104T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20251031T040100Z
UID:363c0a22-b60e-11f0-8a95-0242ac11001c
DESCRIPTION:https://mrsmalls.com/events/acousticafe-open-stage-14/\nMONDAY 
 NOV 3\, 2025 - WYEP 91.3 & Straub Brewing Presents: AcoustiCafe Open Stage
  with host Gibson Musisko ft Zach Miller and Carcasso the Fox!\nTHEME: “
 JOURNEY”\nNot the band. But maybe a little like the band\, what with the
  inspirational motifs and emotional introspection. But more like the journ
 ey in The Hobbit\, a great adventure which leads to dynamic character arcs
  for the heroes. So imagine Journey the band\, but they're all hobbits\, a
 nd their songs are cooler - then do that.\nGIBSON MUSISKO leads the amazin
 g PosterChild\, which is releasing a new album in January 2026 - they are 
 playing tonight (Thu Oct 30) at Poetry Lounge\, with a couple shows on the
  road before coming back for Nov 15 opening for Zack Keim at Club Cafe.\nN
 EW STUFF!!\nZACH MILLER is a brand new songwriter on the scene who Gibson 
 digs\, we're psyched to check him out!\nCARCASSO THE FOX is an awesome ban
 d name - fronted by our AC friend David Montez\, also brand new and sparkl
 y!!!
LOCATION:The Funhouse at Mr. Smalls
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ken Waldman & Mark Tamsula
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251119T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20251119T210000
DTSTAMP:20251031T040100Z
UID:36414c12-b60e-11f0-8a95-0242ac11001c
DESCRIPTION:https://www.poetrymillvale.com/event/ken-waldman/\nAlaskan Poet
 \, Writer\, Teacher\, Fiddler with Pittsburgh Fiddler\, Banjo Player\, Gui
 taristExpect an evening of fun\, inspiration\, and surprises–from rowdy 
 fiddle and banjo duets\, to savory twin fiddling\, to original waltzes\, t
 o rare Southwest Pennsylvania Appalachian fiddle tunes. They’re all a ba
 ckdrop to Ken Waldman’s poetry and Alaska-influenced storytelling. \nA f
 ormer college professor with an MFA in Creative Writing\, Ken Waldman has 
 published seventeen full-length poetry collections\, three additional full
 -length poetry volumes for younger readers\, a memoir\, a creative writing
  manual\, a short story collection\, and a novel\, all from respected inde
 pendent small presses. \n  \nMark Tamsula plays fiddle\, banjo\, guitar\,
  and mandolin in the Old Time Country style and knows more than 700 tunes 
 and songs\, including a repertoire of music specific to the SW Pennsylvani
 a region. Mark has been performing and teaching in the Pittsburgh area for
  over 30 years. You can visit his website at www.appalachianmusic.net.
LOCATION:Poetry Lounge\, 313 North Ave.
END:VEVENT
