BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AcoustiCafe Open Stage
DTSTART:20251111T000000Z
DTEND:20251111T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20251107T210111Z
UID:e3ffd7ce-bc1c-11f0-8eb0-0242ac110022
DESCRIPTION:https://mrsmalls.com/events/acousticafe-open-stage-15/\nMONDAY 
 NOV 10\, 2025\n  \nWYEP 91.3 & Straub Brewing Presents:AcoustiCafe Open St
 age with host Scarfire Media featuring Moonshine Jasmine and Craig Veltri!
 !\n  \nTheme. PROTEST/ Change . Its that time of year when the weather and
  time change. It is also ( unfortunately) a time in history where we Need 
 Change!!! Whether it is about the weather or about politics\, Sing out you
 r favorite songs about the change happening or the change you want to see.
 \n  \nSCARFIRE MEDIA LLC - The voice of the independent arts. Pittsburgh's
  newest artist development company made by musicians for musicians.\n  \nM
 OONSHINE JASMINE - Your Favorite Blues Rock Band. Bringing you retro vibes
  with a brand new flare.\n  \nMEGAN PENNINGTON - Redifining the idea of th
 e DIY musician since 2014. Owns Scarfire Media and fronts Moonshine Jasmin
 e\, when she's not teaching guitar or playing solo.\n  \nCRAIG VELTRI -To 
 turn a phrase from his song “Home Out on the Shore\,” Craig Veltri is 
 a “country/urban hybrid” In August 2020\, Veltri released his first EP
 \, Vagabond. Produced by former Charlie Daniels Band drummer\, Jack Gavin\
 , this EP is a culmination of Veltri "cutting his teeth" in Nashville for 
 the previous 5 years.\n  \nVeltri has released 6 singles since Vagabond co
 ntinuing to flex and stretch his creative range. Whether it be "Shine On"\
 , a Beatles inspired song penned by Veltri and produced by fellow Pittsbur
 gh native Bryan Cole\, or “Wandering Eye"\, a song with a Hank Williams 
 inspired motif co-written by Abby Hankins and produced by PT Houston of Of
 f The Row Studios\, Craig Veltri intends to never shy away from any genre 
 of music and refuses to be pigeonholed.\n  \nIn November 2022\, he release
 d a video for the single "Makin' Noise on Music Row" filmed entirely on lo
 cation in Nashville\, TN with the help of Eli Adelman and Ten Bears Produc
 tions.\n  \nHis latest record\, a full length\, acoustic\, concept record 
 entitled "Letters to the Defendant" details the downfall of his marriage d
 ue to alcoholism\, his personal housecleaning and redemption. Letters to T
 he Defendant is now available on limited edition vinyl.\nDEB COOK is a Pit
 tsburgh-based artist\, singer-songwriter\, and producer whose voice has be
 en heard alongside countless musicians throughout the region’s vibrant m
 usic scene. After years of collaborating and lending her vocals to a wide 
 range of artists\, Deb is now stepping into her own spotlight\, creating o
 riginal music in partnership with acclaimed Pittsburgh songwriter Adam Lev
 ine under the project Aliquid Novi.\n  \nAs the founder of Steel Kitty Pro
 ductions\, Deb has built a platform dedicated to amplifying underrepresent
 ed voices in the arts. From curating open stages like AcoustiCafe to co-pr
 oducing the Pittsburgh Women’s Music Festival\, Deb has become a corners
 tone in cultivating the city’s creative ecosystem.\n  \nWith Aliquid Nov
 i\, Deb transforms her years of collaboration into a new chapter of person
 al expression. Working with Adam Levine\, she blends evocative vocals with
  layered\, genre-bending arrangements that capture raw emotion and hidden 
 moments of beauty. The band’s album HEAT(2025) showcases Deb’s evoluti
 on from a sought-after supporting artist into a dynamic front-woman and co
 -creator.\n  \nWhether producing under the Steel Kitty banner or performin
 g with Aliquid Novi\, Deb Cook continues to shape Pittsburgh’s music cul
 ture—uniting her artistry\, advocacy\, and entrepreneurial spirit to upl
 ift others while boldly embracing her own sound.
LOCATION:The Funhouse at Mr. Smalls
END:VEVENT
