BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:APES OF THE STATE
DTSTART:20260219T010000Z
DTEND:20260219T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20251126T050059Z
UID:e5f5b29e-ca84-11f0-a4d8-0242ac110022
DESCRIPTION:https://app.opendate.io/e/apes-of-the-state-february-18-2026-61
 9349\n  APES OF THE STATE - This City Isn't Big Enough 10th Anniversary To
 ur with support from RENT STRIKE  $15 7PM DOORS / 8PM MUSIC ALL AGES  for 
 fans of... Pat the Bunny\, Mischief Brew\, Pigeon Pit  BIO: Apes of the St
 ate is an independent Lancaster\, PA based folk punk band.  Apes of the St
 ate was born from the post-rehab bedroom folk punk project of singer/songw
 riter April Hartman in 2015. In her words: “I picked up a guitar and sta
 rted writing about s*** instead of doing drugs about it.” Their sound is
  a distinct blend of classic folk punk\, emo\, pop punk\, folk\, and blueg
 rass with attitude fueled vocals spitting clever lyrical wordplay. The cur
 rent lineup consists of Dan Ebersole on mandolin & electric guitar\, Molli
 e Swartz on bass & violin\, & Ian Cornele on drums.  Despite their growth 
 Apes of the State remains fiercely independent and practices a DIY ethos. 
 They hope to serve as an example that you can achieve success outside of t
 he traditional music industry framework. In April’s words\, “we don’
 t beg for anyone to pay attention to us and give us opportunities – we c
 reate them for ourselves and our community.”   
LOCATION:Bottlerocket Social Hall
END:VEVENT
