BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AcoustiCafe Open Stage
DTSTART:20251202T000000Z
DTEND:20251202T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20251130T060057Z
UID:f0856f8a-cdb1-11f0-8e59-0242ac11001e
DESCRIPTION:https://mrsmalls.com/events/acousticafe-open-stage-18/\nMONDAY 
 DECEMBER 1\, 2025 - WYEP 91.3 & Straub Brewing Presents: AcoustiCafe Open 
 Stage with host Danny Rectenwald ft. Mark Williams & Obscure Spirits with 
 special guests The EastShore Chorale!\nTheme. RECONCILIATION\nFor example\
 , reconciling a desire to list our host\, two features and a special guest
  in an event title with a 100-character limit! But also more poetic and mu
 sical interpretations of the concept 🙂\nDANNY RECTENWALD is a true Guit
 arist Around Town\, playing classical instrumentals\, teaching\, backing s
 inger/songwriters like Molly Alphabet and Mark Dignam\, and leading the Fu
 sion Groove band Favorite Band among many other pursuits!! Find out more a
 t\nhttps://dannyrec.bandcamp.com/\nMARK WILLIAMS hosts Hello\, Humans! - a
  show our neighbor Mark Williams created to give kids and adults tools and
  language they can use to introduce mindfulness to their everyday lives.\n
 https://www.wqed.org/hello-humans/\nOBSCURE SPIRITS writes "we are an indi
 e-alternative thing and are a little lost perhaps now more than ever" - we
 've seen Brian of Obscure Spirits perform solo a few times at AC\, psyched
  to hear the whole band!\nTHE EASTSHORE CHORALE - it's become a happy trad
 ition to welcome The EastShore Chorale as special guests as they kick off 
 their seasonal concerts - They will perform Fri Dec 19 at Waverly Church i
 n Regent Square and Sat Dec 20 at Calvary Church in the North Side - The E
 astShore Chorale is a non-sectarian\, intergenerational community choir ba
 sed in Regent Square\, Pittsburgh. As part of Eastman Community Projects\,
  a non-profit that focuses communities on becoming more art-centric\, the 
 choir seeks to uplift and enrich the community through the performance of 
 a wide range of music\, and to provide an opportunity for people to contri
 bute to Pittsburgh’s thriving arts scene.
LOCATION:The Funhouse at Mr. Smalls
END:VEVENT
