UID:b827698e-d6c3-11f0-b893-0242ac11001e
DESCRIPTION:https://app.opendate.io/e/holmes-january-10-2026-639484\n  Holm
 es had a breakthrough year with her scene-stealing portrayal of “Hailee"
  in A24/Amazon’s OVERCOMPENSATING from Benito Skinner and recurring on s
 eason 4 of the Emmy award-winning series HACKS.  Holmes gained recognition
  for the lead role of “Kelly Mallet” in Paul Feig’s FOX comedy WELCO
 ME TO FLATCH\, then quickly reunited with Feig on his feature JACKPOT! sta
 rring Jon Cena & Awkwafina adding an additional cameo role in ANOTHER SIMP
 LE FAVOR.  On the development side\, Holmes previously sold a pilot STUCK 
 with co-creator Caleb Hearon to Hulu\, about two queer best friends who de
 spite their lofty words about leaving Kansas City\, find themselves actual
 ly pleased about being “stuck” there.  Why'd We Book It? Holmes's roll
  in OVERCOMPENSATING is iconic\, From the quotable lines to her iconic out
 fits. She becomes the latest cast member (Mary Beth Barone\, Wally Baram) 
 to make their way to the Bottlerocket stage\, her first solo headlining sh
 ow (they were here with Mekki Leeper 2 years ago!) in Pittsburgh. Her tikt
 ok's are the good cringe that you know we all have in ourselves.  For Fans
  Of... Nikki Glaser\, Meg Stalter\, Wally Baram\, Mary Beth Barone    Seat
 ing/Show Information: You can not purchase tickets to multiple shows.   Th
 is show will have theater seating. Seats will be assigned upon arrival\, o
 r can be chosen ahead of time for an additional fee.   QR Code Ordering wi
 ll be available for this performance.  Doors open at 5pm.  Don't miss our 
 famous Bottlerocket Pre-Show Clip Collection\, beginning one hour before t
 he start of the performance.  This show is ALL AGES  *all information subj
 ect to change as needed.    Bottlerocket FAQ:   All shows starting before 
 10pm are all ages unless otherwise noted.  Free parking is available at 82
 4 Industry Street and 205 Allen Street\, as well as other public lots in t
 he area.  Live Music shows have limited seating options\, please arrive ea
 rly or reach out to the venue directly if you know that you require a seat
 .  Doors open at 5pm for all shows unless noted otherwise. The time listed
  on the ticket is the event's true start time.  Most shows have a preshow 
 experience starting 1 hour before the show.  All tickets are non-refundabl
 e - our full refund policy can be viewed here  Please contact us ahead of 
 time with any accesibilty requests or concerns\, we're happy to accomodate
