BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BOTTLE TALKS: A Lecture Series
DTSTART:20260103T010000Z
DTEND:20260103T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20251217T180129Z
UID:69e6b82a-db72-11f0-b7ce-0242ac110024
DESCRIPTION:https://app.opendate.io/e/bottle-talks-a-lecture-series-january
 -02-2026-649336\n Is your New Years Resolution to get a little smarter thi
 s year? Here's a great place to start\, the kick off to our 2026 season of
  Bottle Talks\, our LECTURE SERIES featuring some of the most interesting 
 academics in the city presenting their work in a good old fashion dive bar
 .  From dinosaurs to conceptual art\, these talks have run the gaumet of t
 opics and interests - while still being fun enough to enjoy with a draft b
 eer or cocktail!  Leslie A. Pryzbylek - Senior Curator of the Heinz Histor
 y Center "How's That History? Exploring the Heinz History Center Archives"
  The Heinz History center is uniquely dedicated to preserving Western PA h
 istory\; which can lead to some pretty odd things in their collection. A b
 aking pan that helped originate a famous Burnt Almond Torte recipe\, the s
 ign of a bohemian coffee shop\, a paper mache character from a lost Kennyw
 ood ride. Even a shovel with 6 handles! As odd as of some of these pieces 
 may be\, they all work together to tell the story of our city and region\,
  and the people who call it home. Join Senior Curator Leslie A. Pryzbylek 
 as she spotlights some of the strangest and oddest things in the museums a
 rchives\; things that may make you ask "wait... how is that history?" - an
 d learn about their importance in the ongoing research the museum does eve
 ry day!  Isaac Pleta - Associated Artists of Pittsburgh "I Love Conceptual
  Art\, And You Can Too!" In his popular instagram series ‘Returns to Art
 \,’ - Isaac Pleta has featured over 200 arts exhibitions\, programs\, an
 d sites in and around Pittsburgh - making the sometimes obtuse and indecip
 herable world of contemporary art accessible and fun for all. In this talk
 \, Isaac expands on those ideas - breaking down the barriers to conceptual
  art and highlighting it's ongoing importance\, the exciting work that con
 tinues to be done by local artists\, and how you can sound smarter the nex
 t time you're at an art museum!   Plus an open audience Q&A with both afte
 r.  PLUS! 100% of the ticket sales from this event will be donated back to
  the speakers research departments to help support their ongoing work! 
LOCATION:Bottlerocket Social Hall
END:VEVENT
