BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BOTTLE TALKS: A Lecture Series
DTSTART:20260312T233000Z
DTEND:20260313T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20260117T210106Z
UID:a448a86a-f3e7-11f0-8fb7-0242ac11000f
DESCRIPTION:https://app.opendate.io/e/bottle-talks-a-lecture-series-march-1
 2-2026-655570\n Join us for our 2026 season of Bottle Talks\, a LECTURE SE
 RIES featuring some of the most interesting academics in the city presenti
 ng their work in a good old fashion dive bar.  From dinosaurs to conceptua
 l art\, these talks have run the gaumet of topics and interests - while st
 ill being fun enough to enjoy with a draft beer or cocktail!  March's edit
 ion feature's a full night takeover from Pittsburgh's own NATIONAL AVIARY\
 , including an onstage appearnce by a real life AFRICAN PENGUIN\, right in
  Bottlerocket!  Katie Manion - AZA SAFE African Penguins Vice Program Chai
 r and Curator of Education Cathy Schlott - Director of Animal Programs  "A
 ll About the AZA SAFE African Penguin Program" Penguins are undeniably cha
 rismatic—and full of surprises. Dive into the fascinating world of pengu
 ins to discover their remarkable adaptations\, quirky behaviors\, and the 
 challenges they face in the wild. The National Aviary is home to a thrivin
 g colony of African Penguins and proudly leads the AZA SAFE African Pengui
 n program dedicated to their survival.   With fewer than 9\,000 breeding p
 airs remaining in the wild\, these birds are critically endangered and nee
 d our help more than ever. Hear from AZA SAFE African Penguins Vice Progra
 m Chair and Curator of Education Katie Manion and Director of Animal Progr
 ams Cathy Schlott as they share behind-the-scenes insights\, conservation 
 success stories\, and ways you can make a difference. Plus\, get ready for
  a special appearance by an Ambassador African Penguin—because no pengui
 n talk is complete without a penguin.  Plus an open audience Q&A with both
  after.  PLUS! 100% of the ticket sales from this event will be donated ba
 ck to the speakers research departments to help support their ongoing work
 ! 
LOCATION:Bottlerocket Social Hall
END:VEVENT
