DESCRIPTION:https://thunderbirdmusichall.com/event/citizen-soldier/thunderb
 ird-cafe-music-hall/pittsburgh-pennsylvania/\n\nCitizen Soldier\nSaturday\
 , May 30\, 2026Thunderbird Music Hall4053 Butler Street\, Pittsburgh\, PAD
 oors @ 6pmShow @ 7pmAGE RESTRICTION: 18+\n \n\nCitizen Soldier was born i
 n 2016 when frontman Jake Segura penned the lyrics to “Let It Burn” fr
 om a psychiatric hospital. Now practicing as a clinical therapist\, he imp
 lements intensely emotional lyrical themes on mental health into their mus
 ic. The band presents an accessible message that combats stigmatization an
 d provides a group therapy dynamic.\n \nBased in Salt Lake City\, Utah\, 
 Segura is joined by guitarists Matt Duffney and Kooper Hanosky\, bassist/k
 eyboardist Wonitta\, and drummer Kyle Persell.\n\nTicket Tier Info:General
  Admission Tickets – Standing Room Only\nThere are no additional entry
  protocols at this time. Entry requirements are subject to change. By pur
 chasing tickets to this event you agree to abide by entry requirements in 
 effect at the time of the event. Check the venue website leading up to 
 your event for the latest protocols. Please visit https://thunderbirdmusic
 hall.com/safety/ for more information on Covid-19 Safety. All sales are f
 inal. 
LOCATION:Thunderbird Music Hall
END:VEVENT
