BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Weedeater
DTSTART:20260420T000000Z
DTEND:20260420T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260123T180113Z
UID:81668f90-f885-11f0-9392-0242ac11000e
DESCRIPTION:https://thunderbirdmusichall.com/event/weedeater-2/thunderbird-
 cafe-music-hall/pittsburgh-pennsylvania/\n\nWeedeaterConanSunday April 19\
 , 2026Thunderbird Music Hall4053 Butler Street\, Pittsburgh\, PADoors @ 7:
 00pmShow @ 7:30pmAGE RESTRICTION: 18+http://weedmetal.com/Weedeater was bo
 rn the mid-’90s\, in Wilmington\, NC\, originally taking shape as a side
  project of vocalist/bassist “Dixie” Dave Collins\, who was otherwise 
 engaged with sludge metal cult favorites  at the time. However\, upon tha
 t band’s official demise in 1998\, Collins was free to concentrate his e
 fforts on Weedeater\, which released two sludgecore albums to kick off the
  new millennium: 2001’s And Justice for Y’All and 2002’s Sixteen Ton
 s\, both produced by stoner specialist Billy Anderson. Collins later decid
 ed to tour briefly as bass player for  and also found time to lend his fo
 ur strings to Wilmington neighbors\, but continued to work with Weedeater 
 guitarist Shep and drummer Keko\, touring relentlessly over the years\, wi
 th the likes of C.O.C. and . Busy as he was\, Collins and co. finally got 
 around to recording their third long-player\, God Luck and Good Speed\, wh
 ich was release through Southern Lord in 2007. ~ Eduardo Rivadavia\, Rovih
 ttps://www.hailconan.com/Conan – the sound of unending hammer blows into
  the earth. A galloping charging war horse heading for your town. So heavy
  that the gods look away\, intimidated by their unearthly delivery. \n \
 nTicket Tier Info: GAGeneral Admission Tickets – Standing Room Only\nThe
 re are no additional entry protocols at this time. Entry requirements ar
 e subject to change. By purchasing tickets to this event you agree to abid
 e by entry requirements in effect at the time of the event. Check the v
 enue website leading up to your event for the latest protocols. Please vis
 it https://thunderbirdmusichall.com/safety/ for more information on Covid-
 19 Safety. All sales are final. 
