BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DOG PARTY
DTSTART:20260326T000000Z
DTEND:20260326T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260123T210115Z
UID:a7bff3ac-f89e-11f0-8456-0242ac11000e
DESCRIPTION:https://app.opendate.io/e/dog-party-march-25-2026-657247\n  DOG
  PARTY with support tba  $15 ADV / $18 DOS 7PM DOORS / 8PM MUSIC ALL AGES 
  for fans of... Ramones\, The Muffs\, Colleen Green\, The Go-Go's  BIO: Do
 g Party is a California-based\, indie rock'n'roll band\, composed of siste
 rs\, Gwendolyn and Lucy Giles. Compared with bands like The Go-Go's\, The 
 Ramones\, The White Stripes\, and The Runaways\, Dog Party establishes the
 ir own unique west coast sound with a dash of punk and a sprinkle of pop. 
  Dog Party formed in 2007 when the sisters were just 10 and 8 years of age
 . After debuting at their elementary school talent show\, Dog Party quickl
 y started playing shows around their hometown of Sacramento. They released
  their debut self-titled record in 2009 on Half of Nothing Records.  Dog P
 arty soon caught the attention of Kepi Ghoulie of the Groovie Ghoulies. Af
 ter rocking numerous hometown shows together\, Ghoulie took Dog Party out 
 on their first tour. From 2011 to 2016\, Dog Party would embark on numerou
 s US and European tours opening for Kepi Ghoulie and performing as his bac
 king band.  In 2013\, Dog Party released their 3rd album “Lost Control
 ” (Engineered by Chris Woodhouse) and debut release on Asian Man Records
 \, generating buzz and launching them in the DIY music community. Furtherm
 ore\, Dog Party released “Vol.4” (2015) and “‘Til You’re Mine”
  (2016) on Asian Man Records.  In 2016\, Dog Party was the special guest o
 n Green Day’s Revolution Radio tour. This was a full circle moment for t
 he band\, as Gwendolyn was first inspired to pick up a guitar after hearin
 g American Idiot.  In 2018\, Dog Party released their 6th album “Hit & R
 un” on Brat Mag + Music. Dog Party followed the release with a headline 
 tour\, in addition to tours supporting The Aquabats\, Reel Big Fish\, Bad 
 Cop Bad Cop\, and CJ Ramone throughout 2019.  Dog Party has also been feat
 ured films SLC Punk 2: Punk’s Dead (2016) and Coast (2021) in the live c
 oncert band footage   With their most recent release\, Dog Party put out t
 heir 7th studio album\, “Dangerous” on their brand new label called Sn
 eak Dog Records on May 17th\, 2024. “Dangerous” was recorded in San Jo
 se\, CA at District Recording and produced by Ryan Perras and Dog Party.  
 In 2025\, Dog Party opened up for Jack White for the very last show of his
  No Name tour. This was a huge accomplishment for the band\, as Jack White
  is their music hero.    
LOCATION:Bottlerocket Social Hall
END:VEVENT
