BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Heading North x Old Neon (Old Neon’s Final Show!)
DTSTART:20260405T000000Z
DTEND:20260405T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260209T185952Z
UID:83de49c2-05e9-11f1-bf12-0242ac110022
DESCRIPTION:https://mrsmalls.com/events/heading-north-x-old-neon/\nTICKETS 
 ON SALE AT NOON\, WEDNESDAY FEB 4Heading North is Asha Edson (vocals)\, Ae
 dan Symons (guitar)\, Cee Frink (bass)\, Hannah Kozak (guitar)\, and Mario
  Tierno (drums). Heading North started as five friends coming together in 
 guitarist Aedan Symons’ living room to celebrate their love of music in 
 February 2023. After a successful first single and well-received debut EP\
 , the band quickly shifted from a pleasurable hobby to a full fledged\, un
 imaginable musical project. Heading North combines elements of emo\, pop p
 unk\, and metalcore to create their own space in the emo alternative scene
 \; boisterous guitars\, ethereal melodies\, and brutal breakdowns have hel
 ped them gain popularity in their home city of Pittsburgh.Old Neon is unli
 kely. Five strangers from Pittsburgh\, PA coming together as the world was
  opening up again\, never knowing if they would ever get to play a show. U
 nlikely that a band would survive through so many personal and creative di
 fferences to create their own tapestry of pop punk and grow together to be
 come something greater than the sum of their parts. Unlikely that they wou
 ld share stages with some of the biggest names in their genre\, to challen
 ge themselves as writers\, and make it work at all. From the brink of brea
 king up altogether\, the band has delivered their most moving work. The pr
 oducer of their latest EP Matt Brasch (The Wonder Years\, Cold Climb It) h
 as stated that they have done “better than make it work. Not only did th
 e band make things work\, they succeeded in stepping up their craft as son
 gwriters and performers throughout the project. They dug deep for beautifu
 l and explosive performances.”This Event Is All AgesAll Sales Are Final.
LOCATION:The Funhouse at Mr. Smalls
END:VEVENT
