BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Acousticafe Songwriter Series
DTSTART:20260417T230000Z
DTEND:20260418T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260216T200121Z
UID:43c82ffe-0b72-11f1-be3b-aa4e6ea5cfaa
DESCRIPTION:https://mrsmalls.com/events/acousticafe-songwriter-series-12/\n
 Brian Junker - Fingerstyle acoustic guitar\, old-time Appalachian banjo\, 
 a little mandolin here and there\, and a gentle tenor voice… Brian Junke
 r writes and sings folk/pop songs rendered on traditional instruments\, vi
 gnettes of the lives all around us.  Brian writes and plays his own music 
 as well as the music of many great but often not well-known singer/songwri
 ters.  He also enjoys old-time jams\, choirs\, and anyplace else where com
 munity gathers around music.  You can find his music on Soundcloud\, Band
 camp\, and social media.Caleb Pogyor - Caleb Pogyor has moved away from Pi
 ttsburgh a few times over the years\, but the magnetic pull of the city th
 at shaped and nurtured his roots always calls him home. Growing up among i
 ts rolling hills\, deep valleys\, and the mystical mystery of the “fourt
 h hidden river\,” Caleb draws inspiration from the landscape as much as 
 from the deep-rooted friendships that define it.  His sound reflects t
 hat journey. Once immersed in the nu-metal grooves of KoRn and Primer 55\,
  Caleb eventually found his voice through the introspective songwriting of
  Sufjan Stevens and Elliott Smith\, as well as the expansive textures of R
 adiohead. Listeners may hear echoes reminiscent of Fleet Foxes and Wilco.D
 an Petrich - Dan Petrich is a singer-songwriter who has been creating and
  sharing original music in Pittsburgh for many years. His music is inform
 ed by traditional folk\, American Primitive guitar\, ambient\, and even fi
 eld recordings. He has three full length records to his credit. In the sp
 ring of 2026\, he will release his first all instrumental record\, Soundin
 gs. You can find his music on Bandcamp\, Spotify\, Instagram\, and occasio
 nally WYEP.This Event Is All Ages
LOCATION:Mr. Smalls Cafe
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Taking Back Sunday
