BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Weedeater w/ Conan\, Telekinetic Yeti\, Funerals
DTSTART:20260420T000000Z
DTEND:20260420T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260218T230117Z
UID:bb98a282-0d1d-11f1-9d5d-52b0da6adf07
DESCRIPTION:https://thunderbirdmusichall.com/event/weedeater-w-conan-teleki
 netic-yeti-funerals/thunderbird-cafe-music-hall/pittsburgh-pennsylvania/\n
 \nWeedeaterConan\, Telekinetic Yeti\, FuneralsSunday April 19\, 2026Thunde
 rbird Music Hall4053 Butler Street\, Pittsburgh\, PADoors @ 7:00pmShow @ 7
 :30pmAGE RESTRICTION: 18+http://weedmetal.com/Weedeater was born the mid-
 ’90s\, in Wilmington\, NC\, originally taking shape as a side project of
  vocalist/bassist “Dixie” Dave Collins\, who was otherwise engaged wit
 h sludge metal cult favorites  at the time. However\, upon that band’s 
 official demise in 1998\, Collins was free to concentrate his efforts on W
 eedeater\, which released two sludgecore albums to kick off the new millen
 nium: 2001’s And Justice for Y’All and 2002’s Sixteen Tons\, both pr
 oduced by stoner specialist Billy Anderson. Collins later decided to tour 
 briefly as bass player for  and also found time to lend his four strings 
 to Wilmington neighbors\, but continued to work with Weedeater guitarist S
 hep and drummer Keko\, touring relentlessly over the years\, with the like
 s of C.O.C. and . Busy as he was\, Collins and co. finally got around to r
 ecording their third long-player\, God Luck and Good Speed\, which was rel
 ease through Southern Lord in 2007. ~ Eduardo Rivadavia\, Rovihttps://www.
 hailconan.com/Conan – the sound of unending hammer blows into the earth.
  A galloping charging war horse heading for your town. So heavy that the g
 ods look away\, intimidated by their unearthly delivery. https://telekine
 ticyeti.com/Based out of Iowa\, Telekinetic Yeti is a two-man band that de
 livers sonic brutality melded with psychedelic doom wizardry\, forged by t
 he worship of the almighty riff and honed by relentless touring and dedica
 tion to their craft.\n \nTicket Tier Info: GAGeneral Admission Tickets 
 – Standing Room Only\nThere are no additional entry protocols at this 
 time. Entry requirements are subject to change. By purchasing tickets to t
 his event you agree to abide by entry requirements in effect at the time
  of the event. Check the venue website leading up to your event for the l
 atest protocols. Please visit https://thunderbirdmusichall.com/safety/ for
  more information on Covid-19 Safety. All sales are final. 
LOCATION:Thunderbird Music Hall
END:VEVENT
