BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BOTTLEROCKET BOOK CLUB w/ PAAR
DTSTART:20260316T233000Z
DTEND:20260317T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20260220T035617Z
UID:1bdcf858-0e10-11f1-9d54-8aa4b99a53f6
DESCRIPTION:https://app.opendate.io/e/bottlerocket-book-club-w-paar-march-1
 6-2026-659461\n Calling all bookworms! Whether you’re a book lover or yo
 u’re seeking community and want to join a new club\, this is your chance
 ! It’s the VERY FIRST edition of the BOTTLEROCKET BOOK CLUB...Led by Pit
 tsburgh Action Against Rape!  We’ll be meeting in the bar to discuss the
  BOOK OF THE MONTH\, enjoying some cocktails (or mocktails) and having a g
 reat time! This is an inclusive event\, and all are welcome- even if it’
 s been a while since you’ve read anything!  For the FIRST EVER Bottleroc
 ket Book Club\, we’re diving into “SPEAK” by LAURIE HALSE ANDERSON w
 hich we recommend picking up locally at STAY GOLD BOOKS.  Book blurb: Spea
 k is Laurie Halse Anderson’s breakout young adult novel\, originally pub
 lished in 1999. The novel follows Melinda Sordino\, a high school freshman
  who becomes a social pariah when she calls the police to a party after sh
 e is sexually assaulted. Melinda stops speaking almost entirely as she gra
 pples with her isolation and the trauma of the assault. Through art\, she 
 reclaims her voice and begins to heal. In May\, Prime Stage Theater Compan
 y will debut the first theatrical production of the novel at the New Hazle
 tt Center for Performing Arts.  About PAAR: Pittsburgh Action Against Rape
  (PAAR) was the first victim service agency in Allegheny County\, and one 
 of the first rape crisis centers in the nation. The agency was incorporate
 d as a non-profit entity in 1972 and has been providing essential no-cost 
 services to victims of sexual violence in Allegheny County for 50 years. P
 AAR’s mission is to respond\, educate\, and advocate to end sexual viole
 nce. As of today\, PAAR is the only agency in Allegheny County solely devo
 ted to the issue of sexual violence. PAAR provides comprehensive services 
 to victims of sexual violence and to their families\, serving children and
  adults of all gender identities\, ages\, and socioeconomic backgrounds   
LOCATION:Bottlerocket Social Hall
END:VEVENT
