BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mars at Opposition
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20180727
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20180727
DTSTAMP:20260224T194005Z
UID:9e518596-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:CSVConvertd94e7b0f2175a96448c6c18e97a6565d\nJuly 27 - Mars at O
 pposition. The red planet will be at its closest approach to Earth and its
  face will be fully illuminated by the Sun. It will be brighter than any o
 ther time of the year and will be visible all night long. This is the best
  time to view and photograph Mars. A medium-sized telescope will allow you
  to see some of the dark details on the planet's orange surface.\n\nSource
 : <a href="http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2018.html">h
 ttp://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2018.html</a>
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
