BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Penumbral Lunar Eclipse
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20170211
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20170211
DTSTAMP:20260224T194006Z
UID:9ed795fa-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:CSVConvert81a47cc48c1449111f20faf3e432d2e5\nFebruary 11 - Penum
 bral Lunar Eclipse. A penumbral lunar eclipse occurs when the Moon passes 
 through the Earth's partial shadow or penumbra. During this type of eclips
 e the Moon will darken slightly but not completely. The eclipse will be vi
 sible throughout most of eastern South America\; eastern Canada\; the Atla
 ntic Ocean\; Europe\; Africa\; and western Asia.\n\nSource: <a href="http:
 //www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2017.html">http://www.seasky
 .org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2017.html</a>
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
