BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Full Moon / Supermoon
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20180102
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20180102
DTSTAMP:20260224T194006Z
UID:9eddae9a-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:CSVConvertb36ef8c261f29be2b9d035c3949e855f\nJanuary 2 - Full Mo
 on / Supermoon. The Moon will be located on the opposite side of the Earth
  as the Sun and its face will be will be fully illuminated. This phase occ
 urs at 02:24 UTC. This full moon was known by early Native American tribes
  as the Full Wolf Moon because this was the time of year when hungry wolf 
 packs howled outside their camps. This moon has also been know as the Old 
 Moon and the Moon After Yule. This is also the first of two supermoons for
  2018. The Moon will be at its closest approach to the Earth and may look 
 slightly larger and brighter than usual.\n\nSource: <a href="http://www.se
 asky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2018.html">http://www.seasky.org/ast
 ronomy/astronomy-calendar-2018.html</a>
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
