BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Geminids Meteor Shower
DTSTART:20181213T050000Z
DTEND:20181213T060000Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194006Z
UID:9f0505c6-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:CSVConvertdf860601c66e8c424a07bd14dd31a751\nDecember 13-14 - Ge
 minids Meteor Shower. The Geminids is the king of the meteor showers. It i
 s considered by many to be the best shower in the heavens producing up to 
 120 multicolored meteors per hour at its peak. It is produced by debris le
 ft behind by an asteroid known as 3200 Phaethon which was discovered in 19
 82. The shower runs annually from December 7-17. It peaks this year on the
  night of the 13th and morning of the 14th. The first quarter moon will se
 t shortly after midnight leaving dark skies for what should be an excellen
 t early morning show. Best viewing will be from a dark location after midn
 ight. Meteors will radiate from the constellation Gemini but can appear an
 ywhere in the sky.\n\nSource: <a href="http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/ast
 ronomy-calendar-2018.html">http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calen
 dar-2018.html</a>
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
