DESCRIPTION:CSVConvert9a277cbd0e58cdc00d61e687b8b34bc3\nJuly 2 - Total Sola
 r Eclipse. A total solar eclipse occurs when the moon completely blocks th
 e Sun revealing the Sun's beautiful outer atmosphere known as the corona. 
 The path of totality will only be visible in parts of the southern pacific
  Ocean\; central Chile\; and central Argentina. A partial eclipse will be 
 visible in most parts of the southern Pacific Ocean and western South Amer
 ica.\n\nSource: <a href="http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calenda
 r-2019.html">http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2019.html<
 /a>
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
