BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Astronomy Lecture
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20140916T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20140916T203000
DTSTAMP:20260224T194007Z
UID:9fd17278-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:vtmikrdfbi0r7kngu7184nm438_R20140916T233000@google.com\nSession
  2 on Sept.16 will take a look at the earliest fraction of time in the his
 tory of the universe\, called the Planck epoch after Nobel Prize-winning p
 hysicist\, Max Planck.\n\nLecture: The Big Bang and Then Some – a Layman
 ’s Perspective\n\nLearn about how everything we now enjoy in the night s
 ky got started.\n\nhttps://nightsky.jpl.nasa.gov/club/event-view.cfm?Event
 _ID=59333\n \nOpen Rain or shine\, cloudy or clear\n\nFour Tuesdays\, 7:30
  PM – 9:00 PM\,  September 9th\, 16th\, 23rd\, and 30th\n\n<a href="http
 ://www.post-gazette.com/local/south/2014/08/28/Seminar-series-takes-a-look
 -at-theBig-Bang/stories/201408250220#ixzz3CkN7WGSj">PG article</a>\n\nKD 7
 /16/2014\n\nUpdated KD 9/14/2014
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ursids Meteor Shower
DTSTART:20181221T050000Z
DTEND:20181221T060000Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194007Z
UID:9fd6fa0e-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:CSVConvert3705ac5ba2fc51c468c897ff0eafd5ca\nDecember 21-22 - Ur
 sids Meteor Shower. The Ursids is a minor meteor shower producing about 5-
 10 meteors per hour. It is produced by dust grains left behind by comet Tu
 ttle which was first discovered in 1790. The shower runs annually from Dec
 ember 17-25. It peaks this year on the the night of the 21st and morning o
 f the 22nd. This year the glare from the full moon will hide all but the b
 rightest meteors. If you are extremely patient you might still be able to 
 catch a few good ones. Best viewing will be just after midnight from a dar
 k location far away from city lights. Meteors will radiate from the conste
 llation Ursa Minor but can appear anywhere in the sky.\n\nSource: <a href=
 "http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2018.html">http://www.
 seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2018.html</a>
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:MeteorsWagmanCamelopardalids
DTSTART:20140524T053000Z
DTEND:20140524T063000Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194007Z
UID:9fda038e-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:piovp7crbd2vlpu2euvvvtiq1o@google.com\n\nWe will have the gates
  open by 1:30 AM Friday Night/Saturday morning for viewing the Cameloparda
 lids\, weather permitting\, of course.  It's too early to tell what the co
 nditions will be like or if this shower will put on an excellent show.  I 
 always have doubts about these predictions\, especially after Comets ISON 
 and PANSTARRS.  I do hope for the best.  Just being cautious.  \n \nTom Re
 iland  \n
LOCATION:Wagman Observatory\, Kurn Road\, Tarentum\, PA\, United States
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Membership Meeting
