BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Transit of Venus
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20120605
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20120605
DTSTAMP:20260224T194008Z
UID:a0001cc2-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:qsjtk2e87buig3iq2ftjs1k5uc@google.com\n\n\n\nhttp://www.transit
 ofvenus.org/\n\nProtect your eyes.  There are several safe ways to watch V
 enus transit the sun.  \n•Rear projection screen\n•Solar filtered tele
 scope\n•#14 or greater welding glass\n•Disposable "eclipse shades"\n
 •Live webcast\n•More\n\nLook for possible updates for viewing options 
 sponsored by AAAP.\n\nPosted Jan. 10\, 2012\, KD\n\n\nTransit of Venus\n\n
 Tuesday\, June 5\, 2012\n\nhttp://www.transitofvenus.org/\n\nLook for poss
 ible updates for viewing options sponsored by AAAP.\n\n \n\n\n\nProtect yo
 ur eyes. \n\nThere are several safe ways to watch Venus transit the sun.  
 \n\n•Rear projection screen\n\n•Solar filtered telescope\n\n•#14 or 
 greater welding glass\n\n•Disposable "eclipse shades"\n\n•Live webcast
 s\, http://www.transitofvenus.org/\n\n \n\n \n\n \n\nClear western horizon
 \, evening of June 5. \n\nTimes (Mingo Observatory):\n\ningress exterior\n
 \nJun 5\n18:04:05\n\ningress interior\n\nJun 5\n18:21:35\n\ntransit center
 \n\nJun 5\n21:27:30\n\negress interior\n\nJun 6\n00:33:02\n\negress exteri
 or\n\nJun 6\n00:50:55\n\nUpdate 6/2/2012  KD\n\n  We at Wagman Obs are ope
 n to the public that evening\, weather permitting from the start until sun
 set.  Publicity has been sent out to the media and it's been on facebook a
 s well.  We'll be open at 6 PM for the public. First contact for us\, depe
 nding on whose estimate you believe\, will be somewhere between 6:04 and 6
 :09.\n    By the way\, I don't think that we'll need to put up the parking
  lights only signs.  : )\n \nTom\n\n&\n\nAt Mingo we will view the transit
  from its beginning (6:04PM EDST) until 7:30 – 7:45 PM when the sun will
  be behind some trees.\n\n \n\nBill \n
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
