BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Draconids
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20111008
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20111008
DTSTAMP:20260224T194008Z
UID:a046c78a-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:l1o60dhntmtauodn8iag4s3eh4@google.com\nThe Draconids\, a period
 ic meteor shower\, have produced short-lived meteor storms (1933\nand 1946
 ) and enhanced rates during many other years. Most of these\noccurred when
  the parent comet\, 21P/Giacobini-Zinner returned to\nperihelion. The last
  time it did this was in 2005\, resulting in an\noutburst of about 35 mete
 ors per hour. The best chance to see\nactivity will be on October 8th and 
 9th.  The International Meteor\nOrganization (IMO) feels that 2011 will br
 ing a better chance for Draconids. KD10/06/2010
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
