BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Raccoon Creek/Hillman State Park Star Party
DTSTART:20161015T220000Z
DTEND:20161015T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194009Z
UID:a0cd677c-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:fn6ujo0lvv05ffu73voai2e3l4@google.com\nWe will hold a star part
 y at Raccoon State Park Saturday\, October 15\, 2016: starting at 6:15PM. 
 Actually the location is Hillman State Park which is adjacent to Raccoon. 
 This was announced early in the summer\, but we now have directions. \n\nG
 eorge Guzik will give a presentation starting at 6:15 followed by the star
  party on the radio controlled plane runway. This is on top of a hill with
  clear viewing in all directions.\n\nIf you would like to help out by brin
 ging a scope or binoculars\, or just be there to talk to the visitors\, pl
 ease reply to this and let me know. Info for AAAP Member Volunteers: Shane
  will provide detailed directions to the site.  It does involve driving up
  a pretty well maintained grave road.  \n\n-Fred Klein (09/07/16)\n\n-----
 --------------------------------\nDirections to Hillman SP's Radio Control
  Airport/Airfield\n\nFrom the North (Beaver)\n\nTake PA-18 south. Turn Lef
 t at Light in Florence onto Steubenville Pike Continue 1.5 miles on Steube
 nville Pike Turn Left on Haul Road Continue 1.7 miles on Haul Road (Gravel
  and Asphalt Road) Turn Right on Kramer Road (Gravel Road) Continue 0.7 mi
 les on Kramer Road and turn left into entrance of Hillman State Park's Mod
 el Airfield Follow gravel road to airfield at top of hill.\n\n**Please not
 e that once you enter Hillman State Park\, follow signage for Radio Contro
 l Model Airport to find Hillman State Park's Model Airfield.\n\n\nFrom the
  South (Burgettstown and Washington)\n\nTake PA-18 north. Turn Right at Li
 ght in Florence onto Steubenville Pike Continue 1.5 miles on Steubenville 
 Pike Turn Left on Haul Road Continue 1.7 miles on Haul Road (Gravel and As
 phalt Road) Turn Right on Kramer Road (Gravel Road) Continue 0.7 miles on 
 Kramer Road and turn left into entrance of Hillman State Park's Model Airf
 ield Follow gravel road to airfield at top of hill.\n\n**Please note that 
 once you enter Hillman State Park\, follow signage for Radio Control Model
  Airport to find Hillman State Park's Model Airfield.\n\n\nFrom East (Pitt
 sburgh)\n\nTake US-22 West. Take the PA-18 exit for Florence/Burgettstown 
 Turn Left at Light onto PA-18 North Turn Right at Light onto Steubenville 
 Pike Continue 1.5 miles on Steubenville Pike Turn Left on Haul Road Contin
 ue 1.7 miles on Haul Road (Gravel and Asphalt Road) Turn Right on Kramer R
 oad (Gravel Road) Continue 0.7 miles on Kramer Road and turn left into ent
 rance of Hillman State Park's Model Airfield Follow gravel road to airfiel
 d at top of hill.\n\n**Please note that once you enter Hillman State Park\
 , follow signage for Radio Control Model Airport to find Hillman State Par
 k's Model Airfield.\n\n\nFrom West (Weirton and Steubenville)\n\nTake US-2
 2 East. Take the PA-18 exit for Florence/Burgettstown Turn Left onto PA-18
  North. Turn Right at Light onto Steubenville Pike Continue 1.5 miles on S
 teubenville Pike Turn Left on Haul Road Continue 1.7 miles on Haul Road (G
 ravel and Asphalt Road) Turn Right on Kramer Road (Gravel Road) Continue 0
 .7 miles on Kramer Road and turn left into entrance of Hillman State Park'
 s Model Airfield Follow gravel road to airfield at top of hill.\n\n**Pleas
 e note that once you enter Hillman State Park\, follow signage for Radio C
 ontrol Model Airport to find Hillman State Park's Model Airfield.\n-------
 ------------------------------\n\nStar Party at Hillman State Park\nMeetin
 g location will be emailed to registered attendees.\nSaturday\, October 15
 \, 2016: starting at 6:15PM\n\nAs the sky begins to darken and the stars c
 ome out\, join the Amateur Astronomers Association of Pittsburgh (AAAP) to
  learn about and see some of the amazing celestial objects in the night sk
 y. Following a short presentation (45 minutes)\, we will head out and look
  at some of the items in the night sky with a variety of telescopes (basic
  and advanced models)\, and you may stay as long as you like for this seco
 nd part. Please note this program is weather permitting\, so if the sky is
  overcast or rain is forecasted\, the program will be rescheduled. If the 
 sky is clear or a few scattered clouds\, the Star Party is a go. You may b
 ring your telescope to use or look through one set up by the AAAP. Please 
 remember to bring extra layers of clothing for program since it can get qu
 ite cool at night. To fully enjoy the night sky and faint objects in teles
 copes\, the use of use cell phones\, white lights or flashlights\, glow st
 icks\, and flash photography is not permitted. To register\, please visit 
 DCNR website at (add website site location later)\, and for question\, cal
 l Shane Miller at 724-899-3611.\n\nHave a good day\,\n\nShane Miller | Env
 ironmental Education Specialist Department of Conservation\n& Natural Reso
 urces Bureau of State Parks | Raccoon Creek/Hillman State Park\nComplex\n3
 000 State Route 18 | Hookstown\, PA 15050\nPhone: 724.899.3611 Fax: 724.89
 9.2290\nEmail: shanemille@pa.gov\nwww.dcnr.state.pa.us | www.friendsofracc
 oon.org\n-------------------------------------\n\nHere is a link to the si
 te:\n\nSite Location: <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/place/Model+Air
 plane+Field\,+Burgettstown\,+PA+15021/@40.4620125\,-80.4058862\,14.53z/dat
 a=!4m5!3m4!1s0x883446c3028c2231:0xfa9efee35deb2377!8m2!3d40.4606081!4d-80.
 3970911">https://www.google.com/maps/place/Model+Airplane+Field\,+Burgetts
 town\,+PA+15021/@40.4620125\,-80.4058862\,14.53z/data=!4m5!3m4!1s0x883446c
 3028c2231:0xfa9efee35deb2377!8m2!3d40.4606081!4d-80.3970911</a>\n\nRaccoon
  Creek Events Calendar: <a href="http://events.dcnr.pa.gov/raccoon_creek_s
 tate_park/calendar">http://events.dcnr.pa.gov/raccoon_creek_state_park/cal
 endar</a>\n\nThe sky conditions for October 15.\n6:39  Sunset (259 degrees
 )\n6:42 Moon Rise (84 degrees)\n7:07 Civil Twilight\n7:38 Nautical Twiligh
 t\, deep space objects visible\n8:08 Venus sets (242 degrees)\n9:14 Saturn
  sets\n\nPlanets visible Venus\, Saturn\, Neptune\, Uranus\, Moon Many dee
 p sky objects including Globular Cluster M13 Ring Nebula M57 Open Cluster 
 M11 Andromeda Galaxy M31\n\nI think we should advertise start of party as 
 7PM\, but mention Full Moon rise at 6:42 (moon is full at 4:32 next mornin
 g). The talk would start at 6:15 \n\nIf you would like to help with this\,
  please let me know.\nFred K\n\nKD 05/25/2016\n
LOCATION:Hillman State Park\, Burgettstown\, PA 15021\, USA
END:VEVENT
