BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Better Observing Classes
DTSTART:20150902T233000Z
DTEND:20150903T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194009Z
UID:a0f60b14-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:ihpt93aqujunas1rs3kb0k1dbs@google.com\nAAAP Members\, \n\nI hav
 e scheduled the Better Observing Techniques Classes for Sep 2 & 3 and Sep 
 30 & Oct 1 (Wednesdays & Thursdays) at Wagman Observatory starting at 7:30
  PM\, weather permitting.  If you need assistance with your scopes\, colli
 mation of your Newtonian scopes or other optics\, bring them to these sess
 ions.\n \nTom Reiland
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AAS Eclipse 2017 Workshop
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20160610
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20160610
DTSTAMP:20260224T194009Z
UID:a0fb24a0-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:6m2738p1750t7v89khoionh2v8@google.com\nThe Astronomical Associa
 tion of Southern Illinois would like to invite you to the next American As
 tronomical Society Eclipse 2017 workshop to be held on the campus of South
 ern Illinois University Carbondale\, Friday\, June 10 and Saturday\, June 
 11\, 2016. The workshop will feature two days of top national speakers pre
 senting and hosting break out sessions on the 2017 eclipse. Individuals in
 volved in eclipse event and outreach planning are encouraged to attend as 
 a full participant and take part in all sessions including the closed sess
 ions on Day 2. All other sessions will be open to the general public\, whi
 ch must register in advance. Day 2 will also include a Citizen CATE Experi
 ment workshop open to registered participants and pubic. The workshop take
 s place in Carbondale\, Illinois at the SIU Carbondale Student Center. All
  attendees must register in advance.\n\nRegistration costs: \nGeneral Publ
 ic - $10 (Day 1)\; $12 (Day 1 and Day 2)\nCitizen CATE Workshop only - $20
  (Day 2)\nFull Participant - $180  (includes all meals\, sessions\, and lo
 cal transportation)\nStudent Participant - $80 (Includes all meals\, sessi
 ons\, and local transportation)\n\nMore information and registration info 
 at: \n\n<a href="http://conferenceservices.siu.edu/conferences/eclipse-wor
 kshop.html">http://conferenceservices.siu.edu/conferences/eclipse-workshop
 .html</a>\n\n<a href="http://eclipse.siu.edu/about-the-eclipse/american-as
 tronomical-society-eclipse-2017-workshop/">http://eclipse.siu.edu/about-th
 e-eclipse/american-astronomical-society-eclipse-2017-workshop/</a>\n \nPRE
 SENTERS INCLUDE:\nMichael Bakich\, Astronomy Magazine\nDavid Baron\, forme
 r NPR correspondent\nBob Baer\, SIU Carbondale eclipse committee\nFred Esp
 enak\, “Mr. Eclipse”\nDon Ficken\, St. Louis Astronomical Society\, St
 . Louis Eclipse Task Force\nChris Giersh\, NASA Edge\nShadia Habbal\, Insi
 tute for Astronomy\, University of Hawaii\nLou Mayo\, NASA Eclipse 2017\nM
 ichelle Nichols\, Adler Planetarium\nTaryn Maon\, Alder\, Planetarium\nMat
 t Penn\, NSO\, Citizen CATE Experiment\nJay Ryan\, AmericanEclipseUSA.com\
 nJim Todd\, Oregon Museum of Science and Industry\nMark Stevens\, Stargeez
 erAstronomy.com\nErnie Wright\, NASA Goddard Space Flight Center\nMichael 
 Zeiler\, GreatAmericanEclipse.com\nCharles Fulco\, former Planetarium and 
 Space Sciences Director\, Port Chester (NY) Public Schools\nMike Kentriana
 kis\, AAS Solar Eclipse Project Manager for Eclipse 2017.\nDan McGlaun\, E
 clipse2017.org\nLuca Quaglia\, Flash Spectrum Cinematography\nCinnamon Whe
 eles-Smith\, Carbondale Tourism\nXavier Jubier\, Google Interactive Eclisp
 e Maps
LOCATION:SIU Student Recreation Center\, 300 E Grand Ave\, Carbondale\, IL 
 62901\, United States
END:VEVENT
