BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Full Moon
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20170312
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20170312
DTSTAMP:20260224T194010Z
UID:a15ed63a-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:CSVConverta017fd058c90fcee05086b9c1246a2fe\nMarch 12 - Full Moo
 n. The Moon will be located on the opposite side of the Earth as the Sun a
 nd its face will be will be fully illuminated. This phase occurs at 14:54 
 UTC. This full moon was known by early Native American tribes as the Full 
 Worm Moon because this was the time of year when the ground would begin to
  soften and the earthworms would reappear. This moon has also been known a
 s the Full Crow Moon\; the Full Crust Moon\; the Full Sap Moon\; and the L
 enten Moon.\n\nSource: <a href="http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-
 calendar-2017.html">http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-201
 7.html</a>
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Allegheny Observatory Open House
DTSTART:20180928T230000Z
DTEND:20180929T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194010Z
UID:a161a86a-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:5l8fqhclim88uah5rqd0aqhf1n@google.com\nThe Allegheny Observator
 y Open house is held once a year and it differs from the tour in that more
  of the building is opened to the public.  Instead of having a tour guide\
 , you follow a designated tour path around the building.  Both of the main
  telescopes are outfitted for visual use and the members of the Amateur As
 tronomers Association of Pittsburgh set up additional telescopes on the fr
 ont lawn. Open house is a family night therefore the maximum group size is
  approximately six.\n\nYou must get tickets to this event and they are fre
 e of charge you may do so by calling Allegheny Observatory at 412-321-2400
 . Reservations will be taken beginning at 9:00 a.m. Wednesday August 1st 2
 018. 
LOCATION:159 Riverview Ave\, Pittsburgh\, PA 15214\, USA
END:VEVENT
