BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AskNobelWinnerDL
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20091030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20091030
DTSTAMP:20260224T194011Z
UID:a1e1b4f6-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:1s5kcn5dv886b2si8cktqsrjtg@google.com\nhttp://www.youtube.com/t
 henobelprize  \n\nAsk a Nobel Laureate\, John Mather \nFrom: thenobelprize
  | October 20\, 2009 | 977 views \nHave you ever wanted to put your questi
 on directly to a Nobel Laureate? Now is your chance! NASA's John Mather\, 
 recipient of the 2006 Nobel Prize in Physics for measuring the echoes of t
 he Big Bang\, will answer a selection of your video questions. Upload your
  question by clicking below and posting a video response. The deadline for
  questions is 30 OCTOBER. Anyone can ask a question\, and you can post as 
 many questions as you like!\n\nSOME TIPS:\nBe original and personal -- Cho
 ose your own approach\, your perspective is important. \n\nKeep it brief -
 - Your question should ideally be less than 30 seconds. \n\nLook good -- K
 eep that camera steady and speak loudly. \n\nProvide context -- Let us kno
 w who you are\, and where you live\, work or study. \n\nRate your favourit
 e questions\, and a selection of the most popular questions will be answer
 ed by John Mather. Keep checking the playlist to see new questions and the
  most popular questions and/or topics. \n\nPlease note -- All videos are s
 ubject to the YouTube terms of use. By submitting a video\, you also grant
  Nobelprize.org a licence to reproduce and communicate the video to the pu
 blic at its discretion. \n\n\nKD 10/21/09
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
