DESCRIPTION:CSVConvert1a742dc05c2180538cb010c07c4a8ce9\nApril 16 - New Moon
 . The Moon will located on the same side of the Earth as the Sun and will 
 not be visible in the night sky. This phase occurs at 01:58 UTC. This is t
 he best time of the month to observe faint objects such as galaxies and st
 ar clusters because there is no moonlight to interfere.\n\nSource: <a href
 ="http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2018.html">http://www
 .seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2018.html</a>
LOCATION:None
