DESCRIPTION:7dnlgfihaafs87o9ckv2c2qrnr@google.com\nGeneral Business Meeting
 \nGuest Speaker and Topic: Prof. Arthur Kosowky presents "Simons Observato
 ry: The Next Great Microwave Telescopes". \n\nArthur Kosowky is the curren
 t physics and astronomy department chair at the University of Pittsburgh. 
 Bio: https://bit.ly/2N2hpor\n\nAAAP meetings are always free and open to t
 he public. This meeting will take place in Room 343 of Alumni Hall on the 
 University of Pittsburgh campus in Oakland.\n\nParking Information: There 
 is street parking on all of the streets around Alumni Hall which is free a
 fter 6:00p.m.  The under ground parking garage at Soldiers and Sailors Mem
 orial Hall is a $5.00 flat rate after 4:00p.m.  Be carful not to park on a
 ny surface lot\, most of those are owned by the university and they are en
 forced 24 hours a day.
LOCATION:4227 Fifth Ave\, Pittsburgh\, PA 15260
END:VEVENT
