BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Delta Aquarids Meteor Shower
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20190728
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20190728
DTSTAMP:20260224T194013Z
UID:a35893cc-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:CSVConvert0a72c49713fdf97ebedc996d861d4904\nJuly 28-29 - Delta 
 Aquarids Meteor Shower. The Delta Aquarids is an average shower that can p
 roduce up to 20 meteors per hour at its peak. It is produced by debris lef
 t behind by comets Marsden and Kracht. The shower runs annually from July 
 12 to August 23. It peaks this year on the night of July 28 and morning of
  July 29. The waning crescent moon will not be too much of a problem this 
 year. The skies should be dark enough for what could be a good show. Best 
 viewing will be from a dark location after midnight. Meteors will radiate 
 from the constellation Aquarius but can appear anywhere in the sky.
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
