BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:New Moon
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20190504
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20190504
DTSTAMP:20260224T194014Z
UID:a3a408b6-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:CSVConvert29fc0da62b951cb5fd0d37908f5129a9\nMay 4 - New Moon. T
 he Moon will located on the same side of the Earth as the Sun and will not
  be visible in the night sky. This phase occurs at 22:46 UTC. This is the 
 best time of the month to observe faint objects such as galaxies and star 
 clusters because there is no moonlight to interfere.\n\nSource: <a href="h
 ttp://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2019.html">http://www.se
 asky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2019.html</a>
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:New Moon
