DESCRIPTION:do063mabda1eknt81u18pqrnhs@google.com\nUPDATE: Due to a resourc
 e conflict\, this class had to be cancelled.\n\nLearn Astro-Photography Ba
 sics from One of Our Best Imagers\n\nLong-time Guide Star readers are sure
 ly impressed by the quality of AAAP images in the newsletter’s “Astro-
 Atmo” section. Most rank right up there with what is shown in Sky & Tele
 scope and Astronomy magazines. If you like to take a crack at modern astro
 -imaging\, you can attend a free class this month given by Frank Weilgus\,
  one of most accomplished (and published) imagers. The date is September 1
 6\, the time is 7:30 pm and the location is Wagman Observatory. No need to
  sign up\, just show up. Bring your cameras too if you have any questions 
 for Frank.
LOCATION:Wagman Observatory\, 225 Kurn Rd\, Tarentum\, PA 15084\, USA
END:VEVENT
