DESCRIPTION:CSVConvert7b12fb2b08bcca8d251646a72416c3f0\nFebruary 15 - New M
 oon. The Moon will located on the same side of the Earth as the Sun and wi
 ll not be visible in the night sky. This phase occurs at 21:05 UTC. This i
 s the best time of the month to observe faint objects such as galaxies and
  star clusters because there is no moonlight to interfere.\n\nSource: <a h
 ref="http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2018.html">http://
 www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2018.html</a>
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
