BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:New Moon
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20180117
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20180117
DTSTAMP:20260224T194018Z
UID:a5f19444-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:CSVConvert6f74693e1d24dc9a7aadf56bd8b7afee\nJanuary 17 - New Mo
 on. The Moon will located on the same side of the Earth as the Sun and wil
 l not be visible in the night sky. This phase occurs at 02:17 UTC. This is
  the best time of the month to observe faint objects such as galaxies and 
 star clusters because there is no moonlight to interfere.\n\nSource: <a hr
 ef="http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2018.html">http://w
 ww.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2018.html</a>
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
