BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ursids Meteor Shower
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20191221
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20191221
DTSTAMP:20260224T194018Z
UID:a606ae6a-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:CSVConvertc812492afc014616763c7843c7f71d8f\nDecember 21-22 - Ur
 sids Meteor Shower. The Ursids is a minor meteor shower producing about 5-
 10 meteors per hour. It is produced by dust grains left behind by comet Tu
 ttle which was first discovered in 1790. The shower runs annually from Dec
 ember 17 - 25. It peaks this year on the the night of the 21st and morning
  of the 22nd. The waning crescent moon should not interfere too much this 
 year. Skies should still be dark enough for what could be a good show. Bes
 t viewing will be just after midnight from a dark location far away from c
 ity lights. Meteors will radiate from the constellation Ursa Minor but can
  appear anywhere in the sky.
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Perseids
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20120811
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20120811
DTSTAMP:20260224T194018Z
UID:a60be1aa-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:52qc31aflumhfvdbdjq1eh4guc@google.com\nStarting at mid to late 
 evening on the nights of August 11/12 and 12/13\, watch for the Perseid me
 teors to streak across this short summer night from late night until dawn\
 , with only a little interference from the waning crescent moon.\n\nKD 7/2
 4/12
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
