UID:a646c68a-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:CSVConvert2697a90f866e4dc7a3a8de9a5b5d494f\nAugust 11 - New Moo
 n. The Moon will located on the same side of the Earth as the Sun and will
  not be visible in the night sky. This phase occurs at 09:58 UTC. This is 
 the best time of the month to observe faint objects such as galaxies and s
 tar clusters because there is no moonlight to interfere.\n\nSource: <a hre
 f="http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2018.html">http://ww
 w.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2018.html</a>
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
