BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Penumbral Lunar Eclipse 6:32AM
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20111210
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20111210
DTSTAMP:20260224T194018Z
UID:a653b39a-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:guasjn4rp2khf1p5u8mka0mbao@google.com\nThe Moon Disappears in E
 arth's Shadow: Dec 10th  \n\nA penumbral eclipse will be visible from most
  of the East Coast\, starting at 6:32 A.M. EST\, just before the Moon sets
  (7:30AM EST).\n\nServe coffee to your neighbors as you watch the Moon set
 (7:30AM EST)\, eclipsed in Earth's shadow (starting at 6:32 A.M. EST)\, an
 d turn around and watch the Sun rise(7:31AM EST)\, morning of Saturday\, D
 ecember 10th.\n\nShow them why eclipses happen using the activity* from th
 e Shadows & Silhouettes ToolKit:\n\n* Download the activity here:  http://
 nightsky.jpl.nasa.gov/download-view.cfm?Doc_ID=327 \n\nNo matter where you
  are\, you can join a webcast with Star Gazers\, featuring NSN member Dean
  Regas from the Cincinnati Observatory.\n\nhttp://www.stargazersonline.org
 /webcast/ \n\nDetails on the eclipse:\nhttp://eclipse.gsfc.nasa.gov/OH/OH2
 011.html#LE2011Dec10T \n\n\n\n December 10\, 2011\n Rises Sets Day Length 
 \nSun 7:31 A.M. 4:54 P.M. 09:23 \nMoon 5:06 P.M. 7:30 A.M.  \nMercury 6:21
  A.M. 4:14 P.M.  \nVenus 9:45 A.M. 6:56 P.M.  \nMars 11:32 P.M. 12:39 P.M.
   \nJupiter 2:20 P.M. 3:40 A.M.  \nSaturn 3:12 A.M. 2:21 P.M.  \nUranus 1:
 05 P.M. 1:10 A.M.  \nNeptune 11:47 A.M. 10:25 P.M.  \nPluto 8:37 A.M. 6:25
  P.M.  \n\nKD 11/7/2011
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
