BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:New Moon
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20190928
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20190928
DTSTAMP:20260224T194020Z
UID:a73e8730-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:CSVConverta647fcb0a33465463026472ad7cfdbdc\nSeptember 28 - New 
 Moon. The Moon will located on the same side of the Earth as the Sun and w
 ill not be visible in the night sky. This phase occurs at 18:26 UTC. This 
 is the best time of the month to observe faint objects such as galaxies an
 d star clusters because there is no moonlight to interfere.\n\nSource: <a 
 href="http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2019.html">http:/
 /www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2019.html</a>
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
