BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AO Open House
DTSTART:20141010T230000Z
DTEND:20141011T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194020Z
UID:a75362b8-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:smo6s0u3ek15t8hmg29a642mv8@google.com\nAlleghney Observatory Op
 en House will be on Friday the 10th of October starting at 7:00P.M.  We ne
 ed volunteers for various spots inside of the building and people to bring
  telescopes to setup on the front lawn.  If you would like to volunteer\, 
 let me know.\n\nThanks.\nLou \n\nAs per Lou's list post\n\nKD\n\nhttp://ww
 w.post-gazette.com/local/city/2013/08/01/Reservations-being-taken-for-Alle
 gheny-Observatory-open-house/stories/201308010326\n\n\nPittsburgh Post-Gaz
 ette\nReservations for the free annual open house at Allegheny Observatory
  will be taken by phone beginning at 9 a.m. today.\n\nOpen house at the hi
 storic observatory in the city's Riverview Park will be held from 7 to 10 
 p.m. Friday\, Oct. 11. Groups will be permitted to enter the building ever
 y half hour.\n\nDuring open house\, visitors see and look though the 30-in
 ch Thaw Refractor\, the observatory's primary research instrument. The 13-
 inch Fitz-Clark also will show off the night sky.\n\nMembers of the Amateu
 r Astronomers Association of Pittsburgh will set up portable telescopes on
  the lawn for public viewing.\n\nParticipants will enter the observatory e
 very half-hour and will begin the self-guided tour with an introductory ta
 lk in the lecture hall.\n\nSpace is limited and registration is a must. Ca
 ll 412-321-2400.\nnning at 9 a.m. today.\n\nOpen house at the historic obs
 ervatory in the city's Riverview Park will be held from 7 to 10 p.m. Frida
 y\, Oct. 11. Groups will be permitted to enter the building every half hou
 r.\n\nDuring open house\, visitors see and look though the 30-inch Thaw Re
 fractor\, the observatory's primary research instrument. The 13-inch Fitz-
 Clark also will show off the night sky.\n\nMembers of the Amateur Astronom
 ers Association of Pittsburgh will set up portable telescopes on the lawn 
 for public viewing.\n\nParticipants will enter the observatory every half-
 hour and will begin the self-guided tour with an introductory talk in the 
 lecture hall.\n\nSpace is limited and registration is a must. Call 412-321
 -2400.\n\nPG
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
