BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Earth Hour 830-9:30PM
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20110326
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20110326
DTSTAMP:20260224T194022Z
UID:a8675e52-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:3p10iv50p7bkaq9th96bpaeaus@google.com\nEven if you cannot be at
  Carnegie Science Center that morning or afternoon\, or at Mingo Observato
 ry\, perhaps you can share the stars in your own neighborhood for Earth Ho
 ur 2011. http://journeytothestars.wordpress.com/2011/02/15/go-beyond-the-h
 our-earth-hour-2011/\n\nHere is a link to the 2011 Earth Hour Video: http:
 //www.youtube.com/watch?v=4Mxjbip6y04&feature=player_embedded\n\nThe Earth
  Hour Website states: Billed as the largest voluntary event ever witnessed
 \, Earth Hour will be observed on Saturday\, March 26 at 8:30 p.m. (local 
 time) with millions of people around the world turning off their lights in
  celebration of the one thing we all have in common – our planet. Gather
  friends or family for this simple act that saves energy\, reduces polluti
 on\, and nurtures a conservation spirit. When the lights go back on\, thin
 k about what else you can do to make a difference. Save the date and sign 
 up now. http://www.earthhour.org/Homepage.aspx?vote
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
