BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Total Lunar Eclipse
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20190121
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20190121
DTSTAMP:20260224T194022Z
UID:a89620d4-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:CSVConvertf260450e3fdb51c4364a4d25abe60853\nJanuary 21 - Total 
 Lunar Eclipse. A total lunar eclipse occurs when the Moon passes completel
 y through the Earth's dark shadow (or umbra). During this type of eclipse 
 the Moon will gradually get darker and then take on a rusty or blood red c
 olor. The eclipse will be visible throughout most of North America\; South
  America\; the eastern Pacific Ocean\; western Atlantic Ocean\; extreme we
 stern Europe\; and extreme western Africa.\n\nSource: <a href="http://www.
 seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2019.html">http://www.seasky.org/a
 stronomy/astronomy-calendar-2019.html</a>
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
