BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Covered Bridge Festival 
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20150919
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20150919
DTSTAMP:20260224T194023Z
UID:a8df7f72-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:ou6dkdi54g6hf0j5b8jhjkml80@google.com\nCovered Bridge Festival 
 \nHeld the third weekend of September each year\, this signature event kic
 ks off the Fall festival season. 2015 it coincides with a Mingo Star Party
  Weekend. The  Ebenezer Bridge in Mingo Creek County Park is one of the 10
  festival locations offers a charming atmosphere and an array of activitie
 s\, including hand-made arts & crafts\, homestyle food\, historic re-enact
 ments\, demonstrations\, children's activities & live entertainment. It tr
 aw a tremendous crowd and therefore traffic patterns are regulated during 
 festival hours.\n\nThe "upper festival" involved the Ballfield Area\, Mans
 ion Hill Road Extension ( ie the road abover the "lower gate."  The refuse
  truck use Shelter 10 Road.\n\n           \n\nClick <a href="http://visitw
 ashingtoncountypa.com/CustomPage.aspx?Name=44thcoveredbridgefestival.aspx"
 >45th annual Washington & Greene Counties'\n\nCovered Bridge Festival</a>\
 n\n\nKD 3/28/2015
LOCATION:Ebernezer Covered Bridge\, Mingo Creek County Park
END:VEVENT
