UID:a90eba08-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:CSVConvert246049b4086d884d06c5973d091a1399\nFebruary 4 - New Mo
 on. The Moon will located on the same side of the Earth as the Sun and wil
 l not be visible in the night sky. This phase occurs at 21:03 UTC. This is
  the best time of the month to observe faint objects such as galaxies and 
 star clusters because there is no moonlight to interfere.\n\nSource: <a hr
 ef="http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2019.html">http://w
 ww.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2019.html</a>
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
