SUMMARY:Mercury at Greatest Eastern Elongation
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20170401
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20170401
DTSTAMP:20260224T194024Z
UID:a9a27cb6-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:CSVConvert4146794476eb662000bd704272f3738e\nApril 1 - Mercury a
 t Greatest Eastern Elongation. The planet Mercury reaches greatest eastern
  elongation of 19 degrees from the Sun. This is the best time to view Merc
 ury since it will be at its highest point above the horizon in the evening
  sky. Look for the planet low in the western sky just after sunset.\n\nSou
 rce: <a href="http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2017.html
 ">http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2017.html</a>
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
