BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Canc.Better Observing Tech Class Class
DTSTART:20141014T230000Z
DTEND:20141015T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194024Z
UID:aa03f7ac-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:j9mp3k4f6ah8gab67qqfi8u1qs@google.com\nTue. 10/14/2014 Cancelle
 d\n\nAn announcement from Tom Reiland\, Director of Wagman Observatory:\nI
 'll be conducting classes on how to find celestial objects without the use
  of a stinking computer. The method is called Starhopping and it's how I n
 avigate around the night sky with my nude eyes\, binoculars and telescopes
 . If I had been using a Goto system all these year\, I would have not disc
 overed Reiland's Cluster (or Reiland 1) and the Supernova in the Whirlpool
  Galaxy.\nThese classes will be on four nights. It will be the same sessio
 n each night. You choose which one is convenient for you. They start at 7 
 PM and last until all of the students have left. Classes will be on Monday
 s and Tuesdays. Sept 15 and 16 and Oct 13 and 14 at Wagman Observatory.\nT
 hey're free\, but you can make a donation if you want. Let me know if yinz
  are interested 'n'at. (Tom Reiland\, Instructor)\n\n\nKD 7/15/2014
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
