BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Total Lunar Eclipse
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20180727
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20180727
DTSTAMP:20260224T194026Z
UID:ab18a2f0-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:CSVConvert71ac388913000b272341f7b04a1ba212\nJuly 27 - Total Lun
 ar Eclipse. A total lunar eclipse occurs when the Moon passes completely t
 hrough the Earth's dark shadow or umbra. During this type of eclipse the M
 oon will gradually get darker and then take on a rusty or blood red color.
  The eclipse will be visible throughout most of Europe\; Africa\; western 
 and central Asia\; the Indian Ocean\; and Western Australia. (NASA Map and
  Eclipse Information)\n\nSource: <a href="http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/
 astronomy-calendar-2018.html">http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-ca
 lendar-2018.html</a>
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
