BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Astronomy Lecture
DTSTART:20140930T233000Z
DTEND:20141001T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194027Z
UID:ab520f5e-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:i6f4ei01mjrg512g57f1rjps38@google.com\nThe final session of the
  series on Sept. 30\, "Afterglow\," will take the audience up to 10 second
 s after the Big Bang and then leap forward to 380\,000 years. It will cove
 r the remnants of the Big Bang called the cosmic microwave background\, wh
 ich is still evident in the universe.\n\n\nLecture: The Big Bang and Then 
 Some – a Layman’s Perspective\n\nLearn about how everything we now enj
 oy in the night sky got started.\n\nhttps://nightsky.jpl.nasa.gov/club/eve
 nt-view.cfm?Event_ID=59333\n \nOpen Rain or shine\, cloudy or clear\n\nFou
 r Tuesdays\, 7:30 PM – 9:00 PM\,  September 9th\, 16th\, 23rd\, and 30th
 \n\n\n\n<a href="http://www.post-gazette.com/local/south/2014/08/28/Semina
 r-series-takes-a-look-at-theBig-Bang/stories/201408250220#ixzz3CkN7WGSj">P
 G article</a>\n\nKD 7/16/2014\n\nUpdated KD 9/14/2014
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
