BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Martian Meteor Storm
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20141019
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20141019
DTSTAMP:20260224T194027Z
UID:ab971fb8-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:e6kmd6tdljgb90s2qr2qb6jvlc@google.com\nOn October 19\, 2014\, C
 omet C/2013 A1 (Siding Spring)\nwill pass within 120\,000 km of Mars.\nThi
 s is closer than all known Earth-comet encounters.\nA collision has been r
 uled out\, but Mars and its manmade\nsatellites will pass through the coma
  and tail.\nMars will be showered with meteors and satellites will\nhave a
 n increased risk of meteoroid impacts.\n\nKD 8/29/2014
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
