BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Annular Solar Eclipse
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20191226
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20191226
DTSTAMP:20260224T194027Z
UID:abb478ce-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:CSVConvert5371d40abfe372c9d3a254c80438dda5\nDecember 26 - Annul
 ar Solar Eclipse. An annular solar eclipse occurs when the Moon is too far
  away from the Earth to completely cover the Sun. This results in a ring o
 f light around the darkened Moon. The Sun's corona is not visible during a
 n annular eclipse. The path of of the eclipse will begin in Saudi Arabia a
 nd move east through southern India\; northern Sri Lanka\; parts of the In
 dian Ocean\; and Indonesia before ending in the Pacific Ocean. A partial e
 clipse will be visible throughout most of Asia and northern Australia.\n\n
 Source: <a href="http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2019.h
 tml">http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2019.html</a>
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
