BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY: Eta Aquarids Meteor Shower
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20160506
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20160506
DTSTAMP:20260224T194028Z
UID:abe4c74a-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:7kmkdudc52cs22b27qnkblg5jk@google.com\nBright Moon phases will 
 obscure many of this year’s best meteor showers\, but a new Moon on the 
 night of May 6 ensures dark skies for the Eta Aquarids\, which is composed
  of the remnants of the famous Comet Halley. Meteors—up to 30 per hour i
 n the Northern Hemisphere and 60 per hour in the Southern—will appear to
  radiate from Aquarius.\n\nSource: <a href="http://www.telescopes.com/blog
 s/helpful-information/46104069-the-best-celestial-events-of-2016">http://w
 ww.telescopes.com/blogs/helpful-information/46104069-the-best-celestial-ev
 ents-of-2016</a>\n\nPosted by Kathy Desantis ( <a href="mailto:kappa@3ap.o
 rg">kappa@3ap.org</a> ).
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
