BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kunkle Park Star Party
DTSTART:20180916T010000Z
DTEND:20180916T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194028Z
UID:ac51379a-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:5bc39t9mmaunhvaolqmnoaeab9@google.com\nSee craters\, fissures a
 nd mountains on the moon.  The planet Mars and it polar caps will be visib
 le throughout the evening\, as will Jupiter and several of its large moons
 . Saturn with its ring system and several moons will be a showpiece object
  and the small blue-green dot of the sun’s most distant planet\, Neptune
 \, will also be visible.  We will see beautiful star clusters in our Milky
  Way Galaxy.  Planetary nebulae\, the remnants of exploded stars like our 
 sun will also be visible.  Distant galaxies will also be observed.\n\nThey
  are all part of the show during the Amateur Astronomers Association of Pi
 ttsburgh’s FREE Star Gazing Party at Kunkle Park\, in Washington Townshi
 p (south of Apollo).  This star gazing party is scheduled for Saturday\, S
 eptember 15\, 2018\, starting at dusk\, WEATHER PERMITTING. \n\nKunkle Par
 k is located behind the Washington Township Municipal Building.  For GPS u
 sers\, that’s 285 Pine Run Church Road\, Apollo\, PA 15613.  (Near the S
 tate Police barracks on Route 66.)  GPS users can also insert the followin
 g coordinates: 40 degrees\, 32.92 minutes north latitude\, 79 degrees\, 36
 .26 minutes west longitude.\n\nFor more astronomy information and details 
 about AAAP club meetings and observatories\,check out our web page at: www
 .3ap.org\n\nContact: Terry Trees - (724) 337-3231 - ( treest@comcast.net )
LOCATION:285 Pine Run Church Rd\, Apollo\, PA 15613\, USA
END:VEVENT
