END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Comet Elenin
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20111013
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20111013
DTSTAMP:20260224T194028Z
UID:ac5c89f6-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:een2aedjhngrk062u9kehdc8g0@google.com\nComet Elenin\n\nComet El
 enin should be at its brightest shortly before the time of its closest app
 roach to Earth on Oct. 16\, 2011. At its closest point\, it will be 22 mil
 lion miles (35 million kilometers) from us.\n\nhttp://www.jpl.nasa.gov/new
 s/news.cfm?release=2011-255 \n\n\nWARNING!\nThe comets listed on Heavens-A
 bove can get very close to the sun. Never attempt to observe objects close
  to the sun without taking the proper precautions. In particular\, never p
 oint optical instruments near the sun and look through them\, or you risk 
 permanent eye damage or blindness. \n\nhttp://heavens-above.com/comet.aspx
 ?cid=C%2F2010%20X1&lat=0&lng=0&loc=unspecified&alt=0&tz=cet\n\nKD10/08/11
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
