DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20140408
DTSTAMP:20260224T194029Z
UID:acd23020-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:d0imdp7o6kg05jbt3jls1gi450@google.com\nApril 8 - Mars at Opposi
 tion. The red planet will be at its closest approach to Earth and its face
  will be fully illuminated by the Sun. This is the best time to view and p
 hotograph Mars. A medium-sized telescope will allow you to see some of the
  dark details on the planet's orange surface. You may even be able to see 
 one or both of the bright white polar ice caps.\nhttp://www.seasky.org/ast
 ronomy/astronomy-calendar-2014.html\nKD 12/22/2013
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
