BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Zoo Party for the Planet
DTSTART:20140426T150000Z
DTEND:20140426T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194030Z
UID:ad13574e-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:h7ljo7hkta2du6b6juolk5hhq8@google.com\nConservation Education D
 epartment\nWILD EARTH DAY\nat the Pittsburgh Zoo & PPG Aquarium\n\n\n\nSat
 urday at the Zoo April 26\, 2014 11AM-3PM\n\nParty for the Planet Saturday
 \, April 26\, 2014 11AM-3PM\n\nExhibitor set-up will begin at 9AM. All exh
 ibitors must be unloaded and set-up by 10:30AM. Table-covers and skirting 
 are not provided by the Zoo. Items such as balloons\, straws\, and Frisbee
 s are not permitted in the Zoo for the safety of our animals. If you plan 
 on distributing a “promotional giveaway” to Zoo visitors\, please have
  this item cleared with the Zoo ahead of time. \n\n \n \nHere are two even
 ts  at the Pittsburgh Zoo http://www.pittsburghzoo.org/ where AAAP has an 
 opportunity to share the schedules for the 2014 Star Party Season and astr
 onomy outreach.  More than one person can volunteer.\n \nIf you are new to
  the club. Understand at opportunities like this members like to do one or
  more of these:\n \n1. Share star party schedules.\n2. Offer telescope vie
 wing - Moon\, bright planets\, distant objects/buildings.\n3. Solar viewin
 g.\n4. Hands on activities like assembling "star wheels\," folding cash re
 gister tape to demonstrate distance in the solar system\, manipulating "fo
 am and sticks" to show refraction\, marble and golf tee to show "plant wob
 ble" and albedo changes used to discover new planets\, etc. Hundreds of ac
 tivity ideas are available through the Night Sky Network http://nightsky.j
 pl.nasa.gov/download-search.cfm\n5. GLOBE at Night http://www.globeatnight
 .org/\n6. Share their own astrophotographs \n7. Talk about their telescope
 \, telescopes in general\, astronomy\, etc
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
