BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mercury at Greatest Eastern Elongation
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20161211
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20161211
DTSTAMP:20260224T194031Z
UID:add38c1c-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:k8m8c0g2ou3r5m8rnriap52ja0@google.com\nDecember 11 - Mercury at
  Greatest Eastern Elongation. The planet Mercury reaches greatest eastern 
 elongation of 20.8 degrees from the Sun. This is the best time to view Mer
 cury since it will be at its highest point above the horizon in the evenin
 g sky. Look for the planet low in the western sky just after sunset.\n\nSo
 urce: <a href="http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2016.htm
 l">http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2016.html</a>
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
