BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SSP / AAAP Joint Meeting
DTSTART:20171018T213000Z
DTEND:20171018T223000Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194031Z
UID:addf9d0e-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:5hpn4bjk0ob03k0tcqn001dcva@google.com\nThe annual joint SSP (Sp
 ectroscopy Society of Pittsburgh) / AAAP meeting is on Wednesday\, October
  18th this year. As in past years\, the event is held at Duquesne Universi
 ty's Power Center Ballroom.\n\nPLEASE NOTE: Reservations for this meeting 
 are required (see link below)\n\nMore Info: <a href="http://www.ssp-pgh.or
 g/october-monthly-meeting-2017">http://www.ssp-pgh.org/october-monthly-mee
 ting-2017/</a>\n\nTECHNOLOGY FORUM – 5:30 PM\n4 H Robotic Team\n\n“4 H
  Robotic Team Demonstration”\nThe 4-H Robotics Group will describe their
  robotics program\, the FIRST (For Inspiration and Recognition of Science 
 and Technology) Competition\, show short videos of the FIRST Program\, the
 ir local robotics group program and competition\, and demonstrate the capa
 bilities of their latest robot which made it to the Semi-Final round of th
 is year’s competition.\n\nTECHNOLOGY PROGRAM – 8:15 PM\nDr. Blaise Can
 zian\n\n“From John Brashear to 21st Century Optics and Telescopes”\nTe
 lescopes have evolved both in technology and mission since the early days 
 of John Brashear’s company. Today’s telescopes are tasked with satelli
 te laser ranging\, laser satellite communication\, challenging astronomica
 l research\, and satellite imaging. Complex engineering combined with new 
 technological advancements in optic fabrication have expanded our space si
 tuational awareness and enable astronomers explore the universe like never
  before
LOCATION:Duquesne University\, 600 Forbes Ave\, Pittsburgh\, PA 15282\, USA
END:VEVENT
