BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lunar Eclipse
DTSTART:20150928T011200Z
DTEND:20150928T021200Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194031Z
UID:adfcadae-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:dt1jm80lbq30p108rvp0sph688@google.com\nThe Oct 8 event is in th
 e early morning hours and we will not be able to watch all of that eclipse
 .  Our best bet is the Sept 27/28\, 2015 Lunar Eclipse\, which reaches mid
 -eclipse at 10:48 PM EDLT on that Sunday night.  We will be listing it on 
 next year's Star Party Schedule at Wagman as\, I'm sure\, they will do for
  Mingo.  Just an early heads up to everyone.\n \nTom \n\nhttp://www.timean
 ddate.com/eclipse/lunar/2015-september-28\nEventUTC TimeTime in Pittsburgh
 *Visible in Pittsburgh\nPenumbral Eclipse beginsSep 28 at 12:13 AMSep 27 a
 t 8:13 PMYes\nPartial Eclipse beginsSep 28 at 1:12 AMSep 27 at 9:12 PMYes\
 nFull Eclipse beginsSep 28 at 2:13 AMSep 27 at 10:13 PMYes\nMaximum Eclips
 eSep 28 at 2:47 AMSep 27 at 10:47 PMYes\nFull Eclipse endsSep 28 at 3:22 A
 MSep 27 at 11:22 PMYes\nPartial Eclipse endsSep 28 at 4:23 AMSep 28 at 12:
 23 AMYes\nPenumbral Eclipse endsSep 28 at 5:22 AMSep 28 at 1:22 AMYes\n* T
 he Moon is above the horizon during this eclipse\, so with good weather co
 nditions in Pittsburgh\, the entire eclipse is visible.\n\nhttp://eclipse.
 gsfc.nasa.gov/LEplot/LEplot2001/LE2015Sep28T.pdf\n\n<a href="http://eclips
 e.gsfc.nasa.gov/LEplot/LEplot2001/LE2015Sep28T.pdf"<a/>\nKD 4/14/24
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
