BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ursids Meteor Shower
DTSTART:20161221T230000Z
DTEND:20161222T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194032Z
UID:ae87d884-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:30rrtcverr97ru5s95igarbc4s@google.com\nDecember 21\, 22 - Ursid
 s Meteor Shower. The Ursids is a minor meteor shower producing about 5-10 
 meteors per hour. It is produced by dust grains left behind by comet Tuttl
 e\, which was first discovered in 1790. The shower runs annually from Dece
 mber 17-25. It peaks this year on the the night of the 21st and morning of
  the 22nd. The second quarter moon will block many of the fainter meteors.
  But if you are patient\, you might still be able to catch a few of the br
 ighter ones. Best viewing will be just after midnight from a dark location
  far away from city lights. Meteors will radiate from the constellation Ur
 sa Minor\, but can appear anywhere in the sky.\n\nSource: <a href="http://
 www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2016.html">http://www.seasky.o
 rg/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2016.html</a>
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
