BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Full Moon / Supermoon / Blue Moon
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20180131
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20180131
DTSTAMP:20260224T194032Z
UID:aeb9d6f4-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:CSVConvert7cacd52b4154987d73ea6433f7c45d2c\nJanuary 31 - Full M
 oon / Supermoon / Blue Moon. The Moon will be located on the opposite side
  of the Earth as the Sun and its face will be will be fully illuminated. T
 his phase occurs at 13:27 UTC. Since this is the second full moon in the s
 ame month it is sometimes referred to as a blue moon. This is also the las
 t of two supermoons for 2018. The Moon will be at its closest approach to 
 the Earth and may look slightly larger and brighter than usual.\n\nSource:
  <a href="http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2018.html">ht
 tp://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2018.html</a>
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
