BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NSN Telecon
DTSTART:20120919T010000Z
DTEND:20120919T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194033Z
UID:af22a38c-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:gh37mp8jjjdsspmuo56h4qbdrs@google.com\n How It Began\, NSN Tele
 con with Chris Impey September 18th\n\nTelecon: How it Began \nwith Chris 
 Impey\n \nTuesday\, September 18th as esteemed University of Arizona profe
 ssor\, researcher\, and author Dr. Chris Impey shares his take on the begi
 nning of the Universe (and beyond). Night Sky Network club members will be
  treated to this exclusive live presentation on how the Universe began\, i
 ncluding Q&A time.\n \nDownload the PowerPoint (10 MB) here:\nhttps://nigh
 tsky.jpl.nasa.gov/docs/CosmologyImpey0912.ppt\n \nOr view the slides onlin
 e:\nhttp://www.astrosociety.org/nsntelecon\n \nThen\, on Tuesday\, Septemb
 er 18th at 9:00 pm EDT\, NSN members are invited to join the live telecon 
 by calling the toll-free line:\n \n1-888-455-9236\nCall up to 15 minutes b
 efore the telecon begins. An operator will answer and:\n- You will be aske
 d for the passcode: NIGHT SKY NETWORK\n- You will be asked to give your NA
 ME and the CLUB you belong to\, and number of people listening with you.\n
  KD 9/14/2012
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ConjunctionMoonMars
DTSTART:20140607T044500Z
DTEND:20140607T054500Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194033Z
UID:af27d096-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:4b8hv0qdfoqntqqcv6aotmn3cs@google.com\nJune 7 - Conjunction of 
 the Moon and Mars. The Moon will pass within two degrees of the the planet
  Mars in the evening sky. The gibbous moon will be at magnitude -12.2 and 
 Mars will be at magnitude -0.8. Look for both objects in the western sky j
 ust after sunset. The pair will be visible in the evening sky for about 6 
 hours after sunset.http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2014
 .html\n\nKD 12/22/2013\n\nKD 12/22/2013\n\n
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
