DESCRIPTION:CSVConverte8cae6d528e4d7212b1e95cf2f1530e4\nJuly 30 - Mercury a
 t Greatest Eastern Elongation. The planet Mercury reaches greatest eastern
  elongation of 27.2 degrees from the Sun. This is the best time to view Me
 rcury since it will be at its highest point above the horizon in the eveni
 ng sky. Look for the planet low in the western sky just after sunset.\n\nS
 ource: <a href="http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2017.ht
 ml">http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2017.html</a>
LOCATION:None
