BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Café Scientifique - Our Universe: The Past 13.8 Billion Years and 
 the Future
DTSTART:20160606T230000Z
DTEND:20160607T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194034Z
UID:af6dbffc-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:pqd0dqq8bfud2bufd065jg5bes@google.com\nAndrew Zentner\, PhD\, U
 niversity of Pittsburgh presents “Our Universe: The Past 13.8 Billion Ye
 ars and the Future”. Like the universe itself\, data about the cosmos co
 ntinues to expand. Zentner’s research aims to make predictions that are 
 unique and testable in a continuing effort to understand what's happening 
 on a galactic scale. His work ranges throughout a broad cross section of c
 osmology\, encompassing galaxy formation\, the phenomenology and identific
 ation of the dark matter and dark energy\, and astrophysical limits on fun
 damental physics. Café Scientifique is always held on the first Monday of
  the month. Food and drinks are available for purchase. Doors open at 6 pm
 . Event is free but parking is $5.\n\nMore Info: <a href="http://tickets.c
 arnegiemuseums.org/csc/CSCSE_CSCCAFESCI_SCS66">http://tickets.carnegiemuse
 ums.org/csc/CSCSE_CSCCAFESCI_SCS66</a>\n\nMore Info: <a href="http://wp.3a
 p.org/calendar/our-pittsburgh-constellation-calendar">Our Pittsburgh Const
 ellation Calendar</a>
LOCATION:Carnegie Science Center
END:VEVENT
