DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20170525
DTSTAMP:20260224T194034Z
UID:af83d65c-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:CSVConvertb15c2f5422ebd6ba6293f301463cd6ba\nMay 25 - New Moon. 
 The Moon will located on the same side of the Earth as the Sun and will no
 t be visible in the night sky. This phase occurs at 19:45 UTC. This is the
  best time of the month to observe faint objects such as galaxies and star
  clusters because there is no moonlight to interfere.\n\nSource: <a href="
 http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2017.html">http://www.s
 easky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2017.html</a>
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
