BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Annular Solar Eclipse
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20170226
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20170226
DTSTAMP:20260224T194035Z
UID:b070f464-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:CSVConvert1a0dd3326c1b61c562d4f32981de6e1e\nFebruary 26 - Annul
 ar Solar Eclipse. An annular solar eclipse occurs when the Moon is too far
  away from the Earth to completely cover the Sun. This results in a ring o
 f light around the darkened Moon. The Sun's corona is not visible during a
 n annular eclipse. The path of the eclipse will begin off the coast of Chi
 le and pass through southern Chile and southern Argentina across the south
 ern Atlantic Ocean and into Angola and Congo in Africa. A partial eclipse 
 will be visible throughout parts of southern South America and southwester
 n Africa.\n\nSource: <a href="http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-ca
 lendar-2017.html">http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy-calendar-2017.
 html</a>
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
