BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:June Solstice
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20170621
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20170621
DTSTAMP:20260224T194035Z
UID:b09b353a-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:CSVConvertda175b337d2f33865df2ba413127360b\nJune 21 - June Sols
 tice. The June solstice occurs at 04:24 UTC. The North Pole of the earth w
 ill be tilted toward the Sun which will have reached its northernmost posi
 tion in the sky and will be directly over the Tropic of Cancer at 23.44 de
 grees north latitude. This is the first day of summer (summer solstice) in
  the Northern Hemisphere and the first day of winter (winter solstice) in 
 the Southern Hemisphere.\n\nSource: <a href="http://www.seasky.org/astrono
 my/astronomy-calendar-2017.html">http://www.seasky.org/astronomy/astronomy
 -calendar-2017.html</a>
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Astroblast
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20110923
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20110923
DTSTAMP:20260224T194035Z
UID:b09defe6-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:aqh8k5ve4q4mg07mbc9b6698js@google.com\n\nThe annual AstroBlast 
 star party is scheduled for the weekend of Friday\, Sep. 24 through Sunday
 \, Sep.\, 25\, so mark your calendars!  Due to the new moon on Sep. 27\, t
 he "bonus" days for observers will be Monday\, Sep. 26 through Thursday\, 
 Sep. 29.  There are no formal events planned for these extra days (those w
 ill be on Friday and Saturday)\, but those attending Astroblast are welcom
 e to stay for additional observing opportunities. \n\nhttp://www.oras.org/
 astrblst.htm\n\n\nFor more information e-mail me\, or see our website:  ww
 w.oras.org and click the AstroBlast link.  The web site has not been updat
 ed for 2011 yet\, but please check in for updates as the time of the event
  nears. \n\nHope to see you! \nJohn O.\nOil Region Astronomical Society\, 
 Inc. \n\n\n__._\,_.___
LOCATION:http://www.oras.org/astrblst.htm
END:VEVENT
