BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Total Lunar Eclipse
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20101221
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20101221
DTSTAMP:20260224T194036Z
UID:b129c156-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:uqohf88qc8imlr3hr1krapkb5k@google.com\nDecember 21 - Total Luna
 r Eclipse. The eclipse will be visible throughout most of eastern Asia\, A
 ustralia\, the Pacific Ocean\, the Americas\, and Europe. (NASA Eclipse In
 formation  http://eclipse.gsfc.nasa.gov/LEplot/LEplot2001/LE2010Dec21T.GIF
  )\n \n December 21 - The Winter Solstice occurs in the northern hemispher
 e at 23:38 UT. The Sun is at its lowest point in the sky and it will be th
 e shortest day of the year. This is also the first day of winter. \nTotal 
 Lunar Eclipse Dec. 21\n\nhttp://eclipse.gsfc.nasa.gov/LEplot/LEplot2001/LE
 2010Dec21T.pdf\n\nContacts \nP1 05:27:43 UTC \nU1 06:32:17 UTC \nU2 07:40:
 21 UTC \nGreatest 08:16:56 UTC \nU3 08:53:34 UTC \nU4 10:01:39 UTC \nP4 11
 :06:04 UTC \n\n*EST is 5 hours behind of Coordinated Universal Time (UTC)\
 n
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
