BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AO Lecture 7P
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20090118
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20090118
DTSTAMP:20260224T194037Z
UID:b19f2cf2-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:brpa2u693ud3ovfdjha54cqghc@google.com\nSchedule\n2008 Allegheny
  Observatory Public Lecture Series\nRefreshments: 7:00pm\, Lecture: 7:30pm
 \, Observatory Tour: 9:00pm\n• 18 January\nProf. Leonard Kisslinger\, CM
 U (Department of Physics)\n“Early Universe Phase Transitions”\n• 15 
 February\nDr. Janos Zsargo\, Pitt (Department of Physics and Astronomy)\n
 “Massive Stars as Engines of Galactic Evolution”\n• 21 March\nRose S
 ullivan\, Lou Coban and Kevin Kepes\, Pitt (Department of Physics and Astr
 onomy)\n“At Twilight Time: Astronomy From the Observers Point of View”
 \n• 18 April\nDr. Michael Ramsey\, Pitt (Department of Geology & Planeta
 ry Science)\n“Thermal Infrared Observations of the Geology of Earth and 
 Mars: Past Results and Future\nDirections of NASA’s Mars\, Moon and Eart
 h Programs”\n• 16 May\nDr. Jeffrey Newman\, Pitt (Department of Physic
 s and Astronomy)\n“New Views of the Distant Universe”\n• 20 June\nDi
 ane Turnshek\, St. Vincent (Physics)\n“Life in the Universe”\n• 18 J
 uly\nProf. George Gatewood\, Pitt (Department of Physics and Astronomy)\n
 “Asteroids\, What Can We Do With Them and About Them”\n• 15 August\n
 Dr. Andrew Zentner\, Pitt (Department of Physics and Astronomy)\n“How Da
 rk Matter Telescopes Reveal the Nature of Dark Energy in The Universe”\n
 • 19 September\nProf. Regina Schulte-Ladbeck\, Pitt (Department of Physi
 cs and Astronomy)\n“Scientific Leadership”\n• 17 October\nProf. John
  Hillier\, Pitt (Department of Physics and Astronomy)\n“Supernovae: Dyin
 g Stars but Cosmic Seeds”\n• 21 November\nProf. Steven Dytman\, Pitt (
 Department of Physics and Astronomy)\n“New Experiments in Neutrino Resea
 rch -- Fundamental Parameters and Supernova\nImplications”
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
