BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:CANCELLEDTom'sClass
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20111018
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20111018
DTSTAMP:20260224T194039Z
UID:b2842e60-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:fsdi2evr3o48hihf5aueth1kg8@google.com\n\nI just checked all of 
 weather sources and there's no doubt about tonight\, it's going to be clou
 dy. I'm canceling tonight's starhopping class.  I'll wait until Thursday a
 fternoon to decide on the private star party.\nBy the way Bill\, I do use 
 the page you mentioned and it showed fewer clouds when I checked it along 
 with my other pages yesterday afternoon.  It has way too many pop-up windo
 ws and it's detail isn't as good as two other pages I use.  I prefer these
  two because of the variety of detail they offer\, motion options and they
 're easier to us.\nhttp://weather.unisys.com/satellite/sat_vis.php?image=i
 r&inv=0&t=cur&region=us\nhttp://weather.unisys.com/satellite/sat_vis.php?i
 mage=ir&inv=0&t=cur&region=ne\n \nTom\n\nKD/18/2011\n\n\nI am planning sev
 eral nights for some sessions for members to come up to Wagman to learn so
 me of my observing methods and informal training on the Manka scope. These
  dates will depend on the weather and attendance.\nI will conduct Starhopp
 ing Classes in September and October\, also weather permitting. Here are t
 he dates for the observing sessions and training:\n \nAug 18 and 19 (Thurs
 day and Friday)\n \nStarhopping Classes\n \nSept 19 and 20\nOct 17 and 18\
 nMondays and Tuesdays\nEmail me at this address if you plan to come to any
  of these programs.\n \nTom Reiland
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mingo Pub. Star Party(dusk)
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20120810
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20120810
DTSTAMP:20260224T194039Z
UID:b2899bd4-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:gsvihthdcmmkn9utr651n8fags@google.com\n\n\nhttps://nightsky.jpl
 .nasa.gov/event-view.cfm?Event_ID=31472\n \n2012 Star Party Schedule Mingo
  Creek Park Observatory April 27\, 28 May 25\, 26 June 22\, 23 July 6\, 7\
 , 20\, 21 August 10\, 11 September 8\, 22 October 6\, 20 Nicholas E. Wagma
 n Observatory February 25\, Winterfest March 31 April 27\, 28 May 25\, 26 
 June 22\, 23 July 27\, 28 August 24\, 25 September 8\, 22 October 6\, 20\n
 \n</p>The   a=href "https://nightsky.jpl.nasa.gov/event-view.cfm?Event_ID=
 31472">August 10 Mingo Public Star Party</a></p>\n  has a special guest\, 
 Dan Handley who will be presenting his new movie:Undaunted:  the Forgotten
  Giants of Allegheny Observatory. http://undauntedthemovie.com/.\n\nShowin
 gs at 8 and 10 PM. \n\n \nUndaunted is cinemagraphic and has a wonderful s
 ound score and tells about the giants(John Brashear(spectroscope\, L3 Bras
 hear built the PMA of the Kepler space telescope)\, Samuel Langley(aviatio
 n\, time zones)\, Keeler (discovered Saturn's rings and their structure)\,
  Michelson–Morley experiment\, etc. of Allegheny Observatory's http://ww
 w.pitt.edu/~aobsvtry/ early history and pioneers and the importance of the
 ir work to astronomy.\n\nHere is the One Minute Trailer http://undauntedth
 emovie.com/.  \nDate: Friday\, 8/10/2012  \nLocation: Mingo Creek Park Obs
 ervatory\, Mansion Hill Road Extension\, Finleyville\, PA 15332\, Monongah
 ela\, PA 15063 (Get Directions)  \n\nNicholas E. Wagman Observatory Februa
 ry 25\, Winterfest March 31\nApril 27\,28 May 25\,26 June 22\,23 July 27\,
 28 August 24\,25 September 8\, 22 October 6\,20
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Off-Site Penguin Court Preserve
DTSTART:20260808T003000Z
DTEND:20260808T013000Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194039Z
UID:b292094a-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:2cqp3fvliqsjju76mmam64ri4p@google.com\nCome enjoy the night sky
  with members of the Amateur Astronomers Association of Pittsburgh.  We&#
 39\;ll start the evening with a short\, astronomy themed presentation\, an
 d then attendees will be invited to look through member&#39\;s telescopes 
 and observe star clusters\, nebulae and even galaxies.\n\nThe topic of the
  presentation will be binocular astronomy.  We&#39\;ll discuss binocular 
 basics\, their use and what you can see.  Once it gets dark\, we&#39\;ll 
 have a station set up with astronomers using a laser pointer to pinpoint s
 pecific targets for you to observe through you&#39\;re own binoculars.\n\n
 Do you have a telescope\, but aren&#39\;t sure how to use it?  Bring it a
 long and one of our members will answer questions and help you get it set 
 up.\n\nSpace is limited\, contact Penquin Court Preserve for details.
LOCATION:Penguin Court Preserve\, 314 Penguin Ct\, Ligonier Township\, PA 1
 5655\, USA
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mingo Star Party
DTSTART:20240906T220000Z
DTEND:20240906T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194039Z
UID:b2974e78-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:3m3e1l0j9m0g5aua5sve6g0cb2@google.com\nCome join the Amateur As
 tronomers Association of Pittsburgh for solar viewing through the observat
 ory&#39\;s 10&quot\; refractor telescope\, followed by a night of looking 
 at the stars through the 10&quot\; or the observatory&#39\;s 24&quot\; Rit
 chey-Chrétien telescope.  Visitors of all ages are welcome to tour the o
 bservatory\, watch a planetarium show\, or listen to presentations on a va
 riety of astronomy related topics.  There are also activities for childre
 n and many of our members set up their own personal scopes for additional 
 viewing opportunities.
LOCATION:Mingo Creek Park Observatory\, 1 Shelter 10 Road\, Finleyville\, P
 A 15332\, USA
END:VEVENT
