BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Members only - Scopes n stuff
DTSTART:20240217T190000Z
DTEND:20240217T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194040Z
UID:b35498ca-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:73die3vmtfuibe2iv146325cjd@google.com\nThe first educational se
 ssion on Astronomy Basics\, equipment and setup will be Saturday February 
 17th\, 2pm at the Mingo Observatory.\n\nI will have several different moun
 t and scope options there\, along with some different eyepieces\, finders\
 , a couple cameras (This is not an astrophotography seminar!) and other mi
 scellaneous equipment.\n\nWe will discuss the different options and some o
 f the pros and cons of each\, and some things you should avoid.  \n\nIf y
 ou have a scope that you need help with\, bring it along.  This is an opp
 ortunity to get 1-1 training on your equipment.  \n\nThe majority of the 
 class will be indoors\, but the building can be chilly\, so dress for the 
 temperature outside.  We will be outside to align finder scopes\, and loo
 k through some eyepieces.\n\nIf Mother Nature favors us\, we might even ge
 t a chance to do some observing.\n\nPlease let me know if you are planning
  on attending.  If you are bringing your equipment\, please let me know w
 hat you're bringing and what you need help with.  I want to make sure eve
 ryone leaves with answers.
LOCATION:Mingo Creek Park Observatory\, 1 Shelter 10 Road\, Finleyville\, P
 A 15332\, USA
END:VEVENT
