BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AAAP Meeting
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20151009T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20151009T203000
DTSTAMP:20260224T194041Z
UID:b3af4a9a-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:1odqot68st9njc0v697vuin0u8@google.com\nhttps://wp.3ap.org/2015/
 10/october-9-2015-730-pm-amateur-astronomers-association-of-pittsburgh-gen
 eral-meeting-at-carnegie-science-center/\n\n\n\nAmateur Astronomers Associ
 ation Monthly Meetings will meet 7:30 PM\, Friday\, October 9\, 2015 at th
 e Science Stage\, Carnegie Science Center\, One Allegheny Ave.Pittsburgh\,
  PA 15212  promptly at 7:30 pm. The parking fee is $5 at the inside lobby 
 kiosk. It is recommended to enter and exit through the same gate.\n\n~~~~~
 ~~~~~~~~~~\nFrom the Guide Star:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nBill Roemer Dives Into 
 Black Holes at AAAP October 9 Club Meeting\nBlack holes are perhaps the mo
 st counterintuitive objects in the Universe: A dimensionless but unbelieva
 bly massive point in space where not even a beam of light can escape\, whe
 re the laws of physics and flow of time breaks down\, were you would be 
 “Spaghettified” if you fell in\, etc.\nWhat better person to make Back
  Holes more comprehensible than our own Bill Roemer\, former Director of M
 ingo Observatory and a frequent AAAP and public lecturer in astronomy. His
  talk\, “Shedding Light On Black Holes”\, takes place October 9\, 2015
 \, 7:30 pm at the Carnegie Science Center on Pittsburgh’s North Shore. B
 ill loves audience interaction with his lectures\, so don’t hesitate to 
 ask if a trip through a Black Hole could send you to a far corner of our U
 niverse\, or to a different universe\, assuming you don’t get spaghettif
 ied in the process.\n \nNote 1: If you haven’t been to the CSC in a long
  while\, remember there is no longer a parking attendant at the entrance b
 ooth. You just grab a ticket out of the machine\, pay inside at one of the
  ticket kiosks in the main lobby (near the gift shop)\, then use the valid
 ated ticket on your way out to raise the exit gate.\n• Note 2: “Scope 
 Give-Away” reminder by John Holtz: “Remember that you can enter the Te
 lescope Give-Away just by attending the October 9 meeting. (See the Septem
 ber Guide Star for the initial announcement.) In addition to the 60 mm Uni
 tron refractor\, the winner (chosen at the December meeting) will get thre
 e carrying cases for the scope and eyepieces\, more than a dozen eyepieces
 \, 15 color and deep-sky filters\, and more! If you want the complete deta
 iled list\, contact John Holtz at President@3ap.org
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
