BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:GaN
DTSTART:20120213T000000Z
DTEND:20120213T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194041Z
UID:b42974aa-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:9p029gfu0mj5rgvo6rru4jbrk0@google.com\nMore stars. Less light. 
 Participate in GLOBE at Night!\n\nCalling all Earthlings! Take a few minut
 es to get involved in the GLOBE at Night campaign to preserve dark skies! 
 GLOBE at Night is a citizen-science campaign open to people all over the w
 orld to raise awareness of the impact of light pollution by inviting citiz
 en-scientists to measure their night sky brightness and report their obser
 vations to a website from a computer or smart phone. Light pollution threa
 tens not only our “right to starlight”\, but can affect energy consump
 tion\, wildlife and health. Through 2011\, people in 115 countries contrib
 uted 66\,000 measurements\, making GLOBE at Night one of the most successf
 ul light pollution awareness campaigns to date. Please join us to particip
 ate in the 2012 campaign an hour after sunset til about 10pm January 14 th
 rough 23\, February 12 through 21\, March 13 through 22\, and April 11 thr
 ough 20. For information and resources\, visit us at www.globeatnight.org.
 \n\n
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Leonids
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20091117
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20091117
DTSTAMP:20260224T194041Z
UID:b42d4dbe-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:6egivagr47uk968lq3tpi9bk9k@google.com\nLeonid Meteor Sower will
  peak this year around Nov. 17-18.  Radian near the "Sickle\," does not ri
 se until after Midnight.  Moon Phase is favorable and as well this year Ea
 rth passes through some old trails\, early evening 17th\, befoe dawn 18th.
  Best viewing S. Asia\, but possibility of a exceptional show here\, makes
  looking for it something to plan for.  KD 11/10/09
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ESO Planets 4PM-
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20111015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20111015
DTSTAMP:20260224T194042Z
UID:b432df54-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:o9f96lpo3mrgcmm8qfr3ed3epg@google.com\nEdgewood Symphony Orches
 tra when they perform Gustav Holst's "The Planets" on Saturday\, October 1
 5\, 2011\, at the Jewish Community Center in Squirrel Hill.  I know that t
 he AAAP is having public star parties at both the Wagman and Mingo Observa
 tories that evening\, but I am hoping that a few people will be willing to
  help out at the ESO event.\n \nWe can set up our displays between 4:00 PM
  and 6:00 PM that Saturday afternoon and the performance will be held late
 r that same evening.  I hope to have one or two tables of displays along w
 ith a few telescopes as floor displays.  They have specifically asked that
  we show the slide presentation that Eric Fischer prepared for the BCSO ev
 ent last April.  \n \nIf you are willing to help\, please call or send me 
 an e-mail message.\n\nJohn M.
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
