BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mt.LebStarParty
DTSTART:20120922T000000Z
DTEND:20120922T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194044Z
UID:b5722154-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:i4tkn05enf5uecbatrhunp1d7s@google.com\nMt. Lebanon Star Party a
 t the Mt. Lebanon Golf Course\n\nhttp://www.mtlebanon.org/index.aspx?NID=2
 129\n\n \n\nAt the invitation of the Mt Lebanon Recreation Dept\, we are h
 aving a star party at the golf course at 8 pm.  The course promises to be 
 a reasonably dark site at a good elevation.  The one glaring light near th
 e clubhouse will be turned off for this event\, and it is a fair distance 
 from the best observing sites in any case.  Several members have volunteer
 ed to share their scopes\, but more are always welcome.  The Rec Dept has 
 gotten quite a few inquiries\, so we expect a good turnout.  If it is clou
 dy that night\, we will do it on Sunday\, Sept 23 instead.  A map of the b
 est areas of the course for setting up our telescopes is shown in the foll
 owing map: http://goo.gl/maps/XkpTt.  A golf cart will be available for mo
 ving equipment from the parking lot up to Stargazing sites A and B.   \n\n
 As per Chris M.\n\nKD 9/14/2012 
LOCATION:Mt. Lebanon Golf Course\, Mt. Lebanon\, PA
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Geminids
DTSTART:20121214T020000Z
DTEND:20121214T030000Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194044Z
UID:b5751bde-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:jvqa33bqpe1qj8jd3iaja50g6s@google.com\nWith no moon to ruin the
  show\, 2012 presents a most favorable year for watching the grand finale 
 of the meteor showers. Best viewing of the Geminids will probably be from 
 about 1 a.m. to 3 a.m. on December 14.\n\nGeminids (space.com)\n\n Comet o
 f Origin: 3200 Phaethon\n Radiant: constellation Gemini\n Active: Dec. 4-1
 7\, 2012\n Peak Activity: Dec. 13-14\, 2012\n Peak Activity Meteor Count: 
 Approximately 120 meteors per hour\n Meteor Velocity: 22 miles (35 kilomet
 ers) per second\n\n Notes: The Geminids are typically one of the best\, an
 d most reliable\, of the annual meteor showers. This year's peak falls per
 fectly with a new moon\, guaranteeing a dark sky for the show in the night
 s on either side of the peak date. This shower is considered one of the be
 st opportunities for younger viewers because the show gets going around 9 
 or 10 p.m.\n\nKD 7/24/2012
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
