BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TOTAL LUNAR ECLIPSE 1:30AM
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20101221
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20101221
DTSTAMP:20260224T194044Z
UID:b5a935c2-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:j8r9eh3jn6ios8ci6c6os0cg1c@google.com\nTOTAL LUNAR ECLIPSE 1:30
 AM EST is a good time to start watching.\n\n<p>Both Mingo and Wagman Obser
 vatories plan to operate on the night of the eclipse if viewing conditions
  are favorable.  It has been suggested Mingo would open at 9PM.</p>\n\n<p>
 <a href="http://eclipse.gsfc.nasa.gov/OH/OHfigures/OH2010-Fig04.pdf">NASA 
 Eclipse Map</a></p>\n\n\n<p><a href="www.mreclipse.com/LEdata/TLE2010Dec21
 /TLE2010Dec21.html\n">Mr. Eclipse Map</a></p>\n<p><a href="http://nightsky
 .jpl.nasa.gov/event-view.cfm?Event_ID=14957\n">NSN Eclipse Post</a></p>\n\
 nDecember 21 - Total Lunar Eclipse. The eclipse will be visible throughout
  most of eastern Asia\, Australia\, the Pacific Ocean\, the Americas\, and
  Europe. (NASA Eclipse Information  http://eclipse.gsfc.nasa.gov/LEplot/LE
 plot2001/LE2010Dec21T.GIF )\n \n December 21 - The Winter Solstice occurs 
 in the northern hemisphere at 23:38 UT. The Sun is at its lowest point in 
 the sky and it will be the shortest day of the year. This is also the firs
 t day of winter. \nTotal Lunar Eclipse Dec. 21\n\nhttp://eclipse.gsfc.nasa
 .gov/LEplot/LEplot2001/LE2010Dec21T.pdf\n\nContacts \nP1 05:27:43 UTC \nU1
  06:32:17 UTC \nU2 07:40:21 UTC \nGreatest 08:16:56 UTC \nU3 08:53:34 UTC 
 \nU4 10:01:39 UTC \nP4 11:06:04 UTC \n\n*EST is 5 hours behind of Coordina
 ted Universal Time (UTC)\n
LOCATION:TOTAL LUNAR ECLIPSE
END:VEVENT
