BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:North AlleghenySP7:30P            
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20090401
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20090401
DTSTAMP:20260224T194045Z
UID:b6624be8-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:huomc6v8m0h44bc2smnhe1kfi8@google.com\nNorth Allegheny Star Par
 ty             \n\n“Telescope Convention/Star Party”\n\n(Underwritten 
 by the N.A. Foundation)\n\nWhen:   Wednesday\, April 1\, 2009 from (Sunset
 ) 7:30 P.M.-????\n\nRain date: Saturday\, April 4 at (www.3ap.org) Wagman
 ’s Observatory in Deer Lakes Park\n\nWhere:  Field behind McKnight Eleme
 ntary and N.A.I. (500 Cumberland Rd. Pittsburgh\, pa 15237)\n\nWho:    Den
 nis Morton and the Amateur Astronomers Association of Pittsburgh invite al
 l North Allegheny students and their families to share the night sky.\n\nW
 hy:    Schmidt-Cassegrain Meade Telescope LXD75 SC-8 has been purchased fo
 r the students at North Allegheny through a grant from the N.A. Foundation
 .\n\nWhat to Yourself\, eyes to view distant and faint objects\,\n\nBring:
   your curiosity\, telescope big or small\, binoculars for lunar observing
 \, flashlight\, warm clothes and hot cocoa. \n\nDuring the North Allegheny
  Telescope Convention we will be observing these and other celestial objec
 ts: Moon\, Saturn\, Spring Constellations and will have discussions on lig
 ht pollution.     \n\n        Follow the luminaries from the parking lot b
 etween McKnight Elementary and N.A.I. to our location in the field behind 
 McKnight. This is a central location in the school district that most stud
 ents/parents will be able to find.  You do not need a telescope to attend\
 , but students are welcome to bring their own to share with others.  Amate
 ur Astronomers from the A.A.A.P will be available to share their knowledge
  and hobby with students. \n\nIf it is a cloudy evening this event will be
  rescheduled for the rain date. Check the web site below for more informat
 ion. http://teachers.northallegheny.org/dmorton/exploring_with_a_telescope
 .htm\n\nSpecial thanks to:\n\n·       The N.A. Foundation for supporting 
 the purchase of this wonderful instrument \n·       Parent organizations 
 at all schools \n·       The N.A. teachers and staff \n·       Mr. Steve
  Parks for the use of the school grounds \n·       AAAP Members\n\n\n\nDe
 nnis R. Morton\n\nNorth Allegheny School District\n\nString Specialist\n\n
 McKnight Elementary\n\n500 Cumberland Rd.\n\nPittsburgh\, PA 15237\n\n(412
 ) 369-5509\n\n dmorton@northallegheny.org\n\nAs per\, Dennis Morton.  KD
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
