BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:WISE Telecon9P
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20110922
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20110922
DTSTAMP:20260224T194045Z
UID:b66d0718-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:qd9hdl2c0mma1at26s91mjf5js@google.com\nUpcoming Telecon Dates\n
 Talk live and interact with NASA scientists. Mark these dates on your cale
 ndar and announce them in your club newsletter to keep on the cutting edge
  of scientific discoveries and NASA Missions:\n- Thursday\, July 28th: In 
 celebration of the release of the Life in the Universe ToolKit\,  Dr. Davi
 d Morrison will speak on Astrobiology\n- Thursday\, September 22nd: Explor
 ing the Dark Side of the Solar System with WISE featuring Dr. Ned Wright \
 n- Thursday\, November 17th: Citizen Science and the LADEE Mission with Br
 ian Day of NASA Ames Research Center\nTelecons for your calendar    \nIn c
 elebration with the release of our latest ToolKit\, Life in the Universe:\
 nAre We Alone?\, the NSN is pleased to engage you with Dr. David Morrison\
 , presenting his passion for astrobiology. Dr. Morrison is the senior scie
 ntist at the NASA Astrobiology Institute\, NASA Ames Research Center at Mo
 ffett Field in California:  http://nightsky.jpl.nasa.gov/club/news-display
 .cfm?News_ID=430\n\nTo log into the Telecon on Thursday\, July 28th betwee
 n 5:45 - 6:00pm (Pacific Time):\nUse the toll-free conference call line: 1
 -888-455-9236\nAn operator will answer and:\n            • You will be a
 sked for the passcode: NIGHT SKY NETWORK\n            • You will be aske
 d to give your NAME and the CLUB you belong to\, and number of people list
 ening with you.\n\nFind the PowerPoint and other download links here soon:
   http://nightsky.jpl.nasa.gov/download-view.cfm?Doc_ID=476\n\nNext upcomi
 ng telecons are:\nThursday\, August 18th: Brooke Hsu\, for bonus telecon o
 n International Observe the Moon Night (InOMN)\nThursday\, September 22nd:
  Exploring the Dark Side of the Solar System with WISE featuring Dr. Ned W
 right Thursday\, November 17th: Citizen Science and the LADEE Mission with
  Brian Day
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
