BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Comet Viewing\, Wagman
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20130308
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20130308
DTSTAMP:20260224T194045Z
UID:b69199f2-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:dckfnoj3m3i72aekfmtm8vnlto@google.com\nComet PANSTARRS   No Com
 et Parties. However\, we will have members operating the scopes at Wagman 
 Obs every clear night from March 8 thru April 7 along with members setting
  up their own scopes on the field. PSAs to the local media on comet will b
 e forthcoming.The comet will set approximately an hour to 75 minutes after
  sunset during this 30 night time frame. Staffing:1. Min. 2 members/ obser
 vatory scope. to operate 2. as many members as possible with their telesco
 pes or binoculars set up on the field. 3. 2-3 membersin Smith Hosp.Rm. 4. 
 Car parkers needed for weekends. Members should arrive well before sunset.
  Variables: 1. Comet magnitude (If 3rd magnitude or fainter\, public inter
 est wil be diminished.) 2. Weather will limit the frequency of our need to
  be at Wagman Observatory. We depend on your gracious assistance to make o
 ur effort to show this interloper to the public. Thank you in advance.Tom 
 Reiland\, Director  Nicholas E Wagman Observatory\n\nKD 1/28/2013
LOCATION:Wagman Obervatory\, Deer Lakes Park\, Tarentum\, PA
END:VEVENT
