BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Butler County Symphony Orchestra 7:30PM
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20110416
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20110416
DTSTAMP:20260224T194049Z
UID:b8996086-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:dart6k21p4vg6p7tfpdlr30u50@google.com\n Butler County Symphony 
 Orchestra\, http://butlersymphony.org/    April 16\, 2011 performance\, wh
 ich will have the theme of "Space."  In addition to Gustav Holts's "The Pl
 anets"\, the BCSO program will include Debussy's "Clair de Lune" and James
  Horner's "Music from Apollo 13."  The performance will be given in the au
 ditorium of the Butler Intermediate High School at 7:30 PM on Saturday\, A
 pril 16. http://nightsky.jpl.nasa.gov/event-view.cfm?Event_ID=25458 It wil
 l be a wonderful evening of music that is right down our alley.\n\nThe BCS
 O committee is inviting the AAAP to set up a few telescopes\, as well as t
 wo or three tables of exhibits\, in the foyer outside the auditorium so th
 at the folks attending the performance can learn a little bit about astron
 omy.  This is similar to what we did for the Pittsburgh Symphony Orchestra
  last year.  In addition\, we will be putting together a slide show of the
  planets to be shown in the auditorium during the last movement of "The Pl
 anets."  \n\nAAAP Volunteers please arrange you participation through John
  M. Tickets are required for this event and a limited number of tickets wi
 ll be provided to AAAP volunteers. See John M.
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
