BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Keystone Trails SP  7PM
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20110930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20110930
DTSTAMP:20260224T194049Z
UID:b8d07d28-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:6qhiigapu559ed2mu5i28vu6f0@google.com\nUpdate:\n Astronmy Progr
 am and Star Gazing at KTA Fall Weekend\, Joyce A. of KTA coordinating with
  George G. from AAAP\nSubject: Astronmy Program and Star Gazing at KTA Fal
 l Weekend\n\n\nWell the weekend will be here before you know it. Just a re
 minder that we are looking forward to you coming Friday\, Sept. 30 at Camp
  Lutherlyn for Astronomy Program and Star Gazing Party.\n George\, I am br
 inging projector\, white sheet and screen. When you get to Lutherlyn's off
 ice\, you will have passed the Shoalis Cabin area. Those cabins will not b
 e used this weekend. It has a picnic pavillion with electric that you you 
 can use for the program. It has a large field next to it that will be dark
  since no cabins will be used there. I think this will be perfect spot for
  Star Gazing Party.\n \nCome early around 6 PM and join our weiner roast p
 icnic at the picnic pavillion. Then around 7:00 PM you could start Astrono
 my program right there. Then around 8:00 PM or dark\, you can start the St
 ar Gazing Party.\n\nKD 9/27/11\n \njoyce\nI received a request for a star 
 party Sept 30 from Joyce Appel .\nDoes anyone want to participate in this 
 Star Party?    It will be a short one from 7: 00 to 8:30 PM . They are hav
 ing a wiener roast that we can take part in. If so please get back to me A
 SAP.\nBill M.\n\n\n\nBill\,\n\n\nI am in charge of organizing a Fall Keyst
 one Trails Association Weekend in the Fall. It will be a Camp Lutherlyn\, 
 near Moraine State Park. Butler Outdoor Club and North Country Trail Assoc
 . is hosting it. Any chance we could have an Astronomy Program and Star Ga
 zing Party Friday night\, Sept. 30 from 7- 8:30 PM? We enjoyed what your c
 lub did at the Outdoor Extravaganza. We are having a Wiener Roast Picnic 6
 - ? and Bonfire later with music. Your club could do this off in a field n
 ot far from there\, but I know it is not good to be near a fire and light.
 \nI don't think we would have electricity unless I can ask if there is any
  near where we will be.\njoyce
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
