BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jazz
DTSTART:20120804T160000Z
DTEND:20120804T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194051Z
UID:b9c57ce2-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:bgq82om24afesfcdqggp8c7k3o@google.com\nWashington County Wine\,
  Jazz and Pops Festival Returns August 4-5\, 2012.\n\n\nThe Washington Win
 e Jazz and Pops festival is a joint fundraiser for the Washington Symphony
  Orchestra and the Mental Health Association.\n\n\n\nBigger and Better tha
 n Ever in 2012! \n\nWashington County Wine\, Jazz and Pops Festival\nAugus
 t 4-5\, 2012\n\n\n"A great success!" . . "Something new and different for 
 Washington County--fantastic wine\, food and sound" . . . "Can we have the
  same location next year?" . . . "This is impressive--the first wine festi
 val I have been to with a full orchestra!" \n\nThese are only a few of the
  wonderful comments and compliments the organizers of the First Annual Was
 hington Wine Jazz and Pops Festival received. The festival provided delici
 ous food\, a variety of wines to suit all palates\, handmade jewelry and e
 xciting entertainment. \n\nWe're sure that you'll find this year's Wine Ja
 zz and Pops Festival\, held the first weekend in August at Mingo Creek Cou
 nty Park in Washington County\, PA\, even more entertaining and enjoyable 
 than last year's event! Once again\, we're bringing you the finest in Jazz
  and Pops music\, together with wonderful wine samplings from regional win
 eries\, and delicious food selections from premier area restaurants. This 
 year\, we've also expanded our offerings from local craft merchants who wi
 ll be offering high-quality items for sale throughout the festival.\n\nThe
  Washington Wine Jazz and Pops festival is a joint fundraiser for the Wash
 ington Symphony Orchestra and the Mental Health Association.\n\nPlease bro
 wse our website to learn more about this year's festival. We've also poste
 d some photos of last year's event here.\n\nTHE FESTIVAL WILL BE HELD RAIN
  OR SHINE!\nContact us: winejazzpops@washsym.org\n\n\n\n\n\nWashington Win
 e\, Jazz & Pops Festival\nSaturday\, Aug 4 12:00p to 7:00p\natMingo Creek 
 Park - Washington County\,Finleyville\,PA\nThe Washington Wine\, Jazz & Po
 ps Festival features a day of jazz and wine-tasting\, and a day of pops an
 d wine-tastings. Plus great food vendors and fun for all. Great music\, go
 od wine\, and a variety of foods to make a unique summer festival in Washi
 ngton County - Mingo Creek Park!\n\nPrice: $20 per person in advance or $2
 5 per person at the gate\nPhone: (724) 225-2061\nAge Suitability:None Spec
 ified\nTags:music\, jazz\, festival\, wine-tasting\, pops\nThe Washington 
 Wine\, Jazz & Pops Festival features a day of jazz and wine-tasting\, and 
 a day of pops and wine-tastings. Plus great food vendors and fun for all. 
 Great music\, good wine\, and a variety of foods to make a unique summer f
 estival in Washington County - Mingo Creek Park!\n\nEvent Website\nCategor
 ies:Music\, Wine\nCreator: Washington Symphony Orchestra\nCreator: Washing
 ton Symphony Orchestra
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Telecon: Kepler's Latest\, July 29th  
DTSTART:20130730T010000Z
DTEND:20130730T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194051Z
UID:b9cada7a-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:juq3ub4glkci951bn16t873gj0@google.com\nTelecon: Kepler's Latest
 \, July 29th  \n    We at the Night Sky Network are excited to present a t
 elecon with Dr. Nick Gautier\, Kepler staff scientist\, at the end of this
  month. He will discuss the latest information on the Kepler mission\, inc
 luding new data returns and updates on the status of the satellite\, which
  should be quite exciting to say the least. The fun begins Monday\, July 2
 9th at 9:00 PM ET/6:00 pm PT. More information on the slides and call in i
 nformation will be available shortly at the following location:\nhttps://n
 ightsky.jpl.nas a.gov/download-view.cfm?Doc_ID=524\n\n
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
