BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Account of Truman Kohman&#39\;s Life and Love of Astronomy\, 191
 6-2010 by Diane Turnshek
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20111015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20111015
DTSTAMP:20260224T194052Z
UID:ba2ae30c-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:vdt9arts3jnigsq0i58svo6ta8@google.com\n\n\nhttp://365daysofastr
 onomy.org/calendar/\n\nSee the podcast scheduled for October 15 - An Accou
 nt of Truman Kohman's\nLife and Love of Astronomy\, 1916-2010 by Diane Tur
 nshek\n\n\nCarnegie Mellon University\nURL:  http://www.cmu.edu/physics\n\
 nTruman Kohman\, an astronomer from Pittsburgh (CMU) who died in 2010\n\n\
 nDiane Turnshek teaches astronomy at CMU\, Pitt and St. Vincent\, and coor
 dinates the physics outreach at CMU. St. Vincent’s planetarium boasts a 
 state-of-the-art Spitz SciDome projector. Diane worked as a planetarium op
 erator at the Carnegie Science Center's Buhl Planetarium\, assisting in th
 e production of shows. In her astronomy outreach efforts\, she has visited
  to schools\, libraries\, camps\, Scouts and Congress. She hosts a monthly
  public lecture series at Allegheny Observatory. She has consulted with ma
 ny who wished to keep their science accurate\, from authors to opera compa
 nies. She is a science fiction author and editor\, whose short fiction has
  been published in Analog Magazine and elsewhere.\n\nINTRO SPONSOR: The De
 partment of Physics at Carnegie Mellon University in Pittsburgh\, PA is pr
 oud to sponsor 365 Days of Astronomy and its efforts to bring the world to
 gether in appreciati...
LOCATION:http://365daysofastronomy.org/calendar/
END:VEVENT
