BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:CANCWagman Winterfest
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20120225
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20120225
DTSTAMP:20260224T194052Z
UID:ba4289e4-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:1v095vg3rea5hl7encqla5738c@google.com\n<p> CANCELLED</p>\n<p>  
   Several of us just discussed the current weather conditions and we have 
 canceled tonight's Winterfest Star Party because of several factors.  None
  of the four sources that I checked indicate any significant clearing.  Th
 ere's still light show predicted until after midnight.  The cold temperatu
 res combined with winds from 15 MPH\, gusting to 35 MPH will make it impos
 sible for observing and extremely hazardous to any and all optics.\n    Be
 tter luck next year and for our first star party of the regular season on 
 March 31.\n \nTom </p> \n<p> as per Tom's 2/25/2012 12:21:09 P.M Yahoo pos
 t\, KD</p>\n\n<p><a href="http://nightsky.jpl.nasa.gov/event-view.cfm?Even
 t_ID=31723"> Wagman Winterfest Event Post</a></p>\n\n<p><a href="http://ww
 w.3ap.org/winterfest/"> Wagman Winterfest Webpage</a></p>\n\nhttp://www.3a
 p.org/winterfest/\n\n<p>Wagman Observatory \nDeer Lakes Regional Park\, Al
 legheny County\,\n40.626550 / -79.812950 \nAddress: 225 Kurn Road\, Tarent
 um\, PA 15084 </p>\n\n\n \n\n\n<p>2012 Star Party Schedule</p>\nMingo Cree
 k Park Observatory April 27 & 28 May 25 & 26 June 22 & 23 July 6\, 7\, 20 
 & 21 August 10 & 11 September 8 & 22 October 6 & 20\nNicholas E. Wagman Ob
 servatory February 25\, Winterfest March 31\nApril 27\,28 May 25\,26 June 
 22\,23 July 27\,28 August 24\,25 September 8\, 22 October 6\,20
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mingo SP
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20110805
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20110805
DTSTAMP:20260224T194052Z
UID:ba460880-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:j2g45c0jn740009i6idcinujng@google.com\n<p> Having a Vesta Fiest
 a?\nNASA's Dawn spacecraft is closing in on the asteroid Vesta. On August 
 6th\, Vesta is in opposition so your star party event can take advantage o
 f the view. \n\nAny of your Public Night Sky Network Calendar events sched
 uled for August 5\, 6\, and 7 will also be featured on Dawn's Vesta Fiesta
  map under "Attend an Event"\nhttp://dawn.jpl.nasa.gov/news/vesta_fiesta.a
 sp\n\nJoin the celebration and tune into Bill Nye and Mission Scientists L
 ive on Streaming Video: \nhttp://dawn.jpl.nasa.gov/news/vesta_fiesta_dawn_
 ps.asp</p><p>2011 Mingo Public Star Parties</p> April 8&9 May 6&7 June 3&4
  July 8&9 August 5&6 August 20 MCPO Picnic September 17 October 1\,15\,&29
 </p>\n<p>Nicholas E. Wagman Observatory</p>\n\n\n<p> 2011  Star Party Sche
 dule</p>\n\n<p>Mar 12 Winterfest \nApril 8 and 9\nMay 6 and 7\nJune 10 and
  11\nJuly 8 and 9\nAugust 5 and 6\nSeptember 2 and 3 and 17 for Dark Sky S
 P\nOctober 8 and 15 for Moonrise SP\nStar Parties begin at dusk.\n \nClub 
 picnic at Deer Lakes Park and members' star party will be June 25 at Minno
 w 2.\n
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NTaurids
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20091111
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20091111
DTSTAMP:20260224T194052Z
UID:ba4acbc2-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:h1a88bu1svhlt0mnuuodfevdq0@google.com\nFrom EarthsndSky\,org\nN
 ovember 12\, 2009 North Taurids\nLike the South Taurids\, this shower is l
 ong lasting (October 12 – December 2) but modest\, and the peak number i
 s forecast at about 7 meteors per hour. Because the South and North Taurid
 s overlap\, there’s some chance of catching a few extra meteors in the m
 ix. Typically\, you see the maximum numbers at around 1 a.m.\, when Taurus
  the Bull rides high in the sky. This year\, the waning crescent moon is a
  minor annoyance at most\, making 2009 a favorable year for the North Taur
 ids. Expect to see the greatest numbers at late night and after midnight o
 n the night November 11-12\, though a few days before and after may offer 
 good viewing as well.\n\nKD 
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
