BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Starhopping sessions
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20121008
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20121008
DTSTAMP:20260224T194052Z
UID:ba85cf56-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:mr4pq6fgrus9llp246bkdqobk0@google.com\nWagman Observatory direc
 tor Tom Reiland will lead an informal class on how to use your telescope a
 nd binoculars to "star hop" to objects of interest. Star hopping involves 
 using star charts to plan your "route" to move the scope from an easily lo
 catable object (like a bright star) to an object not visible to the unaide
 d eye (like a faint galaxy).\n\nAlso covered are topics such as aligning f
 inderscopes\, collimating Newtonian Reflectors and other handy items to en
 hance your viewing pleasure.\n
LOCATION:Wagman Observaotry\, Deer Lakes Park
END:VEVENT
