BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NSN Moon Telecon 9P
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20100722
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20100722
DTSTAMP:20260224T194053Z
UID:bad5763c-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:qrlg65ca6bvuue51ucrjevboic@google.com\nTELECON: Radar Love to O
 bserve the Moon\n\n\nOn Thursday\, July 22nd the Night Sky Network will ho
 st a telecon with two\nspeakers:\n-  Lunar and Planetary scientist Dr. Cat
 herine Neish. Dr. Neish's\npresentation is entitled "Radar Love: Using the
  LRO Mini-RF\, a synthetic\naperture radar on board NASA's Lunar Reconnais
 sance Orbiter for\nexploration". \n-  Mike Simmons sharing with us his ins
 ight on International Observe the\nMoon Night (InOMN). Mike was Co-chair o
 f the hugely successful high-profile\nIYA 2009 100 Hours of Astronomy and 
 has been an amateur astronomer for more\nthan 35 years.\n\nTo join the Tel
 econference on Thursday\, July 22nd at 6:00 pm PDT (9:00 pm\nEastern):\nCa
 ll the toll-free conference line:1-888-455-9236\nCall anytime after 5:45 p
 m the evening of the telecon. An operator will\nanswer and:\n- You will be
  asked for the passcode: NIGHT SKY NETWORK\n- You will be asked to give yo
 ur NAME and the CLUB you belong to\, and\nnumber of people listening with 
 you.\n\nThe PowerPoints and all other downloads and links will be found he
 re by\nJuly 21st: http://nightsky.jpl.nasa.gov/download-view.cfm?Doc_ID=45
 7\n\nOn Thursday\, July 22nd the Night Sky Network will host a telecon wit
 h two\nspeakers:\n-  Lunar and Planetary scientist Dr. Catherine Neish. Dr
 . Neish's\npresentation is entitled "Radar Love: Using the LRO Mini-RF\, a
  synthetic\naperture radar on board NASA's Lunar Reconnaissance Orbiter fo
 r\nexploration". \n-  Mike Simmons sharing with us his insight on Internat
 ional Observe the\nMoon Night (InOMN). Mike was Co-chair of the hugely suc
 cessful high-profile\nIYA 2009 100 Hours of Astronomy and has been an amat
 eur astronomer for more\nthan 35 years.\n\nTo join the Teleconference on T
 hursday\, July 22nd at 6:00 pm PDT (9:00 pm\nEastern):\nCall the toll-free
  conference line:1-888-455-9236\nCall anytime after 5:45 pm the evening of
  the telecon. An operator will\nanswer and:\n- You will be asked for the p
 asscode: NIGHT SKY NETWORK\n- You will be asked to give your NAME and the 
 CLUB you belong to\, and\nnumber of people listening with you.\n\nThe Powe
 rPoints and all other downloads and links will be found here by\nJuly 21st
 : http://nightsky.jpl.nasa.gov/download-view.cfm?Doc_ID=457
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Off-Site Baldwin Borough Library
DTSTART:20261022T230000Z
DTEND:20261023T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194053Z
UID:bada972a-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:31ctv7fk2vsn3vpf8va40sbaru@google.com\nCome enjoy the night sky
  with members of the Amateur Astronomers Association of Pittsburgh.  We&#
 39\;ll start the evening with a short\, astronomy themed presentation\, an
 d then attendees will be invited to look through member&#39\;s telescopes 
 and observe star clusters\, nebulae and even galaxies.\n\nThe topic of the
  presentation will be binocular astronomy.  We&#39\;ll discuss binocular 
 basics\, their use and what you can see.  Once it gets dark\, we&#39\;ll 
 have a station set up with astronomers using a laser pointer to pinpoint s
 pecific targets for you to observe through you&#39\;re own binoculars.\n\n
 Do you have a telescope\, but aren&#39\;t sure how to use it?  Bring it a
 long and one of our members will answer questions and help you get it set 
 up.
LOCATION:Colewood Park\, Pittsburgh\, PA 15236\, USA
END:VEVENT
