BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wagman/WCCC 7:30P
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20110915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20110915
DTSTAMP:20260224T194053Z
UID:bb128612-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:q62jmkm5q9ht1o48p5ebb4kpg8@google.com\n\nRuss and I decided to 
 move the WCCC SP to Sep 15.  He wants to give his students another classro
 om session before they come up to Wagman.\n \nTom  2:30PM 9/8/2011\n \n\nU
 pdate of Sunday 9/4/2011 6PM\nThe star party is at Wagman Observatory\, we
 ather permitting\, starting at 7:30 PM.  I probably won't need much assist
 ance since there be 10 or less students and the teacher.\n \nTom\n\nUpdate
  of Sunday 9/4/2011 5PM\nActually\, it's Russell Namie teaching the WCCC c
 lass\, not Glenn Smith.  We won't reschedule this star party until we are 
 certain that the conditions will make it impossible to conduct any observi
 ng.  It's way too early to make any rash decisions.  If I would have gone 
 by the earlier forecasts for this past weekend\, both nights would have be
 en canceled.\n  \nTom\n\nI've tentatively scheduled a class from WCCC from
  Sept 8\, a Thursday starting around 8 PM.  I'll have confirmation on this
  in a week are two.\nThe Girl Scout Group that was rained out in May will 
 at Wagman Obs on Saturday\, Oct 1.  It will start at 7:30 PM.\nLet me know
  if you can assist with either or both of these events.\nI'm certain that 
 more will be posted later on.\nThanks in advance for your help.\n \nTom\n\
 n__._\,_.___
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Audobon/Telescopes
DTSTART:20131009T000000Z
DTEND:20131009T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194053Z
UID:bb1569f4-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:t4ocho72nuqumccgge5a6i78no@google.com\nWe used to have folks fr
 om Amateur Astronomers come out for our programs in years past\, but I thi
 nk a long series of very cloudy nights caused those to trail off. \n\nWe w
 ould love to rekindle that relationship with you. We are having a night hi
 ke/star gazing program on October 7th at our Succop Conservancy in Butler\
 , and October 8th at our Beechwood Farms location in Fox Chapel.  Both pro
 grams are from 8-10 pm. Our idea was to have a hike led by our naturalists
 \, and also allow time for folks to do some star gazing\, and learn more a
 bout the night sky. \n\nAAAPers please contact Gabi:\n\nGabi Hughes | Envi
 ronmental Educator\n\nAudubon Society of Western Pennsylvania\n\n614 Dorse
 yville Road\, Pittsburgh\, PA 15238\n\n412-963-6100 x21  | aswp.org\n\n \n
 \n\n
LOCATION:None
END:VEVENT
