BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Membership Meeting
DTSTART:20090117T003000Z
DTEND:20090117T013000Z
DTSTAMP:20260224T194055Z
UID:bc30aad8-11b8-11f1-ab09-766b39882e0f
DESCRIPTION:fvnide0clop9s6etegcoga9ri4@google.com\n 1/16/2009\, (Reschedule
 d fr/ 1/9/09)7:30 PM\, Carnegie Science Center\, Pittsburgh\, Main Auditor
 ium\, $3 Parking Fee at CSC Parking Lot.\n\nAAAP President\, Ed Moss\, wil
 l\ndiscuss “Measuring the Universe: Man’s Quest to\nChart the Horizons
  of Space and Time”.\n\n“We go back to ancient times to discover the p
 eople and ideas that contributed to mankind's knowledge of the size and st
 ructure of the Universe. We continue on to\nGalileo and Cassini and others
  in the sixteenth and seventeenth centuries.Knowledge is added in a cumula
 tive manner until webhave an understanding of the Solar system and the rel
 ationship between its parts and the distant stars. We do not\, as of the s
 eventeenth century\, have a complete understanding of the Universe\, but t
 he foundation has been laid to put mankind on the right path to knowledge.
  We will look at the events and people who built this foundation for those
  who would follow. We will see how Aristotle\, Eratosthenes\, Aristarchus\
 , Hipparchus\, and Ptolemy\, each increased our knowledge by building on w
 hat went before. We will look at all these individuals and their contribut
 ion to mankind's knowledge of the size and distances of our universe”.\n
 \nContemporary knowledge seekers are encouraged to come out\nFriday the 9t
 h to climb on the shoulders of giants and chart the horizons of space and 
 time.\n
LOCATION:Carnegie Science Center
END:VEVENT
