 urThursday\, June 18\, 2026Thunderbird Music Hall4053 Butler Street\, Pitt
 sburgh\, PADoors @ 7PMShow @ 8PMAGE RESTRICTION: 18+ or with legal guardia
 n\nhttps://www.winyahband.com/\nThere’s a raw\, restless fire at the hea
 rt of Winyah’s music – in the crackle of their guitars\, the growl of
  Thomas Rowland’s voice\, and songs that always feel like they’rechasi
 ng something just out of reach. With southern swagger\, indie rock bite\, 
 and an unforgettable live show\, the South Carolina five-piece are quickl
 y emerging as one ofthe most exciting new bands in the country\, fueled by
  high ambitions and the desire to build a real community – a space wher
 e people can feel something\, escape\, or just be. Having already played 
 Bonnaroo and Lollapalooza and sold out their first headline tour\, Winyah
  are pushing themselves harder than ever – with an upcoming sophomore al
 bum that promises more of that same friction\, soul\, and intentional son
 gwriting that’s carried them this far. They’re dreamers intent on bec
 oming a face of the new rock-and-roll revival\, building something meant 
 to be felt – together.\nTicket Tier Info:General Admission Tickets – S
 tanding Room Only\nThere are no additional entry protocols at this time.
  Entry requirements are subject to change. By purchasing tickets to this e
 vent you agree to abide by entry requirements in effect at the time of 
 the event. Check the venue website leading up to your event for the latest
  protocols. Please visit https://thunderbirdmusichall.com/safety/ for more
  information on Covid-19 Safety. All sales are final. 
LOCATION:Thunderbird Music Hall
