BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AcoustiCafe Open Stage
DTSTART:20260316T230000Z
DTEND:20260317T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260311T210535Z
UID:0c6b5058-1d8e-11f1-a354-7a8ffbe756ab
DESCRIPTION:https://mrsmalls.com/events/acousticafe-open-stage-31/\nMONDAY 
 MARCH 16\, 2026 - WYEP 91.3 and Straub Brewing Presents: AcoustiCafe Open 
 Stage with host Mark Dignam ft Sickbed and Johanna Sö!!\nTheme. I May Nev
 er Write Another Song Like This One!\n\nBring out your masterworks (or you
 r disasters!) to let the almost-Spring sun shine on its face\, let the win
 d be at its back\, and let the road rise to greet it\, and we're totally n
 ot going to mention St P-mmpfhmrmf day!\n\nMARK DIGNAM is presenting his a
 nnual Calm Before The Storm tribute to Irish Culture this Fri Mar 13 at Th
 e Original Pittsburgh Winery - in the show\, Mark farms out his favorite t
 raditional and contemporary songs from his homeland to local Pittsburghers
 \, who then interpret them as they will\, and go on to perform one of thei
 r own original songs to round out their sets. Featured performers include 
 Mirabelle Skipworth\, Kelsey Wooley Jumper\, Clinton Clegg\, Anne Eliza\, 
 Danny Rectenwald and many more!!\n\nSICKBED plays the music of The Pogues 
 this Saturday at Poetry featuring Eric George\, Pete Bush\, Sean Dwyer Enr
 ight\, Micki Rockenhauser\, Dru Laswell\, Megan Williams\, Pete Guellard\,
  and Steve Sciuli - with Symington Reed & DJ Poptone opening!!\n\nJOHANNA 
 SÖ left Pittsburgh before the pandemic to join Canadian Celtic/folk rocke
 rs The Town Pants and has been touring the universe ever since. The Town P
 ants will play Friday Mar 20 at The Original Pittsburgh Winery\, we're so 
 psyched that Johanna is arriving a little early to hang out with her old b
 uds at AcoustiCafe!!
LOCATION:AcoustiCafe Open Stage
END:VEVENT
