BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Live Album Series: TIM
DTSTART:20260501T000000Z
DTEND:20260501T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260315T190138Z
UID:64f15efa-20a1-11f1-975d-e6256a7f25df
DESCRIPTION:https://app.opendate.io/e/live-album-series-tim-april-30-2026-6
 73122\n  Every generation has it's share of bands who get filed away as pe
 rennial critical darlings yet commercially misunderstood\, only to be redi
 scovered decades later\; The Replacements may be the poster child of that 
 phenomenon for the 80s. Perpetually underselling\, perpetually tripping ov
 er themselves - both literally and metaphorically - there's a reason they'
 ve long been called "the best band to never make it" (although the fact th
 at they spawned an album great enough to join our Live Album series may ac
 tually be proof they did).   TIM was their first major labor effort\, prod
 uced by punk rock god Tommy Ramone himself - and it comes jammed with clas
 sics from a range of Rock & Roll Influences - from the Roy Oberson tinged 
 Swingin Party to the college radio anthem Left of the Dial - the honky ton
 k Stones find a home on Waitress in the Sky\, and Big Star shines through 
 on album opener Hold My Life. Hell\, even their hit Can't Hardly Wait was 
 written during this period of the band\, before being set aside for their 
 follow up effort. It had everything it needed to be a classic\; but in tru
 e Replacements fashion - a series of bizarre circumstances took hold\; was
  tinnitus to blame for Tommy's sloppy mix of the album? Who exactly smuggl
 ed alcohol into their SNL dressing room\, turning what could've been a bre
 akthrough performance into an expletive laden drunken mess (which led to t
 hem being banned from 8H) - which in hindsight is probably a better histor
 ical record of The Replacements than even the greatest performance could'v
 e given them.  We're not in Minnesota\, but dive bar rock always sounds gr
 eat at Bottlerocket. So grab a beer (or a couple) and join TV's Norm bring
 s this classic record to life front to back!   
LOCATION:Bottlerocket Social Hall
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sun King Warriors
DTSTART:20260502T233000Z
DTEND:20260503T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20260316T150119Z
UID:fd58cce4-2148-11f1-9e18-d2591aeff2e8
DESCRIPTION:https://mrsmalls.com/events/sun-king-warriors-2/\nJim Donovan a
 nd The Sun King Warriors are best described as a blend of rhythm heavy roo
 ts rock\, with a strong dose of big barreling drums. Think bluesy Zeppelin
 -esqe bombast\, Santana style percussion with wild Avett Brothers energy.A
 t a Sun King show\, you can expect to dance\, sweat and have the time of y
 our life.The band's music has garnered radio airplay throughout the US and
  Canada\, and has appeared on Billboard’s Americana chart multiple times
 .The band plays regionally at festivals and clubs throughout the mid-atlan
 tic and have opened for 10\,000 Maniacs\, Donovan's former band Rusted Roo
 t and many others.Jim Donovan\, the band’s founder and writer brings alm
 ost three decades of experience to the Sun King Warriors. As a member of t
 he popular 90’s band Rusted Root\, he helped shaped the group’s sound 
 and toured with legendary including The Grateful Dead\, members of Led Zep
 pelin\, Carlos Santana and the Allman Brothers.He also co-authored the ban
 d’s biggest hit\, “Send Me on My Way\,” which has been streamed over
  100 million times on Spotify and used as the wakeup music for NASA’s Ma
 rs rover.This Event Is All AgesAll Sales Are Final.
LOCATION:The Sanctuary at Mr. Smalls
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:MELISSA VILLASENOR (Saturday\, Early)
DTSTART:20260516T230000Z
DTEND:20260517T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260317T040117Z
UID:f2fea3be-21b5-11f1-9e18-d2591aeff2e8
DESCRIPTION:https://app.opendate.io/e/melissa-villasenor-saturday-early-may
 -16-2026-650454\n  Melissa Villasenor broke barriers by becoming the first
 -ever Latina cast member of Saturday Night Live. A comedic impressions exp
 ert\, she got her start as a semifinalist on America’s Got Talent. Some 
 of Melissa’s most memorable SNL impressions include Owen Wilson\, Lady G
 aga\, and Dolly Parton.   An accomplished voice actor\, she has voiced cha
 racters on several television shows including Nickelodeon’s OK K.O.! and
  Rock\, Paper\, Scissors\, and in films Toy Story 4 and Wreck It Ralph 2: 
 Ralph Breaks the Internet\, for which she received a Golden Globe nominati
 on. Melissa was a guest on Jerry Seinfeld’s Comedians in Cars Getting Co
 ffee\, and can be seen in Barry\, Crashing\, and Awkwafina is Nora From Qu
 eens\, to name a few.   Why'd We Book It? Melissa's time on SNL left an im
 pression on anyone who watched - There is nothing better than the Nickelba
 ck sketch or Dirty Talk with Donald Glover. Her talent goes beyond just th
 is as it is always exciting to sit in a theater and know the distinct voic
 e you are hearing is one of your favorite comics. She is incredibly talent
 ed all around as an artist and podcaster in her personal life. All this sa
 id\, we cannot wait to have Melissa join us and hope you are just as excit
 ed.    For Fans Of... Kate McKinnon\, Jenny Slate\, Maria Bamford   Extend
 ed Bio: Her multihyphenate talents range even further. Melissa hosted the 
 2021 Independent Spirit Awards\, published a self-help journal ‘Whoops\,
  I’m Awesome\,’ recorded two music albums\, had a Netflix special\, an
 d creates fine art.  Some of Melissa’s acknowledgements include Forbes 3
 0 Under 30\, Rolling Stone’s 50 Funniest People Right Now\, and CNN’s 
 Women in Comedy.     Seating/Show Information: Limit 4 tickets per transac
 tion. You can not purchase tickets to multiple shows.   This show will hav
 e theater seating. Seats will be assigned upon arrival\, or can be chosen 
 ahead of time for an additional fee.   QR Code Ordering will be available 
 for this performance.  Doors open at 5pm.  Don't miss our famous Bottleroc
 ket Pre-Show Clip Collection\, beginning one hour before the start of the 
 performance.  This show is ALL AGES  *all information subject to change as
  needed.    Bottlerocket FAQ:   All shows starting before 10pm are all age
 s unless otherwise noted.  Free parking is available at 824 Industry Stree
 t and 205 Allen Street\, as well as other public lots in the area.  Live M
 usic shows have limited seating options\, please arrive early or reach out
  to the venue directly if you know that you require a seat.  Doors open at
  5pm for all shows unless noted otherwise. The time listed on the ticket i
 s the event's true start time.  Most shows have a preshow experience start
 ing 1 hour before the show.  All tickets are non-refundable - our full ref
 und policy can be viewed here  Please contact us ahead of time with any ac
 cesibilty requests or concerns\, we're happy to accomodate you.  More FAQ'
 s can be found here   
LOCATION:Bottlerocket Social Hall
END:VEVENT
