BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BOTTLEROCKET BOOK CLUB w/ Allegheny Land Trust
DTSTART:20260420T233000Z
DTEND:20260421T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20260325T210225Z
UID:ecc3c950-288d-11f1-acf4-6a63d21f6d0e
DESCRIPTION:https://app.opendate.io/e/bottlerocket-book-club-w-allegheny-la
 nd-trust-april-20-2026-658654\n The OFFICIAL Bottlerocket Book Club makes 
 its return with a NEW book\, and a NEW host organization for the month of 
 APRIL!  We’ll be meeting in the bar to discuss the BOOK OF THE MONTH\, e
 njoying some cocktails (or mocktails) and having a great time! This is an 
 inclusive event\, and all are welcome- even if it’s been a while since y
 ou’ve read anything!  Whether you’re a bookworm or just generally seek
 ing community and want to join a new club\, this is your chance! This mont
 h is for the NATURE LOVERS- we have Allegheny Land Trust leading the discu
 ssion on “THE SERVICEBERRY: ABUNDANCE AND RECIPROCITY IN THE NATURAL WOR
 LD” by author Robin Wall Kimmerer…which we recommend picking up locall
 y at WHITE WHALE BOOKS!   Book blurb:  As Indigenous scientist and author 
 of Braiding Sweetgrass Robin Wall Kimmerer harvests serviceberries alongsi
 de the birds\, she considers the ethic of reciprocity that lies at the hea
 rt of the gift economy. How\, she asks\, can we learn from Indigenous wisd
 om and the plant world to reimagine what we value most?   About ALLEGHENY 
 LAND TRUST: Allegheny Land trust is a 501c3 land conservation nonprofit th
 at has helped local people save local land in the Pittsburgh region since 
 1993. ALT conserves and cares for more than 4\,000 acres of green space\, 
 and everyone in Allegheny County lives within 8 miles of one of these land
 s. From large swaths of forested land to small plots of community gardens\
 , ALT applies its conservation toolbelt to conserving and stewarding local
  green space\, and invites people to these lands for environmental educati
 on programs 
LOCATION:Bottlerocket Social Hall
END:VEVENT
