UID:cee22550-2a52-11f1-acf4-6a63d21f6d0e
DESCRIPTION:https://www.poetrymillvale.com/event/christy-costello-cancel-th
 e-prom/\n$10 advance (from Humanitix\, and from the locals) and $12 door \
 nTickets on sale starting March 13 at Humanitix online\nand directly from 
 the local opening bands! \nhttps://events.humanitix.com/christy-costello-d
 umplings-cancel-the-prom-at-poetry-lounge \nMinnesota rock ‘n rolla (ex-
 Pink Mink\, Von Bondies)\nCHRISTY COSTELLO and the CC Club Band\nhttps://w
 ww.christycostellomusic.com/\nhttps://www.instagram.com/christylynncostell
 o/\nhttps://christycostello.bandcamp.com/music \n[Recommended if you like:
  Blondie\, Epoxies\, Amyl & Sniffers!] \nwith special guests\nDumplings  
 https://dumplings.bandcamp.com/music\nCancel the Prom  https://www.instag
 ram.com/canceltheprom/ \nChristy Costello is a mover and a shaker in the T
 win Cities music scene. She’s a songwriter\, multi-instrumentalist\, dis
 c jockey\, talent buyer\, promoter\, mother and yogi. Hailing from the Iro
 n Range of Northern Minnesota\, she is no stranger to the great outdoors. 
 \nHer music blends the ferocity and rawness of nature’s elements\, the n
 ew and exciting energy of a house show\, mixed with the adrenaline rush of
  an all-night downtown disco. Her first-rate songwriting has been showcase
 d in previous bands like Pink Mink and Ouija Radio\, as well as her raw an
 d unforgettable stage performances in Monica LaPlante\, Butchers Union\, T
 he Von Bondies and Extraterrestrials. This is Christy’s turn to step to 
 the front.
