BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Big Jus & Steeltown Horns X NASH.V.ILL
DTSTART:20260422T193000Z
DTEND:20260422T203000Z
DTSTAMP:20260403T150122Z
UID:fabf6c26-2f6d-11f1-90fe-46795bee91d1
DESCRIPTION:https://mrsmalls.com/events/big-jus-nash-v-ill/\nOFFSITE EVENT:
  This event will take place at Market Square\, Downtown.Big Jus & Steeltow
 n Horns bring a powerful blend of hip-hop\, soul\, and live brass energy s
 traight out of the Pittsburgh area. Fronted by rapper Big Jus\, the group 
 delivers high-energy performances backed by the rich sound of live horns a
 nd a stellar band led by world-renowned trombonist Reggie Watkins of Steel
 town Horns. Together they create a powerful fusion of street storytelling 
 and classic live band arrangements. Known for engaging crowds and bringing
  real-life experiences into their music\, Big Jus & Steeltown Horns repres
 ent the spirit\, resilience\, and culture of the Steel City. Whether perfo
 rming at festivals\, nightclubs\, or live events\, their unique sound brid
 ges hip-hop and live band performance\, leaving audiences energized and in
 spired.NASH.V.ILL is one of the most sought-after live acts in the Pittsbu
 rgh region — and for good reason. Known for their high-energy\, explosiv
 e performances\, this Pittsburgh-based band delivers a singular musical ex
 perience that fuses funk\, rock\, soul\, blues\, alternative\, and gospel 
 into something entirely their own. What makes NASH.V.ILL truly special is 
 their rare ability to connect with everyone in the room. Whether the crowd
  is filled with young kids\, die-hard rock fans\, families\, or seniors\, 
 NASH.V.ILL commands the stage and brings every generation along for the ri
 de. In 2025\, the band released their debut EP\, It Takes a Village: Vol. 
 1 — a collection of emotionally rich\, heartfelt songs deeply rooted in 
 soul. The project announced NASH.V.ILL as a serious creative force with so
 mething meaningful to say. Their momentum continues to build. Pittsburgh's
  own 91.3 WYEP recently selected NASH.V.ILL as Local Artist of the Month\,
  a testament to their growing impact on the city's cultural landscape. Now
 \, they bring that energy to one of the biggest stages the city has ever s
 een — the 2026 NFL Draft in Pittsburgh. NASH.V.ILL doesn't just perform.
  They make you feel something.This Event Is All Ages
LOCATION:Offsite
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nino Albanese Trio with Liz Berlin
DTSTART:20260422T193000Z
DTEND:20260422T203000Z
DTSTAMP:20260403T150123Z
UID:fac36948-2f6d-11f1-90fe-46795bee91d1
DESCRIPTION:https://mrsmalls.com/events/nino-albanese-trio/\nOFFSITE EVENT:
  This event will take place at One Oxford Center\, Grant St.\, Downtown.Ni
 no Albanese leads a blues driven trio that blends elements of funk\, rock 
 n' roll\, and fusion with improvisation to create a unique experience for 
 every live performance. The trio features Mars on bass guitar and Clarence
  Grant II on drums.Liz Berlin is a founding member of the multi platinum P
 ittsburgh band Rusted Root and has spent more than three decades performin
 g across the United States. She is co owner of Mr. Smalls Theatre\, founde
 r of We Rock Workshopwhich provides free music education for current and f
 ormer foster youth\, and teaches Live Music Touring and Revenue Streams at
  Carnegie Mellon University. Her solo performances are powerful\, hypnotic
 \, and deeply personal\, blending folk\, rock\, and global influences into
  an intimate and dynamic live experience.Danny is integrally rooted in the
  Pittsburgh music scene playing guitar and mandolin in various groups in t
 he area. He maintains a busy performance calendar\, playing solo and in-co
 llaboration at the local and national levels. Danny’s music has been hea
 rd across the entire dial of local radio\, including WRCT\, WQED\, WYEP\, 
 WDVE\, and WXDX. His music has also been utilized commercially\, most nota
 bly his composition\, "Road Song\,” which was used for a nationally-tele
 vised Scott's Lawn Care commercial.Gibson Musisko and Vanessa Prentiss of 
 PosterChild\, a Pittsburgh-based indie rock band.Chet Vincent is a singer 
 songwriter from Pittsburgh\, PA. He recently released an album\, "Static O
 n The Radio" with his band Chet Vincent & The Music Industry.This Event Is
  All Ages
LOCATION:Offsite
END:VEVENT
