BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gully Boys
DTSTART:20260509T000000Z
DTEND:20260509T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260403T180117Z
UID:1c8971e4-2f87-11f1-843d-46795bee91d1
DESCRIPTION:https://mrsmalls.com/events/gully-boys/\nThe Gully Boys origin 
 story begins in the aisles of a Minneapolis thrift shop. Vocalist/guitaris
 t\nKathy Callahan (she/her) and co-worker Nadirah McGill (they/them) spent
  their days sharing\ndreams and building a friendship amongst racks of for
 gotten treasures. When Kathy confided\nher desire to sing in a band\, it s
 et off a groundswell of events: Nadi grabbed a pair of\ndrumsticks\, and t
 he two invited middle school friend Natalie Klemond (she/her) to join on b
 ass.\nFrom there\, a cover of Best Coast’s “Girlfriend” marked the s
 tart of a journey fueled by\nundeniable chemistry\, channeling the raw ene
 rgy of legends like No Doubt\, Garbage\, and Hole\ninto a sound that’s g
 alvanizingly Gully.Two years of relentless gigging followed\, and earned G
 ully Boys the Best New Band crown by\ntheir local Minneapolis City Pages i
 n 2018\, shortly after the release of their debut demo\ncollection\, Not S
 o Brave. Their anticipated follow-up EP\, Phony\, arrived in late 2019\, j
 ust months\nbefore the live music world came to a halt. Inspired by this b
 reak in the action\, the band added\nlead guitarist Mariah Mercedes (they/
 them)\, and worked with producer Zach Zurn at Carpet\nBooth Studio to rele
 ase their Favorite Son EP (2021) and standout singles “See You See”\n(
 2022) and “Optimist” (2023).Grounded in a bond as fierce as their soun
 d\, Gully Boys’ electrifying live performances have\nearned them spots o
 n SXSW stages\, Audiotree sessions\, and tours alongside Nova Twins\,\nMot
 ion City Soundtrack\, Destroy Boys\, Bad Bad Hats\, and more. From the ico
 nic stage at\nMinneapolis’ First Avenue to national gigs that defy expec
 tations\, Gully Boys capture an ethos\nof equal parts anger and tenderness
 —fueling a journey that feels like it’s just getting started.This Even
 t Is All AgesAll Sales Are Final.
LOCATION:The Funhouse at Mr. Smalls
END:VEVENT
