BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Evening With Vanessa Carlton: Veils Tour
DTSTART:20260424T233000Z
DTEND:20260425T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20260412T180149Z
UID:adc6cf6c-3699-11f1-887f-fef293e589ee
DESCRIPTION:https://tickets.citywinery.com/event/an-evening-with-vanessa-ca
 rlton-veils-tour-ucokyq\nCity Winery Pittsburgh presents An Evening With V
 anessa Carlton: Veils Tour live on Friday\, April 24th\, at 7:30PM\, part 
 of a multi-show series. View all Pittsburgh dates and times here!(opens in
  a new tab)Vanessa Carlton continues to expand creatively as an artist as 
 seen in her upcoming seventh studio album Veils produced by Dave Fridmann 
 (MGMT\, Flaming Lips) to be released early 2026. Fridmann also produced he
 r last album Love is An Art (2020).“The album will of course mean differ
 ent things to different people and that is what excites me. I had to embra
 ce my own contradictions in order to see what the world of the album was g
 oing to feel and sound like\,” says Carlton. “I love the metaphor of w
 earing a veil. There are so many layers to all of us. When I look back on 
 the four year process\, I see that I was gradually becoming fascinated wit
 h stoicism.”Through her songs\, Vanessa invites listeners to explore the
  Veils in their own lives. Which Veil are you lifting? Which Veil are you 
 putting on?“Our veils tell a story\, when we choose to take one off or w
 hen we put one on…it is such a personal act\,” says Carlton.Vanessa re
 cently unveiled the first track “Animal” off the upcoming album that l
 ays the foundation in her pursuit for stoicism. Vanessa shared that the so
 ng is about\, “The idea of knowing we cannot control external forces\; s
 he is being hunted and she accepts the reality of what is happening. The a
 cceptance allows her to truly see the animal. Does she even identify with 
 this creature? Every human has an animal within them. Are you hunting? Are
  you being hunted? Who is the animal?”Carlton has constantly challenged 
 both herself and the expectations that surround her throughout her lengthy
 \, accomplished career: she was discovered as a singer-songwriter/pianist 
 when a cassette tape demo was given to legendary music impresario Ahmet Er
 tegun. With her debut single "A Thousand Miles\," Carlton soared to the to
 p of the Billboard charts and garnered multiple Grammy nominations\, and c
 ontinues to captivate audiences across generations as well as genres. VICE
 ’s documentary on “A Thousand Miles” earned the media outlet a 2022 
 News & Documentary Emmy nomination – Watch docuseries here.Though “A T
 housand Miles” is only a small fraction of her body of work and artistic
  identity\, as she continues to evolve as a performer and songwriter. In t
 he summer of 2019\, she made her Broadway debut as Carole King in Beautifu
 l: The Carole King Musical. Carlton most recently scored her first film wi
 th husband John McCauley of Deer Tick for Wish You Were Here directed by J
 ulia Stiles.$1 of every ticket will go to benefit Save The Music and their
  support for music in the schools!Dine At Your Show🍽️  We provide foo
 d and beverage service directly to your table in the venue. Or\, for an ex
 panded menu and more relaxed experience\, arrive early and enjoy a meal in
  our restaurant before the show. When dining in the restaurant\, reservati
 ons are encouraged and can be made via Resy starting one month before the 
 show. View Our Concert Dining Menu.(opens in a new tab)Wine At Your Table(
