BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Eric Bellinger
DTSTART:20260502T233000Z
DTEND:20260503T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20260412T180150Z
UID:adf9d434-3699-11f1-887f-fef293e589ee
DESCRIPTION:https://tickets.citywinery.com/event/eric-bellinger-95sxdh\nCit
 y Winery Pittsburgh presents  Eric Bellinger live on Saturday\, May 2nd\, 
 at 7:30 PM!Eric Bellinger's journey has been a remarkable evolution from t
 he streets of  Compton to becoming an international sensation\, marked by 
 his Grammy-winning  artistry and prolific songwriting skills. Hailing from
  a musical lineage as the  grandson of Bobby Day\, a hit songwriter for th
 e Jackson 5\, Eric faced the pivotal  decision of pursuing a career in ath
 letics or following his musical instincts. He  chose to listen to his hear
 t and committed to his art\, touching the world with not  only his powerfu
 l voice but also his adept songwriting skills.  One of the first pinnacle 
 moments in Bellinger’s career came with his Grammy  Award-winning contri
 butions to Chris Brown's album F.A.M.E.\, solidifying his  reputation as a
  sought-after songwriter. Collaborations with industry giants like  Usher\
 , Justin Bieber\, and Brandy further established his prowess. Opting for  
 independence\, Eric co-founded the YFS (Your Favorite Song) label\, challe
 nging  the constraints of major labels and achieving success with their EM
 PIRE distributed indie team. YFS’s 2016 campaign album Eric B. For Presi
 dent  produced gold singles "Drive By" and "GOAT."  In addition to his Gra
 mmy and Billboard success\, Eric Bellinger's discography  boasts a series 
 of mixtapes\, including "Born II Sing Vol. 1\, Born II Sing Vol. 2\,  and 
 Born II Sing Vol. 3 in 2013. His debut studio album\, The Rebirth\, releas
 ed as a  double album in 2014\, peaked at 23 on the US R&B/Hip Hop charts 
 and 15 on the  US R&B chart. Following The Rebirth\, Eric released studio 
 albums Cuffing Season and Cuffing Season\, Part 2\, which peaked at 6 and 
 23 on the US R&B  chart\, respectively. Mixtapes like Choose Up Season and
  Eventually in 2016  featured notable tracks like "Valet" featuring Fetty 
 Wap and 2 Chainz. Between  2016 and 2017\, Eric released three extended pl
 ays as part of the Eric B. for  President series. Notably\, the series fea
 tured the gold-certified singles "G.O.A.T."  and "Drive By." Further expan
 ding his discography\, Eric dropped the album Eazy  Call in 2018 and a 5-t
 rack EP\, Meditation Music\, inspired by yoga and meditation.  The EP refl
 ected a transformative period in Eric's life and was released during his  
 Eazy Call Tour. In 2021\, Eric Bellinger released New Light\, earning his 
 first  Grammy nomination for Best Progressive R&B Album. This album not on
 ly showcased his continued evolution and commitment to pushing creative  b
 oundaries but also set the stage for his remarkable achievements in the fo
 llowing  years. In May 2022\, Eric announced a publishing deal with Roc Na
 tion\, cementing  his status as a force in the music industry.  The moment
 um continued into 2023 when he dominated the airwaves and  Billboard chart
 s with his hit "Curious\," a flip of D’Angelo’s “Lady\,” featuring
   Cordae and Fabolous. The single surpassed a million views on YouTube\, r
 eached  #1 on Rhythmic Radio\, and climbed to #33 on the Top 40\, solidify
 ing Eric  Bellinger's position as a powerful bridge between talents in the
  industry and a true  hit-maker. His musical brilliance\, as highlighted i
 n "Curious\," showcases his  ability to break down and innovate on classic
  beats\, receiving praise from  D’Angelo himself. Another 2023 break-the
 -internet moment came when  Bellinger’s freestyle about marriage on the 
 Cosmic Kev show went viral and  became a hit recording\, followed by an ep
 ic collaboration with Lil’ Kim and Lola  Brooke on the “Curious” rem
 ix. As Eric is gearing up to release his next album\, he  wanted to do som
 ething different for the promotional run this time around. With  his upcom
 ing single “Cry In Front Of You” set to release\, he thought it was  i
 mportant for fans to see a more raw\, stripped down\, acoustic style perfo
 rmance to  highlight his vocal ability ahead of his new music. Eric plans 
 to slow it down &  open up to the people. An unplugged feel. Showing a mor
 e vulnerable side\, letting  the world deeper into his thoughts. The City 
 Winery Tour will be the perfect  setting to display just that. Beyond his 
 personal success\, Eric's wisdom extends to the establishment of his  arti
 st development firm and record label\, All Wins\, where he nurtures emergi
 ng  talents like Dom Belli\, Steven G\, and Hylan Starr. His dedication to
  being of  service to the next generation underscores his maturity and ins
 ight\, setting him  apart in the R&B game. With a career spanning over a d
 ecade\, Eric Bellinger's  influence in the genre is evident not just in hi
 s introspective lyrics and buttery  vocals but also in his strategic busin
 ess moves and authentic public persona. His  approach to recording "Curiou
 s\," as part of his album 1(800) HIT-EAZY: LINE 2\,  exemplifies his intui
 tive understanding of when to contribute more of his unique  perspective\,
  solidifying his enduring impact on the current R&B scene. Dine At Your Sh
 ow(opens in a new tab)🍽️  We provide food and beverage service direct
 ly to your table in the venue. Or\, for an expanded menu and more relaxed 
 experience\, arrive early and enjoy a meal in our restaurant before the sh
 ow. When dining in the restaurant\, reservations are encouraged and can be
  made via Resy starting one month before the show. View Our Concert Dining
  Menu.(opens in a new tab)Wine At Your Table(opens in a new tab)Reserve yo
 ur preferred wine by filling out this form(opens in a new tab) and have a 
