BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kindred The Family Soul
DTSTART:20260730T220000Z
DTEND:20260730T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260412T180151Z
UID:aed6a4e0-3699-11f1-887f-fef293e589ee
DESCRIPTION:https://tickets.citywinery.com/event/kindred-the-family-soul-kt
 he8o\nCity Winery Pittsburgh presents Kindred The Family Soul live on Thur
 sday\, July 30th\, at 6:00 PM\, part of a multi-show series. View all Pitt
 sburgh dates and times here!(opens in a new tab)Kindred the Family Soul is
  the husband-and-wife duo of Aja Graydon and Fatin Dantzler — artists\, 
 songwriters\, and proud parents whose music celebrates love\, family\, and
  resilience. Both began their musical journeys as teenagers\, with Fatin p
 roducing for Bell Biv DeVoe at 17 and Aja signing her first record deal at
  14 with Delicious Vinyl. Introduced in 1997 through The Roots’ producti
 on camp\, their creative chemistry evolved into partnership and marriage t
 he following year. After Fatin lost his day job\, the couple decided to pe
 rform together\, birthing Kindred the Family Soul. Their reputation grew a
 t Philadelphia’s iconic Black Lily showcase\, alongside talents like Jil
 l Scott\, Musiq Soulchild\, and Floetry. Jill Scott later introduced them 
 to Hidden Beach Recordings\, leading to their debut album\, Surrender to L
 ove (2003). The singles “Far Away” and “Stars” became top ten Urba
 n AC hits\, earning the duo a Soul Train Award and BET nomination. Their s
 econd album\, In This Life Together (2005)\, reinforced their image as amb
 assadors of “Black Love\,” with the hit “Where Would I Be (The Quest
 ion)” and the anthem “Woman First.” The follow-up\, The Arrival (200
 8)\, featured fan favorites “House of Love” and “Just the Way You Ar
 e\,” known for their heartfelt music videos. Amid industry shifts\, the 
 couple turned to self-documentation with the 2009 web series Six Is It!\, 
 chronicling family life while expecting their sixth child. In 2011\, they 
 partnered with Shanachie Records to release Love Has No Recession\, a soci
 ally conscious and critically acclaimed project compared to Marvin Gaye’
 s What’s Going On. The album included “Magic” and the Snoop Dogg col
 laboration “You Got Love\,” affirming their commitment to love and per
 severance. To celebrate their 10-year anniversary\, Kindred released a liv
 e digital album in 2013\, followed by A Couple Friends (2014). The project
  included a companion short film directed by Jamal Hill and their first ch
 ildren’s book\, Mama Said\, “Clean Up!” That year also marked the st
 art of two beloved community events in Philadelphia — Kindred the Family
  Games and Kindred the Family Reunion. In 2015\, the entire Dantzler famil
 y starred in a national Walmart commercial celebrating family reunions —
  garnering over a million YouTube views and becoming one of the retailer
 ’s most popular ads. Their 2016 release\, Legacy of Love\, featured the 
 chart-topping single “All My People\,” a timely anthem of unity and ho
 pe. The following year\, they launched Kindred Presents\, a web series spo
 tlighting artists and cultural voices. Their 2021 album\, Auntie & Unc\, s
 erved as both reflection and manifesto — a celebration of two decades of
  partnership\, growth\, and purpose. “We’re OGs in this Black Loveconv
 ersation\,” they say. “We’ve got wisdom to share\, but life keeps te
 aching.” 2024 and beyond: Kindred continues to tour and inspire audience
 s worldwide. Their latest project\, The Grand Life\, released October 3\, 
 2025\, showcases their timeless soul sound with fresh energy. The new sing
 le — a heartfelt remake of Frankie Beverly & Maze’s “I Need You” 
 — has already received rave reviews from fans and critics alike. Dine At
  Your Show(opens in a new tab)🍽️  We provide food and beverage servic
 e directly to your table in the venue. Or\, for an expanded menu and more 
 relaxed experience\, arrive early and enjoy a meal in our restaurant befor
 e the show. When dining in the restaurant\, reservations are encouraged an
 d can be made via Resy starting one month before the show. View Our Concer
 t Dining Menu.(opens in a new tab)Wine At Your Table(opens in a new tab)Re
 serve your preferred wine by filling out this form(opens in a new tab) and
  have a bottle waiting at your table when you arrive at your show. No more
  waiting for your first drink! We will save your wine preference and have 
 a bottle at your table for all future shows. When you want to change your 
 wine\, come back to this form and update your preference.2-item Per Person
  Minimum🎶  Kindly note there is a 2-item per person food & beverage min
 imum in the concert venue. Food and beverages ordered in the restaurant al
 so count towards the minimum.(opens in a new tab)Become a Vinofile Member(
 opens in a new tab)🍷  Members get 48 hour early access to new shows\, p
 ay no ticket fees\, and earn points to exchange for complimentary tickets.
  Vinofile Plus members also receive many wine benefits. Add a membership t
 o your cart during checkout to start saving now. Already a member? Make su
 re you are signed in to access your benefits. Become a Vinofile Member and
  enjoy the benefits today.(opens in a new tab)(opens in a new tab)(opens i
 n a new tab)DateJul30Doors Open4:30 PMLocationCity Winery Pittsburgh1627 S
 mallman StreetPittsburgh 15222United States(opens in a new tab)
LOCATION:City Winery Pittsburgh
END:VEVENT
