BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sound Series: Cut Worms with special guest Tchotchke
DTSTART:20260514T000000Z
DTEND:20260514T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260412T180152Z
UID:af123af0-3699-11f1-887f-fef293e589ee
DESCRIPTION:10000011-1778702400-1778709600@www.warhol.org\nWe welcome the B
 rooklyn-based singer-songwriter Cut Worms (aka Max Clarke) and his band on
  a tour supporting a new album on Jagjaguwar\, produced by Jeff Tweedy. Wi
 th the new album\, Clarke continues his exploration of what he calls “po
 p essentialism”\; mining the golden hits of yesteryear for a timeless so
 und\, he contemplates age-old questions through a modern lens. Cut Worm’
 s self-titled LP (2023) garnered a spot on the Billboard charts and was ha
 iled by Paste Magazine as one of the best rock albums of the year. He also
  joined Father John Misty on a tour last fall. New York-based pop rock tri
 o\, Tchotchke\, opens the evening. \n\nDoors open at 7:30 p.m.\nThis perfo
 rmance is primarily standing room only. Limited seating is available upon 
 advance request. We are committed to offering inclusive\, engaging experie
 nces for people of all abilities. To request accommodations to enhance you
 r visit\, please contact access@warhol.org or call 412.237.8354.
LOCATION:The Warhol entrance space\, 117 Sandusky Street\, Pittsburgh\, PA\
 , 15212\, United States
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Julia Warhola Mother’s Day
DTSTART:20260509T220000Z
DTEND:20260509T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260412T180152Z
UID:af16061c-3699-11f1-887f-fef293e589ee
DESCRIPTION:10001735-1778349600-1778360400@www.warhol.org\nMembers are invi
 ted to join Carnegie Museums to celebrate Mother’s Day the Julia Warhola
  way.  \nHaving artistic inclinations of her own\, Julia Warhola recogniz
 ed her son’s talent early on and encouraged him in various art activitie
 s. They frequently collaborated on his art projects\, with Julia contribut
 ing her unique handwriting to Warhol’s drawings\, most often as the sign
 ature. Mingle with fellow members over light refreshments\, food and activ
 ities! \n*Refreshments\, food and giveaways available while supplies last.
LOCATION:The Andy Warhol Museum\, 117 Sandusky Street\, Pittsburgh\, PA\, 1
 5212\, United States
END:VEVENT
