BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sound Series: Sunny War
DTSTART:20260617T000000Z
DTEND:20260617T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260412T180152Z
UID:af344640-3699-11f1-887f-fef293e589ee
DESCRIPTION:10001191-1781640000-1781640000@www.warhol.org\nWe welcome back 
 folk/blues/punk songwriter Sunny War (aka Sydney Lyndella Ward) to our int
 imate theater\, on a tour supporting her latest album Armageddon in a Summ
 er Dress on New West Records. Originally from Nashville\, she released her
  debut album\, Worthless\, in 2014. On this new album\, Sunny further refi
 nes her distinct aesthetic at the intersections of punk and roots music. A
 s she puts it\, “To me it’s the same kind of music. If you’re into p
 unk for the lyrics and the message\, there’s definitely a lot of old-tim
 e music that has that spirit.” \n\nDoors open at 7 p.m.
LOCATION:The Warhol theater\, 117 Sandusky Street\, Pittsburgh\, PA\, 15212
 \, United States
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Youth Invasion 2026: America Rewritten
DTSTART:20260508T210000Z
DTEND:20260508T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20260412T180152Z
UID:af37c9aa-3699-11f1-887f-fef293e589ee
DESCRIPTION:10001267-1778259600-1778277600@www.warhol.org\nJoin us for our 
 annual teen takeover of The Warhol! \nYouth Invasion 2026: America Rewrit
 ten is a night led by our Youth Arts Council celebrating 250 years of yout
 h and revolt. Participate in the counterculture by enjoying live music\, p
 erformance\, silkscreen printing\, and a special murder mystery. Tickets f
 or Youth Invasion are free when you register for a free teen membership. P
 lease note the museum will be open to the general public during this event
  as part of our normal Friday evening operating hours.
LOCATION:PA
END:VEVENT
