BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Network Factory XII: Art & Entrepreneurship
DTSTART:20260521T213000Z
DTEND:20260521T223000Z
DTSTAMP:20260412T180152Z
UID:af60a47e-3699-11f1-887f-fef293e589ee
DESCRIPTION:10001734-1779384600-1779391800@www.warhol.org\nJoin The Warhol 
 Academy for an insightful discussion on becoming an entrepreneur in the ar
 ts! Explore the struggles and hacks of working for yourself in a lane of o
 ne’s own choosing. Learn how these professionals have built their own co
 mpany\, brand\, following\, and/or loyal customer base. Our panelists will
  discuss their POV on establishing a business\, marketing\, and the lesser
  seen labor of accounting\, finance and creating a digital presence. Artis
 ts\, entrepreneurs and anyone who leans towards a creative persuasion will
  benefit from the topics and tasks covered with Pittsburgh’s own creativ
 e business owners. You’ll leave with actionable steps to funnel your ide
 as into a sustainable career.  \nSpecial guest panelists: \n\nMorgan Over
 ton\, artist\, founder & owner of Morgan Overton Art Gallery\nCandace Jane
  Opper\, finance & operations director of Casey Droege Cultural Production
 s and owner of Fringe Benefits Bookkeeping\nElisa Cevallos\, photographer 
 & owner of South Breeze Photography\nRyan McLennan\, owner of Bottom Feede
 r Books\nRich Cefalo\, Clearview AVP of business lending & services\nRian-
 Louis (moderator)\, host of Rian Out Loud podcast\n\nA Q&A will follow the
  panel discussion along with an hour of mingling with the audience. \nThe 
 Warhol Academy operates education and opportunity programming with a focus
  on creative workforce growth and expansion guided by a collaborative\, Wa
 rholian perspective. \nSpace is limited and registration is required. \n\n
 Doors open at 5 p.m.
LOCATION:The Warhol theater\, 117 Sandusky Street\, Pittsburgh\, PA\, 15212
 \, United States
END:VEVENT
