UID:ce3e991e-376b-11f1-839d-aec7dd95e29b
DESCRIPTION:https://pittsburghwinery.com/event/thecause-steel-your-face-w-s
 pecial-guest-randy-baumann/\n\n\nThe Original Pittsburgh Winery Presents: 
 theCAUSE ‘Steel Your Face’ recreating a classic PGH Dead show w/ speci
 al guest Randy Baumann on keys!\nDoors at 7PM | Show at 8PM | 21 and over\
 n$15.00 Advance // $20.00 Day of show [+Tax/Fees]\n*This is a general admi
 ssion event. There is plenty of seating available. But it is first come\, 
 first serve and is therefore not guaranteed. \nAbout theCAUSE:WEBSITE | F
 ACEBOOK | INSTAGRAM | LISTEN\ntheCAUSE is a band consisting of 5 Pittsburg
 h musicians who have all been around the proverbial block. Playing tunes f
 rom Grateful Dead\, Phish\, The Beatles\, Bob Dylan and MORE\, including s
 ome very tasty originals\, theCAUSE packs a punch while still paying close
  attention to the delicate touch. The players are Eric “Pappy” Weingra
 d on guitar and vocals (Double Dose\, Reuben’s Painted Mandolin\, The Di
 tch)\, David Tauberg on bass and vocals (Powers Run Band\, Hard to Handle\
 , Cherylann Hawk)\, Mike South on drums (Left for Dead\, Sticky\, West Par
 k Road) and joining us in 2008\, Pittsburgh blues veteran Jill Paone Simmo
 ns brings a whole new dimension to theCAUSE on vocals and continues to roc
 k with us today. Jill also fronts the all-female Dead band Brown Eyed Wome
 n. Michael Cerveris is our permanent part time member playing keyboards (w
 hen he doesn’t have commitments with his other great band the Sun Champs
 ).\n \ntheCAUSE also has had the pleasure in 2012 and 2014 of having guit
 arist Steve Kimock join us on stage and\, for the past several years we’
 ve had Jeff Mattson and Lisa Mackey from Dark Star Orchestra join us for o
 ur annual D-Jam benefit concert.\n\n
LOCATION:Pittsburgh Winery
