BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Holy Gift: A Tribute to Tool w/ special guests Shattered
DTSTART:20260523T010000Z
DTEND:20260523T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20260413T190558Z
UID:ce71c8d4-376b-11f1-839d-aec7dd95e29b
DESCRIPTION:https://pittsburghwinery.com/event/the-holy-gift-a-tribute-to-t
 ool-w-special-guests-shattered/\n\nThe Original PIttsburgh Winery Presents
 : The Holy Gift – A Tribute to Tool w/ special guests Shattered!\n \nDo
 ors at 7PM | Show at 8PM | 21 and over\n$20 Advance / $25 Day of show [+ T
 ax/Fees]\nAbout The Holy Gift:The Holy Gift – A Tribute to Tool is Weste
 rn Pennsylvania’s premier Tool tribute band\, delivering an authentic an
 d electrifying live experience that captures the intensity\, complexity\, 
 and spirit of the legendary prog-metal icons. With masterful musicianship 
 and a deep reverence for the source material\, The Holy Gift recreates Too
 l’s intricate soundscapes\, powerful rhythms\, and mesmerizing performan
 ces\, taking fans on a journey through the band’s most iconic songs. Whe
 ther you’re a die-hard Tool fan or a newcomer to their music\, The Holy 
 Gift brings the energy and precision that make every show an unforgettable
  experience.\n \nAbout Shattered:Shattered is an original hard rock band 
 from Pittsburgh\, PA.  Their music consists of a modern hard rock sound w
 ith heavy hitting riffs and melodic choruses.  Shattered is a 5-piece con
 sisting of Front man – Chris Taylor\, Evan Schlegel on guitar\, Erik Rho
 des on guitar and vocals\, Mike May on bass\, and Kevin Dick on percussion
 .  Shattered has been a prominent band of the rock scene in Pittsburgh an
 d surrounding areas for over a decade\, sharing the stage with bands like 
 Sevendust\, Ten Years\, Hurt\, Cold\, Lacuna Coil\, Bloodywood\, Taproot\,
  Stabbing Westward\, Adelitas Way\, Trapt\, Tantric\, Earshot\, Gemini Syn
 drome\, Smile Empty Soul\, Sick Puppies\, and many others. Shattered has 
 two full length albums. 2012’s Rise of Hypocrisy\, features the fan favo
 rite songs Ridicule and Contagious\, and spans the genre of hard rock from
  the hard-hitting Hypocrite to the melodic ballad The Tie that Binds.  Sh
 attered’s 2017 Album Blackout Sessions boasts even more range while stil
 l holding true to the bands signature hard rock sound.  From the acoustic
  melody of Silhouette to the eerily dark tones of Paralyzed\, to the hard 
 rock punch of Martyr. Fan favorites include Catalyst\, What you Reap\, and
  Reckoning. The Band’s 3rd album release\, an Extended Play entitled 
 “Darker Days” was released in March 2024.  The album’s title track 
 boasts big vocal chants and harmonies that will leave you hooked.  The al
 bum includes five brand new songs\, including the guitar heavy riffs and m
 elodic chorus of “Ghost Town”\, an acoustic ballad – “Coldest Dece
 mber”\, the hard-hitting “Deceit”\, the melodic but driving “World
  Comes Down”\, and title track – “Darker Days”\, along with two si
 ngles previously recorded in 2019\, that were re-remixed and re-mastered (
 The Rising Tide and Am I Godless).Listen to Shattered now on iTunes\, Spot
 ify\, Amazon\, or wherever you stream or download music.\n \n\n
LOCATION:Pittsburgh Winery
END:VEVENT
