BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Donny Benét
DTSTART:20261109T010000Z
DTEND:20261109T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20260414T160526Z
UID:c03589f8-381b-11f1-b3f9-e2b237397ae8
DESCRIPTION:https://thunderbirdmusichall.com/event/donny-ben%c3%a9t/thunder
 bird-cafe-music-hall/pittsburgh-pennsylvania/\n\nDonny Benét\nOTNES\nSund
 ay\, November 8\, 2026Thunderbird Music Hall4053 Butler Street\, Pittsburg
 h\, PADoors @ 7PMShow @ 8PMAGE RESTRICTION: 18+ or with legal guardian\n 
 \n\nhttps://donnybenet.comAfter the success of his 2022 EP Le Piano\, Donn
 y Benét returns with the next chapter in his instrumental series: Il Bass
 o. \nPaying tribute to the bass this time —the foundation\, the glue\, 
 and at times the undeniable boss of music— Il Basso showcases Donny’s 
 passion for the bottom end. \nTo celebrate\, Donny will be taking Il Bass
 o on tour\, performing it live alongside all your favourite Benét classic
 s. Expect an evening overflowing with passion\, heat\, and virtuosity from
  Don and his band. \n\nhttps://www.otnes.band\nOTNES is a Nashville-based
  interdisciplinary artist\, producer\, and multi-instrumentalist. Drawing 
 on a deep love of 60s–90s classics\, experimental sound design\, ambient
  field recordings\, acoustic instruments and analog synths\, she builds a 
 palette that is at once timeless and entirely her own.\nHer debut record\,
  Show Them What’s Inside!\, is a dreamy and cinematic journey through l
 oss\, grief\, and the slow\, necessary work of self-love. The album reflec
 ts OTNES at her most expansive — layering texture\, memory\, and emotion
  into something transformative.\nLive\, OTNES performs alongside tech arti
 st and partner Strangehandle (Jason Brooks) in a fully realized audiovisua
 l experience that weaves together light\, set design\, and performance art
 . \nThis fall\, OTNES joins Donny Benet on tour. She is also at work on n
 ew material born from a self-guided artistic residency in a beloved Frank 
 Lloyd Wright home\, where she spent time exploring the relationship betwee
 n physical space\, sonic process\, and creative practice — capturing fie
 ld recordings and sound explorations that will shape her next chapter. \n
 Ticket Tier Info:General Admission Tickets – Standing Room Only\nThere a
 re no additional entry protocols at this time. Entry requirements are su
 bject to change. By purchasing tickets to this event you agree to abide by
  entry requirements in effect at the time of the event. Check the venue
  website leading up to your event for the latest protocols. Please visit h
 ttps://thunderbirdmusichall.com/safety/ for more information on Covid-19 S
 afety. All sales are final. 
LOCATION:Thunderbird Music Hall
END:VEVENT
