 ve-in-concert/thunderbird-cafe-music-hall/pittsburgh-pennsylvania/\n\nAx a
 nd the Hatchetmen: Live in Concert\nThursday\, July 17\, 2026Thunderbird M
 usic Hall4053 Butler Street\, Pittsburgh\, PADoors @ 7PMShow @ 8PMAGE REST
 RICTION: ALL AGES\n \n\nAx and the Hatchetmen came here to party. The Chi
 cago based indie rock band\, led by singer and guitarist Axel Ellis\, have
  been headlining tours and releasing music since 2018. Rounding out the re
 st of the band are the Hatchetmen- made up of Salvatore Defilippis\, Hunte
 r Olshefke\, Phil Pistone\, Quinn Dolan and Chaandmon Croft. Their debut L
 P “So Much To Tell You” was released in the fall of 2025 on Arista Rec
 ords. They plan on touring and releasing music for the foreseeable future.
  They also will party. \n\nTicket Tier Info:General Admission Tickets –
  Standing Room Only\nThere are no additional entry protocols at this tim
 e. Entry requirements are subject to change. By purchasing tickets to this
