BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BOTTLEROCKET BOOK CLUB w/ JUST HARVEST
DTSTART:20260518T233000Z
DTEND:20260519T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20260428T020231Z
UID:50cfd4ca-42a6-11f1-ac83-6671e396d6cf
DESCRIPTION:https://app.opendate.io/e/bottlerocket-book-club-w-just-harvest
 -may-18-2026-658658\n The OFFICIAL Bottlerocket Book Club makes its return
  with a NEW book\, and a NEW host organization for the month of MAY!  We
 ’ll be meeting in the bar to discuss the BOOK OF THE MONTH\, enjoying so
 me cocktails (or mocktails) and having a great time! This is an inclusive 
 event\, and all are welcome- even if it’s been a while since you’ve re
 ad anything!  Whether you’re a bookworm or just generally seeking commun
 ity and want to join a new club\, this is your chance! This month is for t
 he our Economics aficionado - "BIG HUNGER: THE UNHOLY ALLIANCE BETWEEN COR
 PRATE AMERICA AND ANTI-HUNGER GROUPS" by authour Andrew Fisher. Released 2
 018\, published by MIT Press.  Book blurb:  Food banks and food pantries w
 ere meant to be a stopgap measure\, but manufacturing jobs never came back
 \, recession followed\, and the “emergency food system” became an indu
 stry.  In Big Hunger\, author Andrew Fisher argues that many key anti-hung
 er advocates are missing an essential element of the problem: economic ine
 quality driven by low wages. His research finds that efforts to end hunger
 \, reduce obesity\, and reform farm subsidies are compromised by corporate
  interests.  Encouragingly\, Big Hunger sets forth a vision for what we ca
 n do to put food banks out of business and solve hunger.   About JUST HARV
 EST: was founded in 1986. We work to promote a just system of food access 
 by addressing the root causes of hunger – systemic poverty and inequity 
 – through policy advocacy\, grassroots organizing\, community-based solu
 tions\, and connecting people to benefits. Just Harvest provides SNAP appl
 ication assistance\, free tax preparation\, and farmers market food access
  programs to low-income families in Pittsburgh and beyond. Learn more at j
 ustharvest.org  Promoting Book Store - White Whale 
LOCATION:Bottlerocket Social Hall
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kyle Smith
