BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sean Chambers
DTSTART:20260623T233000Z
DTEND:20260624T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20260428T190204Z
UID:bf243d92-4334-11f1-9aaa-8ee33bc93479
DESCRIPTION:https://tickets.citywinery.com/event/sean-chambers-dgwa1e\nCity
  Winery Pittsburgh presents Sean Chambers live on Tuesday\, June 23rd\, at
  7:30 PM(opens in a new tab)!"Guitarist Chambers achieves the distinctly A
 merican blues/soul/country/rock sound that the Stones used to aspire to lo
 ng ago." - Jerry Shriver\, USA TODAY Florida Music Hall of Fame Inductee S
 ean Chambers began his professional career back in 1998 when he toured wit
 h the legendary Chicago blues guitarist Hubert Sumlin as his guitar player
  and band leader\, while developing his own distinctive style along the wa
 y. During Sean's tenure with Mr. Sumlin\, Britain’s own Guitarist magazi
 ne named Chambers as “One of the top 50 blues guitarists of the last cen
 tury.” Chambers has released nine albums to date. His 2009 breakout\, Te
 n Til Midnight\, garnered rave reviews\, appeared on the Living Blues char
 t for three consecutive months\, and received significant airplay on Siriu
 s/XM Radio blues channel as a “Pick to Click” and "The House of Blues 
 Radio Hour" as a “Blues Breaker". It received steady airplay in 45 state
 s around the U.S\, as well as many markets overseas. “Sean Chambers play
 s with an inner fire that seems to only burn hotter the deeper you get int
 o the disc. "Ten Til Midnight" is bound to perk up some ears!” - Mark Ur
 icheck\, LIVING BLUES MAGAZINE (Dec 28\, 2009) “Chambers' guitar style i
 s electrifying on his new CD Ten Till Midnight! He is absolutely amazing o
 n guitar and equally experienced on vocals.” - Rick Davis\, CROSSROADS B
 LUES SOCIETY OF NORTHERN ILLINOIS (Nov 16\, 2009) Moving on\, Chambers' 8t
 h album entitled "That's What I'm Talkin About" is a tribute to his mentor
 \, the late great Hubert Sumlin. The album reached the Top Ten on the Bill
 board Blues Charts and received great accolades and rave reviews. “It is
  great to see an unsung guitar legend the caliber of Hubert Sumlin\, who p
 layed with Muddy Waters and Howlin’ Wolf\, being celebrated by a young a
 rtist Sean Chambers. Hubert was bending strings before anyone! - Paul Rodg
 ers\, (Bad Company) “Not just the blues rock album of the year\, or inde
 ed the decade. Sean Chambers has produced the blues rock album of the CENT
 URY!! "THAT’S WHAT I'M TALKIN ABOUT" - Gerry Casey\, (Making A Scene) In
  2022\, following the passing of Savoy Brown founder Kim Simmonds—and wi
 th his blessing—Chambers teamed up with the Savoy Brown rhythm section\,
  featuring Pat De Salvo on bass and Garnet Grimm on drums. Being that Savo
 y Brown and Chambers are on the same record label together\, Quarto Valley
  Records\, also home to such greats as Paul Rodgers\, Edgar Winter and mor
 e\, this change made sense and felt right to all three musicians.On Februa
 ry 28th\, 2025 the trio released a live album\, Chambers' 9th. It was reco
 rded at the prestigious "Daryl's House Club". It features 12 blistering an
 d soulful tracks. The album also reached Top Ten on the Billboard Blues Ch
 arts and received great accolades and rave reviews around the globe. “Se
 an Chambers delivers a blistering set on his Live album recorded at Daryl'
 s House Club\, a live album that captures the raw intensity and precision 
 of a seasoned blues-rock road warrior at the top of his game. This isn't j
 ust a live album\; it's a masterclass in how to bring fire to the stage wi
 thout ever losing the feel.” - Colin Campbell\, Blues Matters (Apr 10\, 
 2025) “This is a very cool record! Since we still have a CD player in ou
 r car\, it has had a permanent home there since we got ours! Terrific set 
 list!! Sean Chambers is great and so (of course) is his rhythm section! Gl
 ad to see Sean Chambers\, Pat DeSalvo & Garnet Grimm (the Savoy Brown Rhyt
 hm section) out there playing & recording. Good job! Great record!” -Rog
 er Earl\, (Foghat) Sean Chambers is a refreshingly humble artist\, he is t
 ruly a tour de force with his blazing guitar pyrotechnics\, razor clean fr
 etwork and a great passion for the material he writes and plays…A musici
 an's musician who is loved and respected by all in the industry! “He has
  fire in his hands and a global vision of Blues and Blues Rock\, which mak
 es him one of the best current representatives of the genre! Simply except
 ional!” - François Alaouret\, Rock'N Force (Mar 05\, 2025) -Discography
 : Strong Temptation / Vestige Records Humble Spirits / Rockview Records Te
 n Til Midnight / Blue Heat Records Live from the Long Island Warehouse / B
 lue Heat Records The Rock House Sessions / Blue Heat Records Trouble & Whi
 skey / Quarto Valley Records Welcome To My Blues / Quarto Valley Records T
 hat's What I'm Talkin About / Quarto Valley Records Guest appearance on Ab
 out Them Shoes / Hubert Sumlin / Tone Cool RecordsDine At Your Show(opens 
 in a new tab)🍽️  We provide food and beverage service directly to you
 r table in the venue. Or\, for an expanded menu and more relaxed experienc
 e\, arrive early and enjoy a meal in our restaurant before the show. When 
 dining in the restaurant\, reservations are encouraged and can be made via
  Resy starting one month before the show. View Our Concert Dining Menu.(op
 ens in a new tab)Wine At Your Table(opens in a new tab)Reserve your prefer
 red wine by filling out this form(opens in a new tab) and have a bottle wa
 iting at your table when you arrive at your show. No more waiting for your
  first drink! We will save your wine preference and have a bottle at your 
 table for all future shows. When you want to change your wine\, come back 
 to this form and update your preference.2-item Per Person Minimum🎶  Kin
 dly note there is a 2-item per person food & beverage minimum in the conce
 rt venue. Food and beverages ordered in the restaurant also count towards 
 the minimum.(opens in a new tab)Become a Vinofile Member(opens in a new ta
 b)🍷  Members get 48 hour early access to new shows\, pay no ticket fees
 \, and earn points to exchange for complimentary tickets. Vinofile Plus me
 mbers also receive many wine benefits. Add a membership to your cart durin
 g checkout to start saving now. Already a member? Make sure you are signed
  in to access your benefits. Become a Vinofile Member and enjoy the benefi
 ts today.(opens in a new tab)(opens in a new tab)(opens in a new tab)DateJ
 un23Doors Open6:00 PMLocationCity Winery Pittsburgh1627 Smallman StreetPit
