BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Omar Hakim and Rachel Z: Generations Deconstructed Tour\, Featuring
  the Rock ‘N’ Roll Collective
DTSTART:20260703T233000Z
DTEND:20260704T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20260428T190205Z
UID:bf2f81b6-4334-11f1-9aaa-8ee33bc93479
DESCRIPTION:https://tickets.citywinery.com/event/omar-hakim-and-rachel-z-ge
 nerations-deconstructe-atbp9n\nCity Winery Pittsburgh presents Omar Hakim 
 and Rachel Z: Generations Deconstructed Tour\, Featuring the Rock ‘N’ 
 Roll Collective live on Friday\, July 3rd\, at 7:30 PM(opens in a new tab)
 !Featuring legendary drummer Omar Hakim (Weather Report\, Bowie\, Sting\, 
 Madonna) Rachel Z (Peter Gabriel\, Steps Ahead\, Wayne Shorter) Ozmosys\, 
 and the Rock N’ Roll Collective\, The Generations Deconstructed Tour is 
 a dynamic\, multi-faceted live music experience that bridges generations a
 nd genres. The show features the Rock N’Roll Collective (ages 13-18) per
 forming iconic classic tunes in their original\, high-energy form\, while 
 Ozmosys reimagines those same songs through a bold and sophisticated jazz 
 lens. Audiences will hear familiar hits transformed in real time—moving 
 from faithful renditions to inventive\, genre-bending interpretations—sh
 owcasing the deep musicality\, creativity\, and interplay between these ex
 ceptional artists. This unique concert experience celebrates both the time
 lessness of great music and the limitless possibilities of reinterpretatio
 n. Two bands - Two completely different takes - One unforgettable night. T
 his isn’t just a show—it’s a musical conversation across generations
 \, styles\, and imagination. Feel the originals. Experience the transforma
 tion. The Rock N’ Roll Collective is a powerhouse group of exceptionally
  talented young musicians between the ages of 13 and 18. Designed for stud
 ents who have outgrown traditional music education programs like School of
  Rock\, the Collective offers a professional-level environment where emerg
 ing artists can develop their craft and gain real-world performance experi
 ence. OMAR HAKIM\, Drummer\, began playing at age five. By ten he was perf
 orming publicly with his father Hasan Hakim\, a trombone veteran of the Du
 ke Ellington and Count Basie bands. Omar has toured or recorded with count
 less music industry legends\, including Miles Davis\, Wayne Shorter\, Joe 
 Zawinul\, David Bowie\, Dire Straits\, Michael Jackson\, Chaka Khan\, Mado
 nna\, Daft Punk\, Sting\, George Benson\, Lionel Richie\, Anita Baker\, He
 rbie Hancock\, Queen Latifah\, Celine Dion\, D’Angelo\, as well as his e
 xcellent solo albums and band projects including with his keyboards-virtuo
 so wife Rachel Z. Omar is chair of Berklee’s Percussion Department. RACH
 EL Z\, keyboardist\, synthesist. Grammy-winning\, Grammy-nominated with a 
 long history of award-winning performances in the worlds of jazz and rock.
  Rachel has released 13 albums as bandleader and been a crucial part of co
 untless tours and recordings including Steps Ahead\, Vertú\, the Omar Hak
 im Experience\, OZmosys\, Wayne Shorter\, Stanley Clarke\, Marcus Miller\,
  Terri Lyne Carrington\, Al Di Meola\, and Regina Carter. Her years of tou
 ring with Peter Gabriel include appearances in his live films Growing Up L
 ive & Still Growing Up Live. She is Professor of Jazz\, Contemporary Music
  Studies and Electronic Music\, variously at New School University NYC\, M
 ontclair State University and Cali School of the Arts. The Rock N’ Roll 
 Collective is a powerhouse group of exceptionally talented young musicians
  between the ages of 13 and 18. Designed for students who have outgrown tr
 aditional music education programs like School of Rock\, the Collective of
 fers a professional-level environment where emerging artists can develop t
 heir craft and gain real-world performance experience. Founded by veteran 
 audio engineer and producer Jeremy Gerard\, the Collective is music-direct
 ed by renowned industry professionals Rachel Z Hakim\, Omar Hakim\, Mike P
 ellegrino\, and Ben Moyer. Collective members have performed on tour acros
 s the US & Europe. In 2025\, Collective members completed US & European to
 urs with Frank Zappa alumni and embarked on a separate European tour with 
 Gibby Haynes of the Butthole Surfers. The Rock N’ Roll Collective is not
  just a band — it's a launchpad for the next generation of world-class m
 usicians.Dine At Your Show(opens in a new tab)🍽️  We provide food and
  beverage service directly to your table in the venue. Or\, for an expande
 d menu and more relaxed experience\, arrive early and enjoy a meal in our 
 restaurant before the show. When dining in the restaurant\, reservations a
