BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Idiosympathy X Posterchild
DTSTART:20260620T000000Z
DTEND:20260620T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260505T172551Z
UID:76db9abc-48a7-11f1-9b3c-e20d3611efd6
DESCRIPTION:https://mrsmalls.com/events/idiosympathy-x-posterchild/\nAsleep
  in your heart for 19 years\, Idiosympathy is awakening in 2026 for two bi
 g reunion concerts: First at Mr. Smalls Funhouse Friday June 19th and at B
 ig Rail Brewing June 20th (tickets here on this page).\nWhen the band said
  goodbye in 2007\, they left behind two self-produced releases that stood 
 the test of time: The 2007 full length Overachiever In Love\, and the 2005
  EP We Have Lost Our Self Control. Both were re-released on all the major 
 streaming services in 2025\, to the surprise and delight of a dormant fan 
 base.\nBoth reunion concerts promise to revive what stood out about Idiosy
 mpathy shows: thick textures\, driving rhythms\, memorable melodies\, intr
 icate arrangements\, and soaring vocals... with both old and new tunes and
  some brand new twists. The four original members will be teaming up with 
 two new players\, John DeCola and Brian Schultz\, to deliver the full inst
 rumentation from the albums and more.The band is also pleased to announce 
 a limited\, 100 copy vinyl run of Overachiever In Love. The LP will be ava
 ilable for pre-order through the ticket page here for the Big Rail show\, 
 and will be available for sale at both shows (if they don't sell out from 
 pre-orders).Idiosympathy is teaming up with new friends Posterchild and Ga
 ry Musisko.This Event Is All AgesAll Sales Are Final.
LOCATION:The Funhouse at Mr. Smalls
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:David Ramirez
DTSTART:20260719T000000Z
DTEND:20260719T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260505T172551Z
UID:76de99f6-48a7-11f1-9b3c-e20d3611efd6
DESCRIPTION:https://mrsmalls.com/events/david-ramirez/\nDavid Ramirez is an
  American Americana singer-songwriter based in Austin\, Texas. Most of Ram
 irez music contain themes of sorrow\, moral tribulation\, love\, and redem
 ption. He is known for his deep and reverberant baritone voice. In 2020\, 
 he was awarded Songwriter of the Year by The Austin Chronicle.This Event I
 s All AgesAll Sales Are Final.
LOCATION:The Funhouse at Mr. Smalls
END:VEVENT
