BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sam Barber
DTSTART:20260923T000000Z
DTEND:20260923T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260505T172552Z
UID:772f9efa-48a7-11f1-9b3c-e20d3611efd6
DESCRIPTION:https://www.stagepittsburgh.com/events/sam-barber-22-september-
 2026/\nPittsburgh\, rumor has it that you've been craving an evening jam-p
 acked with the most talked-about country tunes around\, and that's exactly
  what you'll be getting this fall! \nSo gear up - find those those long-lo
 st boots\, buff those oversized belt buckles\, dust off the Stetson\, and 
 yank out your blue jeans from wherever you've been hiding it\, and get rea
 dy for an evening stuffed to the brim with unforgettable melodies that you
 'll take to the grave with you\, and an off-the-charts vibe that will blow
  you away!\nSam Barber has just dropped the news of a mammoth North Americ
 an tour that will see that legendary brand of country at all the iconic ve
 nues - and you're on their radar! The American Route Tour is bringing the 
 viral sensation behind "Straight and Narrow" and hits like "Indigo" and "R
 estless Mind" to cities across the US and Mexico\, and Pittsburgh made the
  cut!\nSpot on Pittsburgh\, Sam Barber is coming to the Stage AE on Tuesda
 y 22nd September 2026 with the biggest country show of the year! The risin
 g country star will be performing tracks from his latest album "Broken Vie
 w" at the outdoor amphitheater on Pittsburgh's North Shore\, right next to
  Acrisure Stadium.\nThe best news is that it won't even cost you an arm an
 d a leg\, since ticket prices are starting from as low as $72! However\, y
 ou'll have to hurry\, because the empty seats are filling up faster than a
  cowboy chasing an outlaw!\nClick on the 'Get Tickets' link now to be redi
 rected to get yours in hand quickly and efficiently!
LOCATION:Stage AE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dandy Andy: Warhol’s Queer History
DTSTART:20270227T200000Z
DTEND:20270227T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260505T172552Z
UID:7732ac80-48a7-11f1-9b3c-e20d3611efd6
DESCRIPTION:10000099-1803740400-1803747600@www.warhol.org\nJoin artist educ
 ators for Dandy Andy\, a monthly tour that focuses on Warhol’s queer his
 tory. While his sexuality is frequently suppressed or debated\, Warhol was
  a gay man who had several partners throughout his life. Warhol’s boyfri
 ends\, including Edward Wallowitch\, John Giorno\, and Jed Johnson\, were 
 also his colleagues and collaborators\, helping to shape and define his ca
 reer as an artist. This tour traces Warhol’s romantic relationships and 
 queer identity against the backdrop of the historical gay rights movement 
 in the United States. Tours meet on the museum’s seventh floor.
LOCATION:The Andy Warhol Museum\, 117 Sandusky Street\, Pittsburgh\, PA\, 1
 5212\, United States
END:VEVENT
