 rbird-cafe-music-hall/pittsburgh-pennsylvania/\n\nBeatles vs. DeadEleanor 
 Walrus and Fungus 35 Years of FungusTerry’s 70th BirthdaySaturday\, Aug
 ust 22\, 2026Thunderbird Music Hall4053 Butler Street\, Pittsburgh\, PA 15
 201Doors @ 7PMShow @ 8PMAGE RESTRICTION: 21+\nPlease join us as we celebra
 te the 35th anniversary of Fungus! That’s right\, for 35 years Fungus ha
 s been presenting Grateful Dead inspired performances in western Pennsylva
 nia that pay homage to the everlasting legacy of Jerry Garcia. They specia
 lize in recreating the festive atmosphere that followed the Dead to each o
 f their concerts. We’ll also be celebrating Terry’s 70th birthday. So 
 come on out\, Fungus always brings the party. \n \nEleanor Walrus formed
  out of a mutual love for the greatest repertoire in the world. Today they
  are Pittsburgh’s premiere psychedelic Beatles revue. Each show pays tri
 bute to the vast brilliance and timelessness of the Fab Four’s compositi
 ons\, often presenting more than fifty of your favorite songs in one eveni
 ng. Please join us\, and re-imagine the greatest generation of songwriting
 \, together with Eleanor Walrus.\nTogether these two titans of Pittsburgh
 ’s jamband scene present an evening that is guaranteed to delight fans o
 f either band.\nTicket Tier Info:General Admission Tickets – Standing Ro
 om Only\nThere are no additional entry protocols at this time. Entry req
