BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kash&#8217\;d Out &#8211\; Good Karma Summer Tour 2026
DTSTART:20260822T000000Z
DTEND:20260822T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260519T150522Z
UID:2881a562-5394-11f1-b83e-4e0f19fff5ec
DESCRIPTION:https://thunderbirdmusichall.com/event/kashd-out-good-karma-sum
 mer-tour-2026/thunderbird-cafe-music-hall/pittsburgh-pennsylvania/\n\n\nKa
 sh’d Out – Good Karma Summer Tour 2026\nW/ RDGLDGRN\nFriday\, August 2
 1\, 2026Thunderbird Music Hall4053 Butler Street\, Pittsburgh\, PA Doors 
 @ 7PMShow @ 8PMAGE RESTRICTION: 21+https://www.kashdout.com\nFlorida based
  Reggae/Rock band Kash’d Out have been hustlin’ hard since the beginni
 ng. After founders Greg Shields (lead vocals) and Jackson Hauserman (guita
 r) met in a studio session\, it wasn’t long before Kash’d Out’s clev
 er lyrics and tasteful guitar riffs were complimented by the unique bass l
 ines of Joey Brohawn\, and rhythmic precision of drummer Marshall Hearne.
  \nKash’d Out quickly caught the attention of Hawaiian favorites Pepper
 \, who signed the band to their label LAW Records and released “The Hook
 up” – Kash’d Out’s first full-length album. Prior to its release\,
  KO hit the road with Pepper and Less Than Jake\, which helped the album c
 limb the Billboard Reggae Charts. Since then\, Kash’d Out has been no st
 ranger to the open road. Storming the nation with an abundance of full U.S
 . tours under their belt\, KO has supported genre heavyweights such as Col
 lie Buddz\, The Expendables\, Iration and headlined multiple US tours of t
 heir own. The band’s drive and passion has landed them in the line up of
  Reggae’s most esteemed festivals such as Reggae Rise Up Florida/Utah/Ma
 ryland\, California Roots\, Dry Diggings and One Love. \nKash’d Out’s
  most recent album\, “Butter” displays their diversity and mission int
 o their own music path. The band has remained steadfast to originality\, y
 et continues to evolve\, revealing different sides to their sound. \nKash
 ’d Out is excited to continue touring the country with a high-energy sho
 w and a genuine love for sharing the music they’ve made with anyone and 
 everyone! Catch them in a town near you by visiting www.kashdout.com/tour-
 dates\nhttps://www.rdgldgrn.com\nRDGLDGRN (pronounced “Red Gold Green”
 ) is a genre-bending trio from Reston\, Virginia\, just outside Washington
 \, D.C.\, blending go-go\, reggae\, rock\, hip-hop\, and alternative music
  into a sound entirely their own. Since forming in 2011\, the band has tou
 red nationally\, appeared on NPR Tiny Desk and Jimmy Kimmel Live!\, and bu
 ilt a loyal following through their independent spirit and high-energy liv
 e shows.\nKnown for collaborations with Dave Grohl and Pharrell Williams\,
  RDGLDGRN has had music featured in The Sims\, Madden NFL\, film\, televis
 ion\, and major ad campaigns. Fresh off a nationwide tour\, the band conti
 nues their latest chapter with The Gold Album\, pushing their sound into n
 ew territory while staying rooted in the creativity and energy that made t
 hem stand out in the first place.Ticket Tier Info:General Admission Ticket
 s – Standing Room Only\n\nFor accessible seating accommodations\, please
  send an email in advance to contact@thunderbirdmusichall.com after ticket
  purchase. All sales are final. 
LOCATION:Thunderbird Music Hall
END:VEVENT
