BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dandy Andy: Warhol’s Queer History
DTSTART:20260613T190000Z
DTEND:20260613T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260526T170548Z
UID:247c816c-5925-11f1-ab40-6a4e58fe1824
DESCRIPTION:10002185-1781362800-1781370000@www.warhol.org\nJoin artist educ
 ators for Dandy Andy\, a monthly tour that focuses on Warhol’s queer his
 tory. While his sexuality is frequently suppressed or debated\, Warhol was
  a gay man who had several partners throughout his life. Warhol’s boyfri
 ends\, including Edward Wallowitch\, John Giorno\, and Jed Johnson\, were 
 also his colleagues and collaborators\, helping to shape and define his ca
 reer as an artist. This tour traces Warhol’s romantic relationships and 
 queer identity against the backdrop of the historical gay rights movement 
 in the United States. Tours meet on the museum’s seventh floor.
LOCATION:The Andy Warhol Museum\, 117 Sandusky Street\, Pittsburgh\, PA\, 1
 5212\, United States
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Etta Cox: Jazz Favorites Brunch
DTSTART:20260627T160000Z
DTEND:20260627T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20260526T190145Z
UID:56e5a93e-5935-11f1-ab40-6a4e58fe1824
DESCRIPTION:https://tickets.citywinery.com/event/etta-cox-jazz-favorites-br
 unch-9d6w99\nCity Winery Pittsburgh presents Etta Cox: Jazz Favorites Brun
 ch on Saturday June 27th\, at 12:00 PM!Etta Cox is one of Pittsburgh’s m
 ost celebrated jazz vocalists and entertainers. Originally from St. Joseph
 \, Missouri\, Cox has spent decades performing across the tri-state area a
 nd beyond\, earning widespread acclaim for her commanding voice and stage 
 presence. She has been voted “Best Jazz Vocalist” in Pittsburgh for ei
 ght consecutive years and has received numerous accolades\, including the 
 Harry Schwalb Award for Excellence in the Arts\, the YWCA Arts and Letters
  Award\, and Talk Magazine’s Walt Harper All That Jazz Award.On Broadway
 \, Cox appeared in I Love My Wife with Lawrence-Hilton Jacobs and The 1940
 ’s Radio Hour with Dee Dee Bridgewater. She starred in Showtime’s The 
 Me Nobody Knows and is well known locally for standout roles in production
 s like Ma Rainey’s Black Bottom at Pittsburgh Public Theater and From th
 e Mississippi Delta\, Spunk\, Avenue X\, and Crowns at City Theatre. She a
 lso starred in Beehive and Two Gentlemen of Verona\, leaving a lasting imp
 ression on Pittsburgh’s theatrical scene.Cox's film credits include Sile
 nt Witness\, Lady Beware\, Criminal Justice\, Bump in the Night\, The Ceme
 tery Club\, Warrior\, and The Next Three Days. She also co-hosted the popu
 lar television talk show CityLife for eight years.Her longtime musical par
 tnership with jazz trombonist Al Dowe led to performances across Pittsburg
 h\, New York\, Atlantic City\, and Key West. Together\, they co-owned two 
 renowned Pittsburgh jazz clubs\, including the celebrated Dowe’s on 9th.
  The duo opened for legends such as Ray Charles\, Doc Severinson\, Debbie 
 Reynolds\, Danny Glover\, and Mavis Staples\, and performed with the Pitts
 burgh Ballet Theatre in Smokin’ Roses at the Byham Theater and Wolf Trap
 .Beyond the spotlight\, Cox is a dedicated educator. She teaches voice and
  solfeggio at Pittsburgh CAPA (Creative and Performing Arts High School) a
 nd offers private lessons at the Karen Prunzik Broadway Dance Studio. A pr
 oud member of Allegheny Center Alliance Church\, Cox credits her faith as 
 the foundation of her success\, believing\, “In all things\, give God th
 e glory.”À la carte brunch is not included in the ticket price and is a
  separate charge.Dine At Your Show(opens in a new tab)🍽️  We provide 
 food and beverage service directly to your table in the venue. Or\, for an
  expanded menu and more relaxed experience\, arrive early and enjoy a meal
  in our restaurant before the show. When dining in the restaurant\, reserv
 ations are encouraged and can be made via Resy starting one month before t
 he show. View Our Concert Dining Menu.(opens in a new tab)Wine At Your Tab
 le(opens in a new tab)Reserve your preferred wine by filling out this form
 (opens in a new tab) and have a bottle waiting at your table when you arri
 ve at your show. No more waiting for your first drink! We will save your w
 ine preference and have a bottle at your table for all future shows. When 
 you want to change your wine\, come back to this form and update your pref
 erence.2-item Per Person Encouraged(opens in a new tab)🎶  While we do n
 ot require a two-item food or beverage minimum\, we strongly encourage it.
  Most ticket revenue goes directly to the artist and production costs\, so
  food and drink purchases help support the staff\, service\, and atmospher
 e that make these intimate shows possible.The good news: we think you’ll
  love the food and wine just as much as the show.Become a Vinofile Member(
 opens in a new tab)🍷  Members get 48 hour early access to new shows\, p
 ay no ticket fees\, and earn points to exchange for complimentary tickets.
  Vinofile Plus members also receive many wine benefits. Add a membership t
