BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kneafsey
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260709T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260709T200000
DTSTAMP:20260527T040140Z
UID:c4045aa6-5980-11f1-ab40-6a4e58fe1824
DESCRIPTION:https://www.poetrymillvale.com/event/kneafsey/\nKneafsey is the
  solo project of Jimmy Drenovsky\, who’s \nbeen the frontman of Chicago
 ’s Motel Breakfast since 2016 \nbut is now stepping out with a project a
 ll his own. Jimmy has been writing music for most of his \nlife – he’s
  a dedicated student of songwriting who’s constantly processing and obse
 rving the \nworld around him. His debut album as Kneafsey is a carefully c
 onstructed batch of songs\, \nwritten throughout his 20’s and recorded p
 atiently over three years to tape by Jimmy and \nproducer Will Hansen (of 
 Milwaukee’s “Old Pup”). \nAfter Jimmy and Will completed the trackin
 g\, they brought in Ziyad Asrar (of Chicago band \nWhitney) to complete th
 e mix and Ian Farmer (of Philly legends Modern Baseball and Slaughter \nBe
 ach\, Dog) to master. \nThe resulting album\, Sad Boy Blues\, is an introd
 uction that invites the listener into private \nconversations and gut-wren
 ching meditations on love\, loss\, and friendship. It’s inviting\, \nvul
 nerable\, earnest\, and contains a surprising self-awareness\, closing wit
 h levity by way of the \ntitle track\, and hinting at a sense of humor inf
 luenced by the likes of John Prine and Adrianne \nLenker.
LOCATION:Poetry Lounge
END:VEVENT
