BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Neon Vanadium – Tuning In
DTSTART:20260726T000000Z
DTEND:20260726T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260530T210201Z
UID:ce160ebc-5c6a-11f1-84e8-8610f2635b81
DESCRIPTION:https://mrsmalls.com/events/neon-vanadium/\nNeon Vanadium is a 
 deeply ambitious\, almost cinematic Pittsburgh rock band with a focus on s
 torytelling\, atmosphere\, and emotional weight. Unafraid to be unconventi
 onal\, experimental\, or heavy. The group was formed in late 2020 by broth
 ers Cameron and Logan Balkovec. Jake Maxeiner tagged along closer to the e
 nd of that year\, and for a long time Neon Vanadium was known as the trio.
  That changed in early 2022 as bassist Matt Kustra joined the lineup\, cha
 nging the trajectory of Neon Vanadium for good. With a deeply personal deb
 ut album\, Neon Vanadium plans to deliver a very immersive show experience
  that begs to be remembered.This Event Is All AgesAll Sales Are Final.
LOCATION:The Funhouse at Mr. Smalls
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dandy Andy: Warhol’s Queer History
DTSTART:20280129T200000Z
DTEND:20280129T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260531T010558Z
UID:e26e3f84-5c8c-11f1-84e8-8610f2635b81
DESCRIPTION:10000110-1832770800-1832778000@www.warhol.org\nJoin artist educ
 ators for Dandy Andy\, a monthly tour that focuses on Warhol’s queer his
 tory. While his sexuality is frequently suppressed or debated\, Warhol was
  a gay man who had several partners throughout his life. Warhol’s boyfri
 ends\, including Edward Wallowitch\, John Giorno\, and Jed Johnson\, were 
 also his colleagues and collaborators\, helping to shape and define his ca
 reer as an artist. This tour traces Warhol’s romantic relationships and 
 queer identity against the backdrop of the historical gay rights movement 
 in the United States. Tours meet on the museum’s seventh floor.
LOCATION:The Andy Warhol Museum\, 117 Sandusky Street\, Pittsburgh\, PA\, 1
 5212\, United States
END:VEVENT
