BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:John Borra // Lorraine Leckie
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260722T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260722T200000
DTSTAMP:20260601T090158Z
UID:8b8ab3fc-5d98-11f1-84e8-8610f2635b81
DESCRIPTION:https://www.poetrymillvale.com/event/john-borra-lorraine-leckie
 /\nJohn Borra & Lorraine Leckie have shared numerous stages in New York an
 d Ontario and now\nlook forward to bringing their show to Pennsylvania and
  Ohio this July 2026. The are both\nseasoned performers and both have thei
 r own disAncAve style and sound but when paired on\nthe same bill it makes
  for a show that is greater than the sum of its parts. \nJohn Borra is a r
 espected figure in Toronto’s music scene\, blending punk’s raw energy 
 with the\nstorytelling tradiAons of folk\, country\, and Americana. From h
 is early days in the 1980s\nunderground scene to his solo career\, Borra h
 as built a reputaAon for authenAcity and passion\,\nearning criAcal acclai
 m with albums like Blue Wine and Casse\,es In Common. His latest project\,
 \nLast Dance at the E Room\, is a deeply personal tribute to his late ment
 or\, Peter J. Moore\, and the\ncreaAve space that played a pivotal role in
  his musical journey. \nLorraine Leckie is a Singer-songwriter and poet wh
 o was born on a horse in Northern Ontario\nand raised on Neil Young’s mu
 sic. In the ’70s\, she embraced punk\, married Steve Leckie of the\nVile
 tones and became a makeup artist. Leckie worked in the fashion industry an
 d with\ncelebrities such as Paul McCartney and Heidi Klum. After a decade 
 in Europe\, she settled in New\nYork. At 37\, she picked up a guitar and b
 egan performing at venues like Bowery Ballroom and\nMercury Lounge. She’
 s often joined by her band: Hugh Pool\, Pavel Cingl\, Keith Robinson\,\nCh
 arles DeChants and Zoe Friedman. Lorraine currently lives in Greenpoint Br
 ooklyn with her\nhusband\, Billy Leroy and a diabolical Irish terrier call
 ed Broghan. Her latest record is Goddamn\nOuter Space.
LOCATION:Poetry Lounge
END:VEVENT
