UID:5b2dd27a-5e9c-11f1-84e8-8610f2635b81
DESCRIPTION:https://thunderbirdmusichall.com/event/all-your-friends-the-ind
 ie-dance-party-2/thunderbird-cafe-music-hall/pittsburgh-pennsylvania/\n\nA
 ll Your Friends – The Indie Dance Party\n \nFriday\, July 17\, 2026Thun
 derbird Music Hall4053 Butler Street\, Pittsburgh\, PADoors @ 8:00PMShow @
  8:30PMAGE RESTRICTION: 18+\n \nhttps://www.allyourfriendsindie.com/\nAn 
 indie dance party for the ones who still romanticize a scratched iPod\, Am
 erican Spirits\, and a blurry night scored by Bloc Party and Crystal Castl
 es. All Your Friends is your basement-floor flashback to the bloghouse\, 
 post-punk revival\, and early Tumblr era — when the jeans were tight\, t
 he eyeliner was smudged\, and every night felt like a house show turned af
 terparty. Expect to move to LCD Soundsystem\, The Rapture\, Foals\, Yeah Y
 eah Yeahs\, TV on the Radio\, and that remix you forgot you loved.The part
 y your Tumblr warned you about\nTicket Tier Info:General Admission Tickets
  – Standing Room Only\nFor accommodated seating arrangements\, email con
 tact@thunderbirdmusichall.com after ticket purchase.All sales are final. 
LOCATION:Thunderbird Music Hall
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Oscar Lindsey X James Eichman
DTSTART:20260729T000000Z
DTEND:20260729T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260602T170528Z
UID:416d2350-5ea5-11f1-84e8-8610f2635b81
DESCRIPTION:https://mrsmalls.com/events/oscar-james/\nOscar Lindsey: Born a
 nd raised in Nashville\, Tennessee to a deeply rooted musical family\, son
 gwriting quickly became Oscar Lindsey's second nature. His self-released 2
 025 LP\, Glitter\, allows influences such as Elliott Smith and Alex G to s
 hine through sonically while providing a wholly original experience to lis
 teners via personal anecdotes and storytelling. Highlight tracks like “F
 orever’s Such A Long Time” and "Ruby" take the intangibles of the comi
 ng-of-age experience and neatly pack them into a single sucker punch. At 2
 4\, Oscar has solidified himself as a songsmith through and through\, maki
 ng introspective folk music feel accessible to the everyday listener\, cre
 ating his own world within the songwriting that draws fans in through its 
 soul-bearing and identifiable qualities.James Eichman: James Eichman is a 
 Nashville born & raised artist whose sound perfectly sits between alt-Amer
 icana & indie rock. Well-respected in the Nashville indie music community\
 , James has toured as a guitarist with Annie DiRusso\, Baby Wave\, Hannah 
 Cole\, Emma Ogier & more while also writing & recording his own debut albu
 m\, St. Catherine Street. James’ songwriting shines through his unique a
 bility to paint vivid characters in each of his songs. His sound\, while r
 eminiscent of The Shins\, Nick Drake\, Jason Molina\, or Alex G\, is a ref
 reshing take on folk rock. James brings listeners in through his poignant 
 storytelling that comes from deeply personal inspirations\, yet feels univ
 ersally relatable. Surrounding the release of St. Catherine Street\, James
  is gearing up to play his project live on tour throughout the summer and 
 fall.This Event Is All AgesAll Sales Are Final.
LOCATION:The Funhouse at Mr. Smalls
END:VEVENT
