BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TITUS ANDRONICUS PERFORMING GREATEST HITS 2008-2015
DTSTART:20260807T000000Z
DTEND:20260807T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260604T040544Z
UID:a9044248-5fca-11f1-89e1-d670261429f1
DESCRIPTION:https://app.opendate.io/e/titus-andronicus-performing-greatest-
 hits-2008-2015-august-06-2026-685861\n  TITUS ANDRONICUS (PERFORMING GREAT
 EST HITS 2008-2015) with support tba  $20 ADV / $25 DOS 7PM DOORS / 8PM MU
 SIC ALL AGES  for fans of... Superchunk\, Japandroids\, Ted Leo\, The Hold
  Steady  BIO: Since emerging onto the scene with their 2008 debut album Th
 e Airing of Grievances and breaking through with 2010's era-defining insta
 nt classic The Monitor\, New Jersey's pride TITUS ANDRONICUS have built an
 d enjoyed a nice little career for themselves : seven studio albums (some 
 justly praised\, some still anticipating their inevitable reappraisal)\, 1
 200+ live concerts across a dozen countries and all 48 continental United 
 States\, a couple few choice credentials to impress the normies (Jimmy Fal
 lon\, Coachella\, rave reviews in Pitchfork/Rolling Stone/etc) and best of
  all\, a modestly-sized but fervently-devoted audience that sticks with th
 em through thick and thin\, revering them as nothing less than The Rock Fa
 n's Rock Band.  Though it has been a rough road at times\, with restless m
 astermind PATRICK STICKLES ushering roughly two dozen “full-time” “o
 fficial” members through the revolving door\, 2025 saw the long-awaited 
 return of prodigal classic-era drummer ERIC HARM to his throne. With 20-ye
 ar veteran guitarist LIAM BETSON in the mix as well\, Titus Andronicus has
  given fans every bit as legitimate a reunion of their “classic lineup
 ” as the likes of Guns 'N' Roses could claim.   The ensemble is rounded 
 out by bassist R.J. GORDON (himself celebrating a record-breaking 10 conse
 cutive years in his current position) and newly(ish) tenured keyboardist 
 “JERSEY” MIKE CARSON – five kings forming like the fiercest of fists
  to smash through the complacency that so commonly hamstrings bands half t
 heir age.   They may be a little softer around the middle and grey at the 
 temples these days\, but Titus Andronicus is rocking as hard as ever\, pla
 ying nothing but the hits\, and always keeping an ear open for an offer th
 ey can't refuse.   “One of the twentieth century's best rock acts” –
  The Atlantic  “If they had broken up on the day that they released 'The
  Monitor\,' they would still be considered one of the most important artis
 ts of this decade.” – Stereogum  “Emotional intensity unrivaled anyw
 here in rock music” – Tiny Mix Tapes  “They're ort of doing a Bruce 
 Springsteen thing but\, like\, more punk\, kind of... uhh I dunno\, you sh
 ould just check 'em out\, they're on Spotify and stuff” – the common p
 erson or casual fan  TOP ALBUMS OF THE 2010's : Pitchfork\, The Needle Dro
 p\, AV Club\, Brooklyn Vegan\, VICE\, etc   
LOCATION:Bottlerocket Social Hall
END:VEVENT
