BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:MK Fullerton / LOWREV
DTSTART:20260711T230000Z
DTEND:20260712T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260605T140137Z
UID:11a594e2-60e7-11f1-b2ff-ca7b99d7d339
DESCRIPTION:https://thunderbirdmusichall.com/event/mk-fullerton-lowrev/thun
 derbird-cafe-music-hall/pittsburgh-pennsylvania/\n\nMK Fullerton / Lowrev\
 nwith Jaxon\, Kid Tigrrr\nSaturday\, July 11\, 2026Thunderbird Music Hall4
 053 Butler Street\, Pittsburgh\, PADoors @ 6PMShow @  7PMAGE RESTRICTION:
  21+\n \nMK Fullerton website\nOriginally from Zelienople and now based i
 n Los Angeles\, singer-songwriter MK Fullerton creates indie rock-pop dra
 wing from alternative and folk influences. Her recent singles are a part 
 of a debut album set for release later this year\, and this hometown perfo
 rmance marks her first Pittsburgh-area show featuring songs from her upco
 ming record.LOWREV website\nWhen Josh Fiedler says that making a solo albu
 m was truly the last thing he ever wanted to do\, trust us: He’s not fr
 onting. While he’s proud of the accomplishments he’s made as a loving
  husband and doting dad\, he’s also made his fair share of heads swivel
  as a founding member/lead guitarist of The Juliana Theory\, the Western
  Pennsylvania post-emo outfit he’s been a founding member of for close
  to 30 years. But it was only last year that he decided to assume his pos
 ition in the spotlight to write and record It’s Hard To Lie To Stranger
 s\, his solo debut for Equal Vision under the sobriquet LOWREV.\nLOWREV w
 ill have an exclusive 7” available only at this album release show. The 
 7” single will have an alternate version of “Its Hard To Lie To Strang
 ers” which is the title track of the new album. The B-Side is a cover of
  the Gin Blossom’s “Till I Hear It From You” \n \nThis 7” is lim
 ited to just 45 copies\, which can be purchased with the ticket\, and be p
 icked up at the LOWREV merch table. Jaxon websiteJaxon is a Los Angeles-b
 ased songwriter whose music lives somewhere between indie rock\, pop\, an
 d alternative. His songs explore love\, loss\, faith\, and the search for 
 meaning\, often through fictional characters and imagined worlds. His las
 t two albums\, Frances Lovegood and De’man Dubois\, are concept albums 
 built around characters he created\, using their stories to explore deepl
 y personal emotions and experiences. Whether performing with a full band o
 r an acoustic guitar\, Jaxon’s goal is simple: make people feel somethi
 ng and remind them they’re not alone. \n\nKid Tigrrr websiteKID TIGRRR
  is the sparkly & ethereal solo project of singer-songwriter Jenna Fournie
 r of the shoegaze/alt-rock band NIIGHTS.Ticket Tier Info:General Admission
  Tickets – Standing Room Only\nFor accessible seating accommodations\, p
 lease send an email in advance to contact@thunderbirdmusichall.com after t
 icket purchase. All sales are final. 
LOCATION:Thunderbird Music Hall
END:VEVENT
