BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fermented Beats
DTSTART:20260829T000000Z
DTEND:20260829T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260611T140150Z
UID:18140140-659e-11f1-a3ea-ae4281c53881
DESCRIPTION:https://thunderbirdmusichall.com/event/fermented-beats/thunderb
 ird-cafe-music-hall/pittsburgh-pennsylvania/\n\n\nFermented Beatsblott\, t
 he Alfomega\nFriday\, August 28\, 2026\nAGE RESTRICTION: 21+\nThunderbird 
 Music Hall4053 Butler StreetPittsburgh\, PA 15201\nLocal Music ShowcaseJoi
 n us for a night with three of Pittsburgh’s most unique and eclectic ban
 ds\, celebrating the end of a chapter for Fermented Beats’ current lineu
 p. Expect to be taken on a soundscape journey\, exploring genres from prog
 ressive jazz fusion and neo-classical\, to avant-rock and funk. Fermented
  Beatshttps://fermentedbeatsmusic.com/\nFermented Beats is a genre-bending
  collective that creates bass-driven instrumental music with engaging horn
 s\, unique effects\, and driving drums. Embracing a diverse breadth of gen
 res\, from psych rock and jazz to experimental prog and neo-classical\, th
 e band utilizes the sounds of clarinet\, saxophone and effects to leave li
 steners scratching their head in awe and curiosity. Rooted in Pittsburgh\,
  the group also explores the abstract\, gritty\, and experimental nature o
 f their personalities. Inspired by nature and fermentation\, and motivated
  by society’s inequities\, they strive to push themselves through odd ti
 me signatures and adventurous compositions. Glance around the stage and yo
 u might find vegetables (likely beets) or a jar of fermented vegetables (a
 lso likely beets) floating about.\nblotthttps://fusionillusionllc.com/home
 \nblott (est. 2025) is a five-piece art rock/neo-fusion group formed by Hi
 ghland Park-based keyboardist and composer\, Henry Schultz. Their live per
 formances consist of bombastic and occasionally dark\, synthesizer-heavy o
 riginals rife with chaotic improvisation\, ambient soundscapes\, pretty pa
 rts\, glimmers of prog\, and bits of funk. … with MARS (electric bass)\
 , Cody House (guitar\, theremin)\, Brandon Kaltenbaugh (drums)\, and Zack 
 Mester (percussion)\nthe Alfomega\nthe Alfomega is a group based out of Pi
 ttsburgh\, PA founded on the creative partnership of Cecily McGowan and Ch
 ris Wood. We combine ascendent musicianship\, unique soundscapes and a tho
 ughtful balance of progressive songcraft and exploratory improvisation. We
  work with a series of collaborators to not only bring our vision to life 
 but to push the envelope of what is possible in a live setting with a limi
 ted number of musicians.\nTicket Tier Info:General Admission Tickets – S
 tanding Room Only\nFor accessible seating accommodations\, please send an 
 email after ticket purchase to contact@thunderbirdmusichall.com.\nAll sale
 s are final.\n 
LOCATION:Thunderbird Music Hall
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:CLOUD NOTHINGS
DTSTART:20260821T000000Z
DTEND:20260821T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260611T160239Z
UID:f8900682-65ae-11f1-a3ea-ae4281c53881
DESCRIPTION:https://app.opendate.io/e/cloud-nothings-august-20-2026-691968\
 n  CLOUD NOTHINGS with support tba  $22 ADV / $26 DOS 7PM DOORS / 8PM MUSI
 C ALL AGES  for fans of... Titus Andronicus\, Metz\, Parquet Courts\, Dino
 saur Jr.  BIO: Some bands never miss. This rare breed consistently puts ou
 t great records every couple years\, avoiding the lengthy hiatuses or egre
 gious sonic missteps that often come with achieving longevity. It’s an o
 ften unsung reliability\, as few realize how truly remarkable it is to put
  art into the world at this rate without letting the quality slip. For nea
 rly 15 years\, Cloud Nothings have continued to hit the target\, steadily 
 becoming a part of the fabric of modern indie rock as we know it with a ru
 n of fantastic albums. This streak continues unabated with their latest fu
 ll-length\, Final Summer–an album that’s so assured\, so instantly sat
 isfying\, that it forces you to pause and realize you’re listening to on
 e of the great American rock bands in their prime.  Recorded with Jeff Zei
 gler (Kurt Vile\, The War On Drugs\, Torres\, Purling Hiss)\, mixed by Sar
 ah Tudzin (Porches\, Tim Heidecker\, Pom Pom Squad)\, and mastered by Jack
  Callahan (Ryley Walker\, Merchandise\, Wolf Eyes)\, Final Summer is burst
 ing with the unbridled joy that only comes from playing guitars and drums 
 loudly. This is not the work of a scrappy new band cramming all of their i
 deas into a debut album or grizzled veterans grinding through another rele
 ase: it’s one of the tightest and most invigorating rock bands active to
 day\, driven to make the best version of themselves.   
LOCATION:Bottlerocket Social Hall
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hiroya Tsukamoto
DTSTART:20260621T000000Z
DTEND:20260621T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260611T160239Z
UID:f8950a88-65ae-11f1-a3ea-ae4281c53881
DESCRIPTION:https://pittsburghwinery.com/event/hiroya-tsukamoto/\n\n\nThe O
 riginal Pittsburgh Winery & Music Night on Jupiter Present: Hiroya Tsukamo
 to!\n\nDOORS AT 6PM | SHOW AT 7PM | 21 AND OVER\n$20.00 in Advance // $25.
 00 Day of show [+Tax/Fees]\n\n*This is a general admission event. There is
  plenty of seating available. But it is first come\, first serve and is th
 erefore not guaranteed. \n \nAbout Hiroya Tsukamoto:\n\n“A Journey Thr
 ough Strings and Stories”\nTsukamoto brings a blend of masterful fingers
 tyle guitar and evocative storytelling that transcends cultural barriers. 
 His artistry\, honed at the prestigious Berklee College of Music\, has bee
 n celebrated on renowned stages like the Blue Note in NYC and the United N
 ations\, and lauded for its “delicate\, fluid\, and beautifully detailed
 ” style by Acoustic Guitar magazine.\nTsukamoto’s concerts are not jus
 t musical events\; they are immersive experiences that weave lyrical narra
 tives with intricate melodies. Recognized for his soulful performances tha
 t create an orchestra at his fingertips\, he invites audiences into his wo
 rld of musical exploration and emotional expression. This is a rare opport
 unity to witness a performer who has been celebrated for his ability to ta
 ke listeners on an “impressionistic journey” (Boston Herald).  Enchan
 ting music that promises to resonate long after the final note is played.\
 n\n\n
LOCATION:Pittsburgh Winery
END:VEVENT
