BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Brook &#038\; The Bluff
DTSTART:20261016T000000Z
DTEND:20261016T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260612T190150Z
UID:2b3826f4-6691-11f1-a3ea-ae4281c53881
DESCRIPTION:https://thunderbirdmusichall.com/event/the-brook-the-bluff-2/th
 underbird-cafe-music-hall/pittsburgh-pennsylvania/\n\nThe Brook and The Bl
 uff\nThe Werewolf Tour\nThursday\, October 15\, 2026Thunderbird Music Hall
 4053 Butler Street\, Pittsburgh\, PADoors @ 7PMShow @ 8PMAGE RESTRICTION: 
 18+ or with legal guardian\n \nhttps://www.brookandbluff.com\n\nThe Brook
  & The Bluff return to their rock & roll roots with Werewolf — a high-vo
 ltage\, live-inspired record that turns up the amps\, pushes the tempo\, a
 nd howls in four-part harmony. Fueled by the sharp songwriting and stacked
  vocals that have defined their catalog\, the album captures the raw\, sup
 ercharged energy of the band’s concerts.\nAfter nearly a decade of nonst
 op touring — earning 200M+ streams with fan favorites like “Halfway Up
 ” and “Everything Is Just a Mess” — the band pressed pause and reg
 rouped in Nashville\, meeting every morning to write and rehearse like the
 y did in their early days at Auburn University. Life unfolded in the backg
 round: weddings\, divorces\, real-world growing pains. Inside the room\, i
 t was all music.\nChanneling the spirit of Creedence\, Petty\, and Eagles\
 , Werewolf delivers loud\, melodic\, deeply human songs like the lead sing
 le “Super Bowl Sunday” — a crashing\, introspective anthem about ego
  and emotional blind spots — alongside the highway-born “105” and th
 e swaggering “Get By\,” confronting modern masculinity\, self-reflecti
 on\, and the cost of chasing the road. “The goal was to treat the record
  like a live set\,” says frontman Joseph Settine. And that’s exactly w
 hat they’ve done.\nVIP PACKAGES\nEarly Entry VIP Package\n\nEarly entry 
 into the venue\nPre-show merchandise shopping access\nOfficial VIP laminat
 e\nOfficial VIP enamel button\nOne general admission ticket\nLimited avail
 ability\n\nEarly Entry VIP purchasers should plan to arrive 30 minutes pri
 or to doors in order to participate in the Early Entry VIP experience.Were
 wolf VIP Package\n\nAccess to an intimate pre-show acoustic performance + 
 Q&A*\nExclusive tour poster\, autographed by the band*\nExclusive VIP tote
  bag*\nGroup photo with The Brook & The Bluff*\nEarly entry into the venue
 \nPre-show merchandise shopping access\nOfficial VIP laminate\nOfficial VI
 P enamel button\nOne general admission ticket\nLimited availability\n\n*ex
 clusive to Werewolf VIP package \nWerewolf VIP purchasers should plan to 
 arrive 1 hour prior to doors in order to participate in the Werewolf VIP e
 xperience.Ticket Tier Info:General Admission Tickets – Standing Room Onl
 y\nFor accessible seating accommodations\, please send an email in advance
  to contact@thunderbirdmusichall.com after ticket purchase. All sales are 
 final. 
LOCATION:Thunderbird Music Hall
END:VEVENT
