BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Danny Golden & Alan Getto
DTSTART:20260713T000000Z
DTEND:20260713T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260615T210143Z
UID:6a01e0b4-68fd-11f1-a3ea-ae4281c53881
DESCRIPTION:https://pittsburghwinery.com/event/danny-golden-alan-getto/\n\n
 The Original Pittsburgh Winery Presents: Danny Golden & Alan Getto!\n$15 A
 dvance / $20 Day of show [+ Tax/Fees]\n\n\nDOORS AT 6PM | SHOW AT 7PM | 21
  AND OVER\nAbout Danny Golden: \nDanny Golden’s music carries the impri
 nt of a uniquely American journey. Born and raised in Pittsburgh\, Pennsyl
 vania\, Golden came of age in a city where the grit of the Rust Belt meets
  the foothills of Appalachia and the sweep of the heartland. Those worlds 
 still echo through his songs. He left Pittsburgh for Colorado College\, wh
 ere he studied philosophy\, classical music\, and bluegrass banjo\, culmin
 ating in a senior thesis in which he reimagined Bach for bluegrass instrum
 ents. From there\, he followed music to Austin\, Texas\, which he has call
 ed home for the last decade. In Austin\, he has performed and recorded as 
 a singer/songwriter\, bandleader\, and musical journeyman\, writing and pl
 aying instruments for artists ranging from indie rock bands to soul singer
 s to country songwriters. Through these varied adventures\, Golden has for
 ged a voice and sound all his own. His music blends folk\, indie rock\, an
 d confessional storytelling into his own distinct brand of Americana. Rece
 ntly\, Golden has toured nationally with his band and performed alongside 
 artists including Shakey Graves\, David Ramirez\, Rob Baird\, and Matthew 
 Logan Vasquez of Delta Spirit. He has received praise from Billboard\, NPR
  Austin\, NBC Austin\, FLOOD Magazine\, Under the Radar\, mxdwn\, and more
 !\n\nMost recently\, in the fall of 2025\, Golden was approached by the te
 am promoting the film Bruce Springsteen: Deliver Me from Nowhere to perfor
 m Springsteen’s Nebraska album live in Austin in a recreation of Bruce
 ’s famous New Jersey bedroom studio and set from the film. The performan
 ce was recorded and released as Live from Nowhere: Songs from Bruce Spring
 steen’s Nebraska.\nDanny Golden’s new album The Big Blue comes out Jun
 e 24\, 2026 and his single\, “Hungry Ghost”\, has been recognized on S
 potify’s Indigo and Tidal’s Wildwood Flowers playlists.\n \nAbout Ala
 n Getto:\nAlan Getto is a musician and songwriter based in Pittsburgh\, Pe
 nnsylvania. Getto’s music pairs pastoral soundscapes with existential ly
 ricism to explore the human condition. To date\, Getto has released three 
 albums\, toured the East Coast\, showcased at Folk Alliance and with SoFar
  Sounds\, and shared stages with Angela Autumn\, Damn Tall Buildings\, and
  Coltt Winter Lepley.\n\n\n
LOCATION:Pittsburgh Winery
END:VEVENT
