BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sound Series: An Evening with Nellie McKay
DTSTART:20261113T010000Z
DTEND:20261113T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20260618T160146Z
UID:01e04122-6b2f-11f1-83f2-82c656f021c5
DESCRIPTION:10002188-1794513600-1794520800@www.warhol.org\nWe welcome back 
 the inimitable singer/songwriter\, Nellie McKay for a special retrospectiv
 e set\, playing songs across her varied catalogue. Since Get Away from Me 
 (2004)\, McKay has released nine eclectic albums\, ranging from pop to jaz
 z to rock & folk\, always defying categorization. Her music has been used 
 on radio\, TV and in the movies\, and she has appeared on many shows\, fro
 m The Late Show with David Letterman to A Prairie Home Companion\, as well
  as writing and performing acclaimed bios of Barbara Graham\, Rachel Carso
 n\, Billy Tipton and Joan Rivers. McKay is also a dedicated advocate for a
 nimal rights\, feminism\, civil rights and environmental protection. \n“
 A renegade songwriter with an ultraflexible Great American Songbook sensib
 ility. McKay finds modern resonances everywhere.” – Rolling Stone \n\n
 Nellie McKay’s performance begins at 8 p.m.
LOCATION:The Warhol theater\, 117 Sandusky Street\, Pittsburgh\, PA\, 15212
 \, United States
END:VEVENT
