BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mixburgh Masters
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260706T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260706T200000
DTSTAMP:20260701T020158Z
UID:d7a37534-74f0-11f1-a280-9e9e635c43f9
DESCRIPTION:https://www.poetrymillvale.com/event/mixburgh-masters/\nMixBurg
 h was created to bring educational events back to the industry\, run by wo
 rking pros\, for working pros. This isn’t about any one brand\, it’s a
 bout a rising tide floating everybody’s boats in this city. \nWe are kic
 king that off with our MixBurgh Masters series\, and we are starting at th
 e top. Sean Enright is the godfather of craft cocktails in Pittsburgh\, th
 e man who literally wrote the book on Pittsburgh drinks. For session one h
 e will host the trade at Poetry Lounge in Millvale for a night of pure tec
 hnique. Three cocktails\, one shaken\, one stirred\, one built in the glas
 s\, with full instruction behind each method. The small decisions that get
  rushed on a busy shift\, slowed down and walked through from first pour t
 o final garnish. \nMasters is something we plan to keep doing. This is the
  first one\, set on a Monday on purpose\, so the people who run this city
 ’s bars every weekend can actually make it. Come hang with the other fol
 ks who take this seriously\, bartenders\, distillers\, everyone working th
 e craft cocktail scene here. \nIt all builds toward MixBurgh 2026\, Pittsb
 urgh’s 1st Cocktail Weekend and Conference\, this November. Learn more a
 t mixburgh.com. \n$50\, proceeds to the MixBurgh Foundation (a nonprofit c
 o-op for our community) \nSeats are limited by the format. Link in bio. We
  will see you behind the bar. \n  \nTICKETS
LOCATION:Poetry Lounge
END:VEVENT
