BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:RACHEL HARRISON: White Whale Books
DTSTART:20260910T233000Z
DTEND:20260911T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20260701T180159Z
UID:f4d4deb4-7576-11f1-9658-9e9e635c43f9
DESCRIPTION:https://app.opendate.io/e/rachel-harrison-white-whale-books-sep
 tember-10-2026-713558\n Presented by Bottlerocket and White Whale Books\, 
 Best Selling Author RACHEL HARRISON leads a live reading\, signing\, and Q
 &A of her new book\, KISS SLAY REPLAY. All tickets include your own copy o
 f the book!   KISS SLAY REPLAY by Rachel Harrison (Berkley Hardcover\; Sep
 tember 8\, 2026) | Review copy access available soon upon request.  Fresh 
 off her New York Times bestseller Play Nice and breakout media coverage in
  outlets like Vulture\, People\, and Elle\, Rachel Harrison returns with a
  wildly inventive wedding slasher and a fresh twist on the “final girl
 ” trope—where survival isn’t guaranteed. In Harrison’s scariest no
 vel yet\, reception guests are murdered repeatedly in a time loop only the
  heroine can break. Cementing her status as the queen of contemporary horr
 or\, Harrison explores what it means to face life straight-on— because w
 hether you’re trapped in a time loop or simply stuck in the horrors of e
 veryday life\, the only way out is through.  BIO Rachel Harrison is the Ne
 w York Times bestselling author of Play Nice\, So Thirsty\, Black Sheep\, 
 Such Sharp Teeth\, Cackle\, and The Return\, which was nominated for a Bra
 m Stoker Award for Superior Achievement in a First Novel. Her short fictio
 n has appeared in numerous anthologies and in her debut collection\, Bad D
 olls. She lives in New Jersey with her husband and their cat/overlord. 
LOCATION:Bottlerocket Social Hall
END:VEVENT
