BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sahūagin w/ Org Dröl
DTSTART:20260815T010000Z
DTEND:20260815T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20260707T160525Z
UID:aa7dd0fe-7a1d-11f1-a896-ba7a2e570787
DESCRIPTION:https://pittsburghwinery.com/event/sah%c5%abagin-w-org-dr%c3%b6
 l/\n\nThe Original Pittsburgh Winery Presents: Sahūagin and Org Dröl!\n$
 10 Advance / $15 Day of show [+ Tax/Fees]\n\n\nDOORS AT 7PM | SHOW AT 8PM 
 | 21 AND OVER\nAbout Sahūagin: \nBrewed in the depths of the Pittsburgh 
 Jam Scene\, Sahūagin is a blend of familiar musical flavors crafted int
 o a new vintage. Featuring alumni from bands such as Trailheads\, Samjamwi
 ch\, The Buckle Downs\, and KGB\, Sahūagin stirs together experience\, 
 a deep admiration for their musical forebears\, and a desire to wade into 
 uncharted waters of improvisational music. Whether you’re a fan of Phish
 \, Grateful Dead\, modern jam bands like Dopapod\, Aqueous\, and Goose\, o
 r just a fan of music\, Sahūagin will satisfy your thirst and have you a
 sking for another. \n \nAbout Org Dröl: \nThe cloaked figures of Org 
 Dröl bring to life a psychedelic fantasy tale from time immemorial. The p
 erspective changes\, the plot thickens & the battle rages on. There are ma
 ny beating hearts but only one dragon. Welcome to the lore.\n\n
LOCATION:Pittsburgh Winery
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sound Series: L’Rain
DTSTART:20260923T000000Z
DTEND:20260923T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260707T160525Z
UID:aa813294-7a1d-11f1-a896-ba7a2e570787
DESCRIPTION:10002189-1790107200-1790114400@www.warhol.org\nWe welcome L’R
 ain\, the musical project of multi-instrumentalist\, composer\, producer a
 nd curator Taja Cheek. Operating at the intersections of art\, music\, fil
 m\, fashion and cultural discourse\, Cheek’s sensibility\, crafted in co
 llaboration with Ben Chapoteau-Katz and Andrew Lappin\, transcends discipl
 ines\, blurs traditional genre boundaries and deconstructs pop tropes. The
  2021 album Fatigue garnered critical acclaim including album of the year 
 from The Wire\, and in May 2026\, L’Rain recorded a live album and conce
 rt film at Walker Art Center in Minneapolis. Cheek was guest curator of th
 e 2024 Whitney Biennial and currently is the artistic director of Performa
 nce Space New York. \n\nDoors open at 7:30 p.m.\nThis performance is prima
 rily standing room only. Limited seating is available upon advance request
 . We are committed to offering inclusive\, engaging experiences for people
  of all abilities. To request accommodations to enhance your visit\, pleas
 e contact access@warhol.org or call 412.237.8354.
LOCATION:The Warhol entrance space\, 117 Sandusky Street\, Pittsburgh\, PA\
 , 15212\, United States
END:VEVENT
