BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Poet Anna Barnes performing "bloom // wilt"
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260805T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260805T180000
DTSTAMP:20260715T060213Z
UID:b975eac4-8012-11f1-8a0d-6aee3c075612
DESCRIPTION:https://www.poetrymillvale.com/event/poet-anna-barnes-performin
 g-bloom-wilt/\nAnna Barnes\, a Cincinnati\, Ohio poet\, announces the rele
 ase of her second book\, “bloom // wilt”\, for adult poetry readers wi
 th interest in topics of gender\, sexuality\, feminism\, matriarchy\, and 
 the war between nature and the manmade world. This 20-poem chapbook follow
 s a character named Chrysanthemum on her journey as she is born in nature\
 , begins to look longingly toward and then ventures into the shimmering ci
 ty in the horizon\, soon finds out that the city is not as beautiful as it
  seems from the outside\, and is only able to return to her natural homela
 nd by dying and being buried in the dirt. Chrysanthemum originated from a 
 poem of the same name in Anna’s first poetry book\, “Out of Ink and Id
 eas” (2025).
LOCATION:Poetry Lounge
END:VEVENT
