BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:I See Stars
DTSTART:20260919T230000Z
DTEND:20260920T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260715T160729Z
UID:479df5ae-8067-11f1-ac8e-6aee3c075612
DESCRIPTION:https://thunderbirdmusichall.com/event/i-see-stars/thunderbird-
 cafe-music-hall/pittsburgh-pennsylvania/\n\nI See Stars\nNate Vickers\nSat
 urday\, September 19\, 2026Thunderbird Music Hall4053 Butler Street\, Pitt
 sburgh\, PADoors @ 6:00 pmShow @ 7:00 pmAGE RESTRICTION: 18+ or with legal
  guardian\n \nhttps://www.iseestarsmusic.com\nNearly a decade since their
  last album\, electronicore pioneers I See Stars return with THE WHEEL\, a
  fully immersive sixth full-length that embodies patience\, purpose\, and 
 fate. Comprised of Devin Oliver (vocals)\, Brent Allen (guitar)\, Andrew O
 liver (keys/programming)\, and Jeff Valentine (bass)\, the band scrapped e
 arly drafts during Covid to create what Devin calls “a culmination of no
 t just the last year or two\, but of the last eight or nine.” Produced b
 y David Bendeth and mixed by Zakk Cervini\, the record reflects both perso
 nal trials—including Devin’s battle with intracranial hypertension and
  the loss of the Oliver brothers’ uncle—and a philosophical surrender 
 to destiny. “This way wasn’t a choice for me\,” Devin says. “It so
 unds almost self-deprecating\, but I actually think it’s been an honor.
 ” The result is a visceral\, vulnerable\, and revitalized statement that
  reaffirms why I See Stars remain one of the genre’s most forward-thinki
 ng forces.\n\n\n\n \n\n\nhttps://natevickers.com/Introducing Nate Vickers
 : the enigmatic force behind the electrifying sounds captivating social me
 dia feeds worldwide. Based in Houston\, this rock/pop virtuoso has mastere
 d the art of leaving audiences spellbound\, all while shrouded in an aura 
 of mystery that leaves followers craving more.To know Nate Vickers is to e
 mbark on a journey shrouded in intrigue\, where every note\, every post\, 
 every shared moment unveils a new layer of his enigmatic persona.\n \nTic
 ket Tier Info:General Admission Tickets – Standing Room Only\nFor access
 ible seating accommodations\, please send an email in advance to contact@t
 hunderbirdmusichall.com after ticket purchase. All sales are final. 
LOCATION:Thunderbird Music Hall
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:PGHwrites: Pittsburgh Poetry Collective’s Steel City Poetry Slam
DTSTART:20260824T230000Z
DTEND:20260825T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260715T180210Z
UID:4d32a086-8077-11f1-ac8e-6aee3c075612
DESCRIPTION:https://cityofasylum.org/program/pghwrites-pittsburgh-poetry-co
 llectives-steel-city-poetry-slam/\nPhoto Courtesy: Pittsburgh Poetry Colle
 ctiveCan’t get enough of the Steel City Slam? Neither can we! This Augu
 st\, City of Asylum welcomes back longtime friends and partners at Pittsbu
 rgh Poetry Collective for another rowdy night with their poetry slam leagu
 e. The slam is a poetry competition where individuals present and perform 
 original works of poetry to an audience staged as an interactive show. And
  we do mean interactive—the audience can respond to the poets or the jud
 ges in any way they see fit. Audience members are encouraged to snap\, cla
 p\, boo\, or cheer (respectfully) at the conclusion of every poem\, during
  scoring\, or even during the poem.The slam and its accompanying interacti
 ve elements place a dual emphasis on writing and performance\, encouraging
  poets to focus on what they’re saying and how they’re saying it. Poet
 s receive a numerical score for their work based on the poets’ content a
 nd performance from judges typically selected from the audience.For more i
 nformation (including rules and other ways to participate)\, visit the Pit
 tsburgh Poetry Collective website. Complimentary drinks and hors d’oeuv
 res will be available at the program for all participants and attendees. 
 About the Artist:The Pittsburgh Poetry Collective exists to celebrate the 
 power of your voice. They make and hold space for self-expression and iden
 tity exploration via spoken word communities\, poetry slams\, writing and 
 performance workshops\, and poet showcases. They believe that poetry heals
 \, speaks\, connects\, and shares our experiences\, similarities\, and dif
 ferences. They welcome all individuals regardless of gender identity or ra
 cial identity\, background\, class\, sexual orientation\, national origin\
 , religion\, ethnicity\, lifestyle\, age\, and disability. By participatin
 g in Pittsburgh Poetry Collective events\, actively or inactively\, you ag
 ree to welcome these individuals as well.About Your Visit: The in-house r
 estaurant\, Cucina Alfabeto\, is closed on Mondays and Tuesdays.Share this
 :
LOCATION:City of Asylum
END:VEVENT
